insert into daily_devotions (edition, day_number, theme, title, scripture_ref, scripture_text, reflection, declaration, prayer, strength_step, prompt) values
('women', 1, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$This Is the Day$d$, $d$Psalm 118:24$d$, $d$This is the day which the LORD hath made; we will rejoice and be glad in it.$d$, $d$Before the coffee, before the to-do list, before the mirror has a chance to speak, God has already named this day: made by Him. You don’t have to earn a good day. You get to receive one. Rejoicing is a choice you make with your mouth before your feelings catch up. Start the year by agreeing with heaven about today.$d$, $d$I declare that today is blessed and filled with God’s favor, and I will rejoice in it.$d$, $d$Lord, thank You for this day. I receive it as a gift from Your hand.$d$, $d$Step outside or open a window for two minutes and breathe deeply while you thank Him.$d$, $d$What would it look like to rejoice on purpose today, before anything goes right?$d$),
('women', 2, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$He Started It$d$, $d$Philippians 1:6$d$, $d$Being confident of this very thing, that he which hath begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ.$d$, $d$New-year goals can feel like pressure: now it all depends on you. But Paul says the One who began the good work is the One who finishes it. Your growth in faith, health, and purpose is His project before it is your project. Your part is to stay yielded and keep showing up. His part is to complete what He started.$d$, $d$I am convinced and sure that He who began a good work in me will bring it to full completion.$d$, $d$Father, I place this year in Your hands. Finish what You started in me.$d$, $d$Write one goal for your body this year and one for your soul. Put them where you’ll see them.$d$, $d$What good work do you sense God has already begun in you?$d$),
('women', 3, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Mercies for Today$d$, $d$Lamentations 3:22-23$d$, $d$It is of the LORD’s mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not. They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness.$d$, $d$Yesterday’s missed workout, sharp word, or second dessert does not follow you into today. His compassions are new every morning, not every New Year. That means you never have to wait for Monday to begin again. Grace resets the day the moment you wake. Receive it, and let it make you gentle with yourself as you start fresh.$d$, $d$I declare that His mercies are new for me this morning, and I begin again in His faithfulness.$d$, $d$Great is Your faithfulness, Lord. I receive Your new mercy today.$d$, $d$Do a gentle ten-minute stretch and let it be a picture of starting fresh.$d$, $d$Where do you need to accept new mercy instead of replaying yesterday?$d$),
('women', 4, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Plans Established$d$, $d$Proverbs 16:3$d$, $d$Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established.$d$, $d$Commit means to roll your weight onto something. Before you build your plan for this year, roll it onto Him. When your works are committed to the Lord, your thoughts settle and become steady. Plans made in His presence carry a peace that plans made in pressure never do. Bring Him the calendar, the goals, and the gym schedule.$d$, $d$I commit my works to the Lord, and my thoughts and plans are established.$d$, $d$Lord, I roll my plans onto You. Establish what is Yours and remove what is not.$d$, $d$Plan your workouts for this week in your calendar, then pray over the schedule.$d$, $d$Which plan do you need to roll onto God instead of carrying alone?$d$),
('women', 5, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Created for Good Works$d$, $d$Ephesians 2:10$d$, $d$For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works, which God hath before ordained that we should walk in them.$d$, $d$Workmanship is the word for a masterpiece, something crafted with intention. You are not a rough draft God is embarrassed by. You are His handiwork, and there are good works already prepared for you to walk in. Caring for your body is part of stewarding the masterpiece so you can walk fully in what He prepared.$d$, $d$I am God’s workmanship, created for good works that He prepared for me.$d$, $d$Thank You for making me with intention. Help me walk in the works You prepared.$d$, $d$Take a 20-minute walk and ask God to show you one good work He has for you this week.$d$, $d$How does seeing yourself as His workmanship change how you treat your body?$d$),
('women', 6, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Behold, New Things$d$, $d$Isaiah 43:19$d$, $d$Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.$d$, $d$God asks a question: will you notice the new thing? He is not only planning something new; it is already springing up. Some seasons feel like wilderness, but He specializes in making roads where there were none. Look for the small green shoots: a better habit, a softer heart, a stronger morning. New things often start small.$d$, $d$I declare that God is doing a new thing in my life, and I will see it spring forth.$d$, $d$Open my eyes, Lord, to the new things You are already doing.$d$, $d$Try one new healthy food or one new exercise this week.$d$, $d$What small new thing has started springing up in your life lately?$d$),
('women', 7, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Rest Is Holy$d$, $d$Matthew 11:28$d$, $d$Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.$d$, $d$Strong women rest. Jesus doesn’t invite the strong to try harder; He invites the weary to come. Rest is not a reward for finishing everything. It is a gift for carrying anything. Your muscles grow in recovery, and so does your soul. On your rest day, come to Him without an agenda and let Him carry what you cannot.$d$, $d$I come to Jesus with every burden, and I receive His rest for my body and soul.$d$, $d$Jesus, I come to You tired and honest. Give me Your rest.$d$, $d$Make this a true rest day: sleep a little longer and skip the guilt.$d$, $d$What makes it hard for you to rest without feeling guilty?$d$),
('women', 8, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$A Woman of Purpose$d$, $d$Esther 4:14$d$, $d$And who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for such a time as this?$d$, $d$Esther didn’t feel ready. She felt afraid. But her position was not an accident, and neither is yours. Where you live, who you love, the work in front of you: you are placed for such a time as this. Purpose rarely announces itself with confidence. It usually shows up as a quiet nudge to step forward anyway.$d$, $d$I declare that I am placed for such a time as this, and I will walk in my purpose.$d$, $d$Lord, give me courage to step into the place You have positioned me.$d$, $d$Stand tall, shoulders back, for one minute. Practice the posture of a woman with purpose.$d$, $d$Where might God have placed you for such a time as this?$d$),
('women', 9, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Strength from the Lord$d$, $d$Ephesians 6:10$d$, $d$Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might.$d$, $d$Notice where the strength comes from: in the Lord, and in the power of His might. Your workouts build muscle, and they’re worth doing. But the strength that carries you through hard conversations, sleepless nights, and long seasons is borrowed from Him. Train your body, and lean your soul. Both kinds of strength grow with use.$d$, $d$I am strong in the Lord and in the power of His might.$d$, $d$Lord, make me strong in You today, in body and in spirit.$d$, $d$Do three rounds of 10 squats and 10 wall push-ups, praying a short phrase between each round.$d$, $d$Where do you need His strength more than your own this week?$d$),
('women', 10, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Fearfully and Wonderfully$d$, $d$Psalm 139:14$d$, $d$I will praise thee; for I am fearfully and wonderfully made: marvellous are thy works; and that my soul knoweth right well.$d$, $d$The psalmist doesn’t just say God’s works are marvelous; he says his soul knows it right well. Many of us know it in theory but argue with the mirror. Today, let praise come before critique. Your body has carried you, healed you, and maybe carried others. It is a marvelous work. Thank Him for it out loud.$d$, $d$I am fearfully and wonderfully made, and my soul knows it well.$d$, $d$I praise You for how You made me. Teach my soul to agree with You.$d$, $d$Name three things your body did for you this week and thank God for each one.$d$, $d$What would change if you spoke to your body the way God speaks about it?$d$),
('women', 11, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$The Joy of the Lord$d$, $d$Nehemiah 8:10$d$, $d$Neither be ye sorry; for the joy of the LORD is your strength.$d$, $d$Joy is not the absence of hard things. Nehemiah spoke these words to people grieving over ruined walls and broken lives. Joy is a strength source. When you choose to rejoice in what God has done, you find energy you didn’t know you had. Some days joy is a feeling. Other days it is a decision that becomes fuel.$d$, $d$The joy of the Lord is my strength today.$d$, $d$Fill me with Your joy, Lord, and let it be my strength.$d$, $d$Put on worship music and move for 15 minutes. Dance counts.$d$, $d$What is one thing God has done that you can rejoice in today?$d$),
('women', 12, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Run with Patience$d$, $d$Hebrews 12:1$d$, $d$Let us lay aside every weight, and the sin which doth so easily beset us, and let us run with patience the race that is set before us.$d$, $d$Runners don’t carry backpacks in races. Some weights aren’t sinful, just heavy: comparison, perfectionism, old shame. Lay them down. And notice the word patience. This race is not a sprint to the perfect body or perfect life. It’s a long, faithful run. Pace yourself with grace and keep moving forward.$d$, $d$I lay aside every weight and run my race with patience.$d$, $d$Show me what I’m carrying that You never asked me to carry.$d$, $d$Walk or jog at an easy pace for 20 minutes, focused on steady breathing, not speed.$d$, $d$What weight do you need to lay down to run freely?$d$),
('women', 13, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Living Sacrifice$d$, $d$Romans 12:1$d$, $d$I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable service.$d$, $d$Paul says worship includes your body. Not just songs on Sunday, but how you rest, eat, move, and serve. Presenting your body to God doesn’t mean punishing it. It means offering it: daily, willingly, as an act of love. Your workout can be worship when you do it to honor Him rather than to escape yourself.$d$, $d$I present my body to God as a living sacrifice, holy and acceptable to Him.$d$, $d$Lord, I offer You my body today. Use it for Your glory.$d$, $d$Before today’s workout, pray: “This is for You.”$d$, $d$How could your next workout become an act of worship?$d$),
('women', 14, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Renewed in Mind$d$, $d$Romans 12:2$d$, $d$And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.$d$, $d$Transformation starts in the mind before it shows in the body. The world shapes women with constant messages about how to look and what to fear. God transforms from the inside, renewing how you think until you can recognize His good will. Fill your mind with His Word more than your feed, and watch your thinking change.$d$, $d$I am transformed by the renewing of my mind, and I recognize God’s good will.$d$, $d$Renew my mind today, Lord. Replace the world’s voice with Yours.$d$, $d$Take one social media break today and use the time to read a Psalm.$d$, $d$Which thought pattern most needs to be renewed in you right now?$d$),
('women', 15, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$God Who Sees$d$, $d$Genesis 16:13$d$, $d$And she called the name of the LORD that spake unto her, Thou God seest me.$d$, $d$Hagar was overlooked, used, and alone in the desert when God met her. She gave Him a name: the God who sees me. Your quiet faithfulness, the early mornings, the meals you prepared, the tears nobody noticed: He sees all of it. You are never invisible to Him. Let that knowledge settle you today.$d$, $d$I declare that I am seen and known by God.$d$, $d$Thank You for seeing me, Lord, even when no one else does.$d$, $d$Sit quietly for five minutes, breathing slowly, simply aware that He sees you.$d$, $d$Where do you feel unseen, and how does Genesis 16:13 speak to that?$d$),
('women', 16, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Well Done in the Small$d$, $d$Luke 16:10$d$, $d$He that is faithful in that which is least is faithful also in much.$d$, $d$Big transformations are built from small faithfulness: one glass of water, one walk, one prayer, one kind response. God pays attention to the little things because that is where character is formed. Don’t despise a small start. Faithfulness in the least is the training ground for much.$d$, $d$I am faithful in small things, and God entrusts me with much.$d$, $d$Help me honor You in the small choices today.$d$, $d$Drink an extra glass of water before every meal today.$d$, $d$What small faithful habit could you commit to this month?$d$),
('women', 17, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Not by Might$d$, $d$Zechariah 4:6$d$, $d$Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.$d$, $d$There is a strength that comes from discipline and a strength that comes from the Spirit. We need discipline, but we can’t white-knuckle our way into lasting change. When willpower runs out, His Spirit doesn’t. Invite Him into your habits. Ask for help with cravings, consistency, and motivation. He delights to supply what you lack.$d$, $d$I live not by my might or power, but by His Spirit.$d$, $d$Holy Spirit, empower me where my willpower runs short.$d$, $d$When a craving or excuse comes today, pause and pray a 10-second prayer for help.$d$, $d$Where are you relying on willpower instead of His Spirit?$d$),
('women', 18, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Seeds and Seasons$d$, $d$Galatians 6:9$d$, $d$And let us not be weary in well doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not.$d$, $d$Seeds don’t sprout overnight. Muscles don’t appear after one workout. Prayers aren’t always answered in a week. But Paul promises a due season. The harvest is coming if you don’t quit. Weariness is normal; fainting is optional. Keep sowing well: the workout, the kind word, the faithful prayer.$d$, $d$I will not grow weary in doing good, for in due season I will reap.$d$, $d$Lord, strengthen me to keep sowing when I can’t see the harvest yet.$d$, $d$Repeat a workout you did earlier this month and notice what’s easier now.$d$, $d$Where are you tempted to quit just before the harvest?$d$),
('women', 19, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Clothed in Strength$d$, $d$Proverbs 31:25$d$, $d$Strength and honour are her clothing; and she shall rejoice in time to come.$d$, $d$The Proverbs 31 woman wears strength and honor. Not anxiety, not hurry, not comparison: strength. And because of it, she laughs at the future. Her confidence isn’t in having everything figured out. It’s in the God who has. Get dressed today in what He gives: strength, dignity, and a settled joy about what’s ahead.$d$, $d$I am clothed in strength and honor, and I rejoice in the days to come.$d$, $d$Clothe me in Your strength today, Lord, and silence my fear of the future.$d$, $d$As you get dressed today, say this verse out loud.$d$, $d$What about the future are you ready to laugh at instead of fear?$d$),
('women', 20, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Waiting Well$d$, $d$Psalm 27:14$d$, $d$Wait on the LORD: be of good courage, and he shall strengthen thine heart: wait, I say, on the LORD.$d$, $d$Waiting takes courage. It is easier to force, fix, or fret than to wait. But the psalmist links waiting with strength: wait, and He shall strengthen your heart. Whatever you’re waiting for, whether healing, a breakthrough, or a change in your body or circumstances, wait on Him, not just for it.$d$, $d$I wait on the Lord with courage, and He strengthens my heart.$d$, $d$Lord, I choose to wait on You. Strengthen my heart while I wait.$d$, $d$Hold a plank or wall-sit as long as you can while repeating “Wait on the Lord.”$d$, $d$What are you waiting for, and how can you wait on Him in it?$d$),
('women', 21, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Delight First$d$, $d$Psalm 37:4$d$, $d$Delight thyself also in the LORD; and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart.$d$, $d$The order matters: delight first. When you delight in Him, your desires begin to align with His. Some desires grow stronger; others quietly fade. This isn’t a formula for getting what you want. It’s an invitation to want Him most, and then trust Him with everything else you long for.$d$, $d$I delight myself in the Lord, and He shapes and fulfills the desires of my heart.$d$, $d$Be my first delight today, Lord.$d$, $d$Spend five minutes writing what you love about God before you open your phone.$d$, $d$What does delighting in the Lord look like for you practically?$d$),
('women', 22, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Peace Like a River$d$, $d$Isaiah 26:3$d$, $d$Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.$d$, $d$Perfect peace is promised to the stayed mind, the mind that keeps returning to Him. You will drift; everyone does. The practice is coming back. When your thoughts race about family, money, or your body, gently bring them back to Him. Every return is an act of trust, and trust is where peace lives.$d$, $d$My mind is stayed on God, and He keeps me in perfect peace.$d$, $d$When my mind wanders today, bring it back to You.$d$, $d$Take a slow walk and breathe in for four counts and out for six counts.$d$, $d$What tends to pull your mind away from peace?$d$),
('women', 23, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$A Living Hope$d$, $d$1 Peter 1:3$d$, $d$Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, which according to his abundant mercy hath begotten us again unto a lively hope by the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead.$d$, $d$Your hope is alive because Jesus is alive. It’s not wishful thinking. It’s anchored in an empty tomb. When a plan falls apart or progress feels slow, your hope doesn’t die with it. It rests on resurrection power, the same power Paul prays you will know is at work in you.$d$, $d$I have a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ.$d$, $d$Thank You for a hope that is alive and cannot be taken from me.$d$, $d$Do something that makes you feel alive today: a brisk walk, a dance, a new route.$d$, $d$Where do you need living hope to replace a dying one?$d$),
('women', 24, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Created to Bear Fruit$d$, $d$John 15:5$d$, $d$I am the vine, ye are the branches: He that abideth in me, and I in him, the same bringeth forth much fruit: for without me ye can do nothing.$d$, $d$Branches don’t strain to grow fruit. They stay connected. Fruitfulness flows from abiding. Before you push harder, check your connection. Are you spending time with Him, listening, resting in His love? Much fruit comes from much abiding. Without Him you can do nothing of lasting value, but with Him you bear fruit that remains.$d$, $d$I abide in Christ, and I bring forth much fruit.$d$, $d$Jesus, I want to stay connected to You today in everything.$d$, $d$Set three phone reminders today that simply say “Abide.”$d$, $d$What helps you stay connected to Jesus during a busy day?$d$),
('women', 25, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$He Restores$d$, $d$Psalm 23:2-3$d$, $d$He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters. He restoreth my soul.$d$, $d$Sometimes God makes us lie down. Sickness, a canceled plan, an unexpected pause: it can feel like a setback, but He may be leading you to green pastures. Restoration happens in stillness. Your soul needs still waters as much as your body needs sleep. Let today be a day of restoring, not just achieving.$d$, $d$The Lord leads me beside still waters and restores my soul.$d$, $d$Shepherd me today, Lord. Restore what has been depleted.$d$, $d$Go to bed 30 minutes earlier tonight.$d$, $d$What restores your soul, and when did you last make time for it?$d$),
('women', 26, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Courage for Today$d$, $d$Joshua 1:9$d$, $d$Have not I commanded thee? Be strong and of a good courage; be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest.$d$, $d$God’s command to be courageous comes with a reason: He is with you wherever you go. Into the gym where you feel out of place, into the hard conversation, into the new season. Courage isn’t the absence of fear. It’s the presence of God, recognized and trusted. Go today knowing He goes with you.$d$, $d$I am strong and courageous, for the Lord my God is with me wherever I go.$d$, $d$Go with me today, Lord, and make me brave.$d$, $d$Try one exercise or class that intimidates you a little.$d$, $d$Where do you need courage this week?$d$),
('women', 27, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$His Word in My Heart$d$, $d$Psalm 119:11$d$, $d$Thy word have I hid in mine heart, that I might not sin against thee.$d$, $d$What you store in your heart is what comes out under pressure. When you hide His Word in your heart, it rises up in moments of temptation, fear, or discouragement. Memorizing Scripture isn’t a school exercise. It’s spiritual strength training, building reserves for the day you need them.$d$, $d$I hide God’s Word in my heart, and it guards my life.$d$, $d$Write Your Word on my heart, Lord.$d$, $d$Memorize this month’s verse, Philippians 1:6, while you walk.$d$, $d$Which verse has carried you through a hard moment before?$d$),
('women', 28, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Grace Is Enough$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 12:9$d$, $d$And he said unto me, My grace is sufficient for thee: for my strength is made perfect in weakness.$d$, $d$Weakness isn’t the opposite of strength in God’s kingdom. It’s the place His strength shows up best. The days you feel least capable are the days His grace has the most room to work. You don’t have to hide your limits from Him. Bring them, and let His sufficient grace fill the gaps.$d$, $d$His grace is sufficient for me, and His strength is made perfect in my weakness.$d$, $d$Lord, here is my weakness. Let Your strength be perfected in it.$d$, $d$Choose a modified version of an exercise today without shame.$d$, $d$What weakness could you hand to God instead of hiding?$d$),
('women', 29, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Faithful to Finish$d$, $d$1 Thessalonians 5:24$d$, $d$Faithful is he that calleth you, who also will do it.$d$, $d$As this first month closes, remember who is carrying this year. He who calls you is faithful, and He will do it. Not you alone, but Him in you. You may have started strong or stumbled already. Either way, He is faithful. Step into the next month leaning on His faithfulness instead of your perfection.$d$, $d$He who called me is faithful, and He will do it.$d$, $d$Thank You for being faithful when I am not. Carry me into this next season.$d$, $d$Look back at your goals from Day 2 and celebrate one step you took.$d$, $d$How has God been faithful to you this month?$d$),
('women', 30, $d$A Good Work Begun$d$, $d$Morning Declarations$d$, $d$Psalm 5:3$d$, $d$My voice shalt thou hear in the morning, O LORD; in the morning will I direct my prayer unto thee, and will look up.$d$, $d$The psalmist directs his prayer in the morning and then looks up, expecting God to answer. Your morning declarations are not wishful thinking. They are directed prayers spoken in faith. Speak them, then live the day looking up, watching for His answers. Mornings shape days, and days shape years.$d$, $d$In the morning I direct my prayer to God, and I look up expecting His answer.$d$, $d$Hear my voice this morning, Lord. I’m watching for You.$d$, $d$Read your seven Morning Declarations out loud before breakfast.$d$, $d$Which morning declaration do you most need to believe right now?$d$),
('women', 31, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$A Spirit of Wisdom$d$, $d$Ephesians 1:17$d$, $d$That the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give unto you the spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of him.$d$, $d$Paul’s first prayer for believers isn’t for comfort or success. It’s for wisdom and revelation in knowing God. Knowing about Him isn’t the same as knowing Him. This month, ask for the kind of knowing that changes how you see everything: your day, your body, your worth, your future.$d$, $d$I receive a spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of God.$d$, $d$Father of glory, let me know You more deeply this month.$d$, $d$Pray Ephesians 1:17 over yourself during a ten-minute walk.$d$, $d$What do you most want to understand about God right now?$d$),
('women', 32, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Enlightened Eyes$d$, $d$Ephesians 1:18$d$, $d$The eyes of your understanding being enlightened; that ye may know what is the hope of his calling, and what the riches of the glory of his inheritance in the saints.$d$, $d$Your heart has eyes. It sees through hope or through fear, through God’s promises or through your past. Paul prays for those eyes to be flooded with light. When they are, you see your calling as hopeful and yourself as part of His rich inheritance. Ask Him to turn the lights on.$d$, $d$The eyes of my heart are flooded with light, and I see the hope of His calling.$d$, $d$Holy Spirit, flood the eyes of my heart with Your light.$d$, $d$Spend five minutes in sunlight today and thank God for His light.$d$, $d$What has your heart been seeing through lately: hope or fear?$d$),
('women', 33, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$The Hope of His Calling$d$, $d$Romans 8:28$d$, $d$And we know that all things work together for good to them that love God, to them who are the called according to his purpose.$d$, $d$You are called. Not just pastors and missionaries: you. And because you’re called according to His purpose, all things are being woven together for good. Not that everything is good, but that He is working in everything. Your calling gives your hardest days a purpose they wouldn’t otherwise have.$d$, $d$I am called according to His purpose, and all things work together for my good.$d$, $d$Lord, weave every part of my story into Your good purpose.$d$, $d$Do a 15-minute workout and thank God that He wastes nothing, not even sweat.$d$, $d$What hard thing might God be working for good in your life?$d$),
('women', 34, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Riches of His Inheritance$d$, $d$Ephesians 1:11$d$, $d$In whom also we have obtained an inheritance, being predestinated according to the purpose of him who worketh all things after the counsel of his own will.$d$, $d$An inheritance is something you receive because of who you belong to, not what you earned. In Christ, you have obtained one. You are not a guest in God’s family. You are an heir. When you feel like you have to prove your place, remember: inheritances are received, not achieved.$d$, $d$I have obtained an inheritance in Christ, and I belong in God’s family.$d$, $d$Thank You that my place in Your family is secure in Christ.$d$, $d$Write down three spiritual riches you have in Christ.$d$, $d$Where are you still trying to earn what God has already given?$d$),
('women', 35, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Surpassing Power$d$, $d$Ephesians 1:19$d$, $d$And what is the exceeding greatness of his power to us-ward who believe, according to the working of his mighty power.$d$, $d$Exceeding greatness. Paul runs out of words trying to describe God’s power toward those who believe. That power isn’t just for heaven or for special people. It is toward you, right now. You don’t generate it. You believe and receive it. Bring your limits today to His exceeding greatness.$d$, $d$The exceeding greatness of God’s power is at work in me because I believe.$d$, $d$Lord, let me know Your mighty power working in me today.$d$, $d$Lift something heavy today, with good form, and remember whose power you carry.$d$, $d$Where do you most need to experience God’s power?$d$),
('women', 36, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Resurrection Strength$d$, $d$Ephesians 1:20$d$, $d$Which he wrought in Christ, when he raised him from the dead, and set him at his own right hand in the heavenly places.$d$, $d$The power at work in you is the same power that raised Jesus from the dead. Let that sink in. Whatever feels dead in your life, whether hope, motivation, a relationship, or a dream, is not beyond the reach of resurrection power. God specializes in raising what looks finished.$d$, $d$The same power that raised Christ from the dead is at work in me.$d$, $d$Breathe resurrection life into every dead place in me, Lord.$d$, $d$Try a new movement today and celebrate what your body can still learn.$d$, $d$What feels dead that you can invite resurrection power into?$d$),
('women', 37, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Seated with Him$d$, $d$Ephesians 2:6$d$, $d$And hath raised us up together, and made us sit together in heavenly places in Christ Jesus.$d$, $d$Seated is a posture of rest and authority. Christ finished His work and sat down, and you are seated with Him. You fight from victory, not for it. On this rest day, take your seat. You don’t have to strive for a place that has already been given to you.$d$, $d$I am seated with Christ in heavenly places, and I rest in His finished work.$d$, $d$Help me live from the seat You’ve given me, not from striving.$d$, $d$Rest day. Sit somewhere peaceful for ten minutes with no phone.$d$, $d$What would living from victory instead of for victory look like?$d$),
('women', 38, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Knowing Him$d$, $d$Philippians 3:10$d$, $d$That I may know him, and the power of his resurrection, and the fellowship of his sufferings.$d$, $d$Paul had achievements, credentials, and a ministry. Yet his deepest desire was simply to know Him. Knowing God includes His resurrection power and the fellowship of His sufferings. He meets you on the mountaintop and in the valley. Every season is an invitation to know Him in a new way.$d$, $d$My deepest desire is to know Him and the power of His resurrection.$d$, $d$Lord, above every goal I have, I want to know You.$d$, $d$Walk in silence for 15 minutes and simply talk with Him.$d$, $d$How have you come to know God in a hard season?$d$),
('women', 39, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Ask for Wisdom$d$, $d$James 1:5$d$, $d$If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.$d$, $d$God gives wisdom liberally, generously, and without scolding you for asking. Not sure what to eat, how to train, how to handle your kids, or what to say? Ask. He doesn’t sigh at your questions. He loves to give wisdom to daughters who ask.$d$, $d$When I lack wisdom, I ask God, and He gives it to me generously.$d$, $d$Lord, I need wisdom for this specific situation. Thank You for giving it.$d$, $d$Before choosing your meals today, pause and ask for wisdom.$d$, $d$Where do you need God’s wisdom most this week?$d$),
('women', 40, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Light for My Path$d$, $d$Psalm 119:105$d$, $d$Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path.$d$, $d$A lamp lights your next step, not the whole road. God’s Word often gives just enough light for today’s step. You may want the five-year plan, but He offers the next faithful step. Take it. Then the light moves with you.$d$, $d$God’s Word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my path.$d$, $d$Show me the next step, Lord, and give me courage to take it.$d$, $d$Take a 20-minute walk and consider one next step God is asking of you.$d$, $d$What is your next faithful step, even if you can’t see the whole road?$d$),
('women', 41, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$He Reveals Secrets$d$, $d$Daniel 2:22$d$, $d$He revealeth the deep and secret things: he knoweth what is in the darkness, and the light dwelleth with him.$d$, $d$Nothing is hidden from God, not your confusion, your fears, or the answer you’ve been looking for. He reveals deep things to those who seek Him. If you feel in the dark about a decision or a struggle, remember: light dwells with Him. Draw near to the One who knows.$d$, $d$God reveals deep things to me, and light dwells with Him.$d$, $d$Reveal what I need to see, Lord. Shine Your light into what feels dark.$d$, $d$Journal for ten minutes about something you don’t understand yet.$d$, $d$What question are you bringing to God this week?$d$),
('women', 42, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$The Mind of Christ$d$, $d$1 Corinthians 2:16$d$, $d$For who hath known the mind of the Lord, that he may instruct him? But we have the mind of Christ.$d$, $d$You don’t just have access to good advice. You have the mind of Christ. His Spirit shapes how you think, decide, and respond. When your mind feels foggy or crowded, remember what you already have. Ask Him to think through you today.$d$, $d$I have the mind of Christ, and His thoughts shape mine.$d$, $d$Think through me today, Jesus. Let Your mind be in me.$d$, $d$Do a focused 20-minute workout with no distractions.$d$, $d$How might Jesus think about the situation you’re facing?$d$),
('women', 43, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Rooted Knowledge$d$, $d$Colossians 1:9$d$, $d$We do not cease to pray for you, and to desire that ye might be filled with the knowledge of his will in all wisdom and spiritual understanding.$d$, $d$Paul prays that believers would be filled with the knowledge of God’s will. Not just guessing, not anxious about missing it, but filled. God isn’t hiding His will from you. As you walk with Him, His will becomes clearer and clearer. Stay close, and trust Him to guide.$d$, $d$I am filled with the knowledge of God’s will in all wisdom.$d$, $d$Fill me with the knowledge of Your will, Lord.$d$, $d$Pray Colossians 1:9 for a friend and send her a message telling her.$d$, $d$Who can you pray this prayer over this week?$d$),
('women', 44, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Walk Worthy$d$, $d$Colossians 1:10$d$, $d$That ye might walk worthy of the Lord unto all pleasing, being fruitful in every good work, and increasing in the knowledge of God.$d$, $d$Knowing God leads to walking with Him. The knowledge grows, and so does the fruit. Walking worthy isn’t about perfection. It’s about direction. Every day, take steps that please Him, and watch the fruit increase in every good work.$d$, $d$I walk worthy of the Lord, fruitful in every good work.$d$, $d$Let my steps please You today, Lord.$d$, $d$Take a long walk and pray for fruit in every area of your life.$d$, $d$What would walking worthy look like in your daily habits?$d$),
('women', 45, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Still and Know$d$, $d$Psalm 46:10$d$, $d$Be still, and know that I am God.$d$, $d$Knowing God sometimes requires stopping. Stillness isn’t laziness. It’s positioning. When you are still, the noise quiets and His voice becomes clear. Today, set aside your striving and simply know: He is God. You don’t have to be.$d$, $d$I am still, and I know that He is God.$d$, $d$Quiet my heart, Lord, so I can know You.$d$, $d$Rest day. Five minutes of stillness, morning and night.$d$, $d$What makes stillness hard for you?$d$),
('women', 46, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Treasure in Seeking$d$, $d$Jeremiah 29:13$d$, $d$And ye shall seek me, and find me, when ye shall search for me with all your heart.$d$, $d$God promises to be found by those who seek Him wholeheartedly. Not perfectly, but wholeheartedly. Bring all of your heart, even the messy, tired, distracted parts. He isn’t hiding from you. He is waiting to be found.$d$, $d$I seek God with all my heart, and I find Him.$d$, $d$I’m searching for You with all my heart, Lord. Let me find You.$d$, $d$Wake up 15 minutes earlier to seek Him before the day begins.$d$, $d$What would seeking God with all your heart look like this week?$d$),
('women', 47, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Spiritual Understanding$d$, $d$Proverbs 2:6$d$, $d$For the LORD giveth wisdom: out of his mouth cometh knowledge and understanding.$d$, $d$Wisdom isn’t earned by information alone. It comes from His mouth. When you read His Word, you’re listening to the source of all understanding. Make room every day to hear Him speak through Scripture before you hear what everyone else has to say.$d$, $d$The Lord gives me wisdom, knowledge, and understanding.$d$, $d$Speak to me through Your Word today, Lord.$d$, $d$Read a chapter of Proverbs today, the one matching today’s date.$d$, $d$What did God speak to you through His Word this week?$d$),
('women', 48, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Hidden Treasure$d$, $d$Proverbs 2:4-5$d$, $d$If thou seekest her as silver, and searchest for her as for hid treasures; Then shalt thou understand the fear of the LORD, and find the knowledge of God.$d$, $d$Treasure hunters dig. They don’t give up after one shovel. Seeking wisdom takes that kind of persistence: reading, praying, asking, listening. And the reward is better than silver. It’s the knowledge of God Himself.$d$, $d$I search for wisdom like hidden treasure, and I find the knowledge of God.$d$, $d$Give me a hunger to dig deeper into You, Lord.$d$, $d$Study one verse deeply today: read it in context and look up one key word.$d$, $d$What spiritual treasure have you found in a season of searching?$d$),
('women', 49, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Heart Knowledge$d$, $d$Psalm 34:8$d$, $d$O taste and see that the LORD is good: blessed is the man that trusteth in him.$d$, $d$Some things can only be known by tasting. You can read a recipe, but you only know it’s good when you take a bite. God invites you to experience His goodness, not just study it. Trust Him in something real today and taste how good He is.$d$, $d$I taste and see that the Lord is good.$d$, $d$Let me experience Your goodness in a fresh way today.$d$, $d$Cook a nourishing meal from the Recipe Book and thank God for each ingredient.$d$, $d$Where have you tasted God’s goodness recently?$d$),
('women', 50, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$He Leads Me$d$, $d$Isaiah 30:21$d$, $d$And thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left.$d$, $d$God’s guidance is often gentle: a word behind you, a quiet nudge. When you turn right or left, He speaks. You don’t have to panic about missing His will. Keep listening. He knows how to get your attention when you need direction.$d$, $d$I hear His voice saying, “This is the way,” and I walk in it.$d$, $d$Help me hear Your gentle direction today, Lord.$d$, $d$Take a walk on a new route and practice listening as you go.$d$, $d$How does God usually speak to you?$d$),
('women', 51, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Christ in You$d$, $d$Colossians 1:27$d$, $d$To whom God would make known what is the riches of the glory of this mystery among the Gentiles; which is Christ in you, the hope of glory.$d$, $d$The mystery isn’t far off. It’s Christ in you. Not a distant God watching from heaven, but the living Christ dwelling in your heart. That’s your hope of glory. You carry Him into every room, every workout, every conversation today.$d$, $d$Christ lives in me, and He is my hope of glory.$d$, $d$Jesus, thank You for living in me. Shine through me today.$d$, $d$As you exercise today, remember that Christ in you goes everywhere you go.$d$, $d$How would today change if you remembered Christ is in you?$d$),
('women', 52, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Rest and Remember$d$, $d$Psalm 103:2$d$, $d$Bless the LORD, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits.$d$, $d$Forgetfulness is a quiet thief. When we forget what God has done, worry grows. Today, rest and remember. List His benefits: forgiveness, healing, rescue, provision, love. A remembering soul is a strong soul.$d$, $d$I bless the Lord with all my soul, and I do not forget His benefits.$d$, $d$I remember Your goodness, Lord. Thank You for all You’ve done.$d$, $d$Rest day. Write a list of ten benefits God has given you.$d$, $d$Which of God’s benefits are you most grateful for today?$d$),
('women', 53, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Glorious Inheritance$d$, $d$Romans 8:17$d$, $d$And if children, then heirs; heirs of God, and joint-heirs with Christ.$d$, $d$Joint-heir with Christ. Whatever belongs to Him, you share. That’s not arrogance; it’s adoption. You may feel small, overlooked, or behind, but in heaven’s records you are a daughter and an heir. Walk today like someone who knows her Father.$d$, $d$I am a child of God and a joint-heir with Christ.$d$, $d$Father, teach me to live like Your daughter.$d$, $d$Stand in front of the mirror and say out loud: “I am a daughter of God.”$d$, $d$What changes when you see yourself as an heir instead of a beggar?$d$),
('women', 54, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Thinking Clearly$d$, $d$Philippians 4:8$d$, $d$Whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things.$d$, $d$What you think on shapes what you see. Paul gives a filter for your mind: true, honorable, just, pure, lovely, good. Run your thoughts through it today, especially your thoughts about yourself. Lies about your worth don’t pass the test. God’s truth does.$d$, $d$I think on what is true, pure, lovely, and praiseworthy.$d$, $d$Guard my thoughts today, Lord. Fill my mind with what is true.$d$, $d$Each time you catch a negative thought about your body today, replace it with a true one.$d$, $d$Which thought about yourself doesn’t pass Philippians 4:8?$d$),
('women', 55, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Understanding Love$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:18$d$, $d$May be able to comprehend with all saints what is the breadth, and length, and depth, and height.$d$, $d$Paul wants you to comprehend something incomprehensible: the dimensions of Christ’s love. It’s wider than your failures, longer than your seasons, deeper than your pain, higher than your dreams. Revelation leads here, to love. Knowing God always ends in knowing how loved you are.$d$, $d$I comprehend the breadth, length, depth, and height of Christ’s love.$d$, $d$Open my understanding to how wide and deep Your love is, Lord.$d$, $d$Stretch in four directions (wide, long, low, high) and pray Ephesians 3:18.$d$, $d$Which dimension of God’s love do you most need right now?$d$),
('women', 56, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$A Teachable Heart$d$, $d$Psalm 25:4-5$d$, $d$Shew me thy ways, O LORD; teach me thy paths. Lead me in thy truth, and teach me.$d$, $d$A teachable heart is a beautiful thing. It says, “I don’t know everything, and I want to learn from You.” Whether you’re learning a new exercise, a new habit, or a new way to love, bring that same humility to God. He is a patient teacher.$d$, $d$I have a teachable heart, and God leads me in His truth.$d$, $d$Teach me Your ways, Lord. I want to learn from You.$d$, $d$Learn proper form for one exercise you’ve been doing wrong.$d$, $d$What is God teaching you in this season?$d$),
('women', 57, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$The Father of Glory$d$, $d$James 1:17$d$, $d$Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning.$d$, $d$Every good gift traces back to Him. The sunrise, a friend’s text, strength in your legs, a good night’s sleep. He doesn’t change His mind about being good to you. When you notice gifts, you start knowing the Giver.$d$, $d$Every good and perfect gift in my life comes from my unchanging Father.$d$, $d$Thank You for every good gift, Father. Help me notice them.$d$, $d$Count gifts on your walk today. Aim for twenty.$d$, $d$What good gift did you almost overlook this week?$d$),
('women', 58, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Revelation Through the Spirit$d$, $d$1 Corinthians 2:10$d$, $d$But God hath revealed them unto us by his Spirit: for the Spirit searcheth all things, yea, the deep things of God.$d$, $d$The Holy Spirit is your teacher and revealer. He searches the deep things of God and makes them known to you. When Scripture suddenly comes alive, when a verse jumps off the page, that’s the Spirit at work. Invite Him into your reading every day.$d$, $d$The Holy Spirit reveals the deep things of God to me.$d$, $d$Holy Spirit, be my teacher. Reveal Jesus to me.$d$, $d$Before reading Scripture today, pause and invite the Holy Spirit to teach you.$d$, $d$When has a verse come alive to you unexpectedly?$d$),
('women', 59, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Rest in Revelation$d$, $d$Exodus 33:14$d$, $d$And he said, My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest.$d$, $d$Moses wanted to know God’s ways, and God answered with His presence and His rest. Sometimes the revelation we need isn’t an answer. It’s His company. His presence is the rest your soul has been looking for.$d$, $d$God’s presence goes with me, and He gives me rest.$d$, $d$Your presence is enough for me, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Take a slow, unhurried walk with no goal except His company.$d$, $d$Where do you need His presence more than His answers?$d$),
('women', 60, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Knowing and Being Known$d$, $d$John 17:3$d$, $d$And this is life eternal, that they might know thee the only true God, and Jesus Christ, whom thou hast sent.$d$, $d$Eternal life isn’t only about forever. It’s about knowing God, starting now. As this month ends, the goal hasn’t been more information. It has been more intimacy. Keep praying Ephesians 1 over yourself. Knowing Him is the life you were made for.$d$, $d$I know the only true God and Jesus Christ, and this is life.$d$, $d$Thank You for letting me know You. Keep drawing me closer, Lord.$d$, $d$Reflect on how your body and spirit have grown this month.$d$, $d$How has your knowing of God grown this month?$d$),
('women', 61, $d$Eyes of My Heart$d$, $d$Morning Prayer$d$, $d$Psalm 143:8$d$, $d$Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk; for I lift up my soul unto thee.$d$, $d$Start tomorrow the way the psalmist did: listening for lovingkindness and asking for direction. Pray your morning prayer from Ephesians. Ask to hear His love before you hear anything else. Then step into the day with your soul lifted to Him.$d$, $d$I hear His lovingkindness in the morning, and He shows me the way to walk.$d$, $d$Let the first voice I hear tomorrow be Your love, Lord.$d$, $d$Set your phone across the room tonight so you start tomorrow with prayer, not a screen.$d$, $d$What would change if His voice came first every morning?$d$),
('women', 62, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$I Bow My Knees$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:14$d$, $d$For this cause I bow my knees unto the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.$d$, $d$Paul’s prayer begins on his knees. Bowing is surrender: an admission that you can’t do life alone, and a declaration that you don’t want to. This month, let your morning start with a bowed heart, even if your knees are sore from yesterday’s leg day.$d$, $d$I bow my knees before the Father, and I surrender my day to Him.$d$, $d$Father, I bow before You. Have Your way in me today.$d$, $d$Begin today by kneeling for one minute of prayer before you stand to stretch.$d$, $d$What does surrender look like for you this season?$d$),
('women', 63, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Named by Him$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:15$d$, $d$Of whom the whole family in heaven and earth is named.$d$, $d$Every family gets its name from Him. Whatever your family story, whether whole, broken, blended, or longing, God is the true Father, and you are named by Him. Your identity doesn’t come from your past or your relationships. It comes from the One who names you His.$d$, $d$I am named by the Father, and I belong to His family.$d$, $d$Father, let Your name over me be louder than every other name I’ve been called.$d$, $d$Pray for each member of your family by name during a walk.$d$, $d$What name has God given you that you need to remember?$d$),
('women', 64, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$According to His Riches$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:16$d$, $d$That he would grant you, according to the riches of his glory, to be strengthened with might by his Spirit in the inner man.$d$, $d$God gives according to His riches, not according to your track record. His glory has no shortage, so His strength for you has no shortage either. When you feel spent, remember the measure He gives by. It’s His wealth, not your reserves.$d$, $d$I am strengthened according to the riches of His glory.$d$, $d$Lord, give to me according to Your riches, not my lack.$d$, $d$Do a strength circuit today and pray Ephesians 3:16 between sets.$d$, $d$Where are you measuring by your lack instead of His riches?$d$),
('women', 65, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Strength Inside$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:16$d$, $d$To be strengthened with might by his Spirit in the inner man.$d$, $d$Your outer strength will rise and fall with age, sleep, and seasons. Your inner strength can keep growing every year. The Spirit strengthens you in the inner woman, where courage, patience, and peace live. Train your body. Let Him train your soul.$d$, $d$I am strengthened with might by His Spirit in my inner woman.$d$, $d$Holy Spirit, make me strong on the inside today.$d$, $d$Hold a plank for as long as you can and pray for inner strength.$d$, $d$Where do you need inner strength more than physical strength?$d$),
('women', 66, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Christ at Home in You$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:17$d$, $d$That Christ may dwell in your hearts by faith.$d$, $d$Dwell means to settle down and be at home. Christ doesn’t want to visit your heart on Sundays. He wants to live there, at home in every room. Even the rooms you keep closed. Even the messy ones. Invite Him in by faith today.$d$, $d$Christ dwells in my heart by faith and is at home in me.$d$, $d$Jesus, make Yourself at home in every room of my heart.$d$, $d$Tidy one space in your home and pray for Jesus to be at home in you.$d$, $d$Is there a room in your heart you’ve kept closed to Him?$d$),
('women', 67, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Rooted$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:17$d$, $d$That ye, being rooted and grounded in love.$d$, $d$Trees with deep roots don’t fall in storms. Paul prays you would be rooted in love: drawing your nourishment, identity, and stability from God’s love. When love is your root, criticism, failure, and storms can shake your branches without uprooting you.$d$, $d$I am rooted and grounded in love.$d$, $d$Lord, send my roots deep into Your love.$d$, $d$Stand barefoot outside for five minutes and pray about being rooted in Him.$d$, $d$What would it mean to draw your security from His love today?$d$),
('women', 68, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Rest in His Love$d$, $d$Zephaniah 3:17$d$, $d$The LORD thy God in the midst of thee is mighty; he will save, he will rejoice over thee with joy; he will rest in his love, he will joy over thee with singing.$d$, $d$God rejoices over you with singing. Read that again slowly. He isn’t tolerating you or waiting for you to improve. He is singing over you. On this rest day, let His love quiet you. You don’t have to perform for a God who already delights in you.$d$, $d$The Lord rejoices over me with joy and sings over me with love.$d$, $d$Quiet me with Your love today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Listen to a worship song lying down, eyes closed.$d$, $d$How does it feel to imagine God singing over you?$d$),
('women', 69, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Grounded$d$, $d$Colossians 2:7$d$, $d$Rooted and built up in him, and stablished in the faith, as ye have been taught, abounding therein with thanksgiving.$d$, $d$Rooted, built up, established, abounding with thanksgiving. Growth in God has a shape: deep roots, strong structure, steady faith, and a grateful heart. Gratitude isn’t just polite. It is a sign of a well-rooted life.$d$, $d$I am rooted and built up in Christ, established in faith, and abounding with thanksgiving.$d$, $d$Make me a woman of deep roots and overflowing gratitude.$d$, $d$Write down five things you’re thankful for about your body.$d$, $d$How does gratitude keep you grounded?$d$),
('women', 70, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Width of His Love$d$, $d$Romans 5:8$d$, $d$But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.$d$, $d$The width of God’s love is wide enough to reach you at your worst. He didn’t wait for you to clean up before loving you. While you were still a sinner, Christ died for you. There is no corner of your life too far for His love to reach.$d$, $d$God’s love is wide enough to reach every part of my life.$d$, $d$Thank You for loving me before I was lovely.$d$, $d$Stretch wide today: arms out, chest open, breathing deep.$d$, $d$What part of your life do you think is outside God’s love?$d$),
('women', 71, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Length of His Love$d$, $d$Jeremiah 31:3$d$, $d$The LORD hath appeared of old unto me, saying, Yea, I have loved thee with an everlasting love: therefore with lovingkindness have I drawn thee.$d$, $d$His love is everlasting. It goes back before you were born and forward forever. It has outlasted every season you’ve walked through, and it will outlast whatever you face today. You can’t outrun it, outgrow it, or exhaust it.$d$, $d$I am loved with an everlasting love.$d$, $d$Draw me with Your lovingkindness, Lord.$d$, $d$Take a longer walk than usual today and thank Him for His long love.$d$, $d$How has God’s love outlasted a hard season in your life?$d$),
('women', 72, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Depth of His Love$d$, $d$Psalm 139:8$d$, $d$If I ascend up into heaven, thou art there: if I make my bed in hell, behold, thou art there.$d$, $d$There is no depth you can sink to where God’s love doesn’t reach. Depression, grief, regret, the lowest places, He is there. You never fall below the reach of His love. If you’re in a low place today, He is already with you there.$d$, $d$There is no depth too deep for God’s love to reach me.$d$, $d$Meet me in the low places, Lord.$d$, $d$Do slow, deep squats today and remember His love reaches every depth.$d$, $d$When has God met you in a low place?$d$),
('women', 73, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Height of His Love$d$, $d$Psalm 103:11$d$, $d$For as the heaven is high above the earth, so great is his mercy toward them that fear him.$d$, $d$Look up. As high as the sky is above you, that’s how great His mercy is toward you. His love lifts you higher than your circumstances and gives you a view above the struggle. When life feels small and crowded, look up.$d$, $d$His mercy toward me is as high as the heavens.$d$, $d$Lift my eyes today, Lord, to the height of Your love.$d$, $d$Stretch tall with your arms overhead and take ten deep breaths.$d$, $d$What would you see differently from His higher view?$d$),
('women', 74, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Love Beyond Knowing$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:19$d$, $d$And to know the love of Christ, which passeth knowledge.$d$, $d$Paul prays that you would know a love that surpasses knowledge. It’s a holy paradox. You can experience more of His love than you could ever explain. Don’t wait to understand it before you receive it. Let it go deeper than your mind can follow.$d$, $d$I know the love of Christ that surpasses knowledge.$d$, $d$Let me experience Your love beyond what I can understand.$d$, $d$Hug someone you love today and let it remind you of His love.$d$, $d$When have you felt God’s love in a way you couldn’t explain?$d$),
('women', 75, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Filled to Fullness$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:19$d$, $d$That ye might be filled with all the fulness of God.$d$, $d$This is where Paul’s prayer ends: filled with all the fullness of God. Not a little more spiritual. Filled. Many women feel empty from pouring out for others. God wants to fill you so completely that you overflow. Receive before you give today.$d$, $d$I am filled with all the fullness of God.$d$, $d$Fill me up, Lord, until I overflow.$d$, $d$Rest day. Do something that refills you: a bath, a book, a nap.$d$, $d$What empties you, and how can you let God fill you?$d$),
('women', 76, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Love Is Patient$d$, $d$1 Corinthians 13:4$d$, $d$Charity suffereth long, and is kind; charity envieth not; charity vaunteth not itself, is not puffed up.$d$, $d$Being rooted in God’s love changes how you love others. Love is patient and kind, not envious or proud. It also changes how you love yourself. Be patient with your progress and kind to your body. Envy no one’s journey.$d$, $d$God’s love in me is patient, kind, and free from envy.$d$, $d$Make me patient and kind, beginning with how I treat myself.$d$, $d$Do today’s workout at a patient pace without comparing yourself to anyone.$d$, $d$Where do you need to be more patient with yourself?$d$),
('women', 77, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$No Fear in Love$d$, $d$1 John 4:18$d$, $d$There is no fear in love; but perfect love casteth out fear.$d$, $d$Fear and love can’t share the same room for long. As His perfect love fills you, fear has to leave: fear of failing, fear of what people think, fear of the future. You don’t fight fear by trying harder. You let love push it out.$d$, $d$Perfect love casts out all fear in me.$d$, $d$Lord, let Your love push every fear out of my heart.$d$, $d$Do one exercise you’ve been afraid to try, with good form and a spotter if needed.$d$, $d$What fear is His love pushing out right now?$d$),
('women', 78, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Loved to Love$d$, $d$1 John 4:19$d$, $d$We love him, because he first loved us.$d$, $d$You don’t have to manufacture love for God. You respond to the love He first gave. Love begins with Him. When you feel dry, don’t try harder to love Him. Sit with how much He loves you, and love will rise in response.$d$, $d$I love God because He first loved me.$d$, $d$Remind me how much You love me, so I can love You back.$d$, $d$Walk for 20 minutes thanking God for specific ways He loves you.$d$, $d$How has God shown you His love this week?$d$),
('women', 79, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Nothing Can Separate$d$, $d$Romans 8:38-39$d$, $d$For I am persuaded, that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor powers, nor things present, nor things to come, Nor height, nor depth, nor any other creature, shall be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord.$d$, $d$Paul makes a list of everything that could possibly come between you and God’s love, and then crosses them all out. Nothing present, nothing future, nothing high or deep. Your worst day can’t separate you from His love. Neither can your best effort earn more of it.$d$, $d$Nothing can separate me from the love of God in Christ Jesus.$d$, $d$I am persuaded, Lord. Nothing can separate me from You.$d$, $d$Write Romans 8:38-39 on a card and keep it in your gym bag.$d$, $d$What have you feared might separate you from God’s love?$d$),
('women', 80, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Abide in Love$d$, $d$John 15:9$d$, $d$As the Father hath loved me, so have I loved you: continue ye in my love.$d$, $d$Jesus loves you the way the Father loves Him. Let that sink in. Then He gives one instruction: continue in it. Stay. Abide. Live there. Don’t visit His love on good days and move out on hard ones. Make His love your address.$d$, $d$I abide in the love of Jesus every day.$d$, $d$Jesus, I choose to live in Your love today.$d$, $d$Set a reminder three times today that says “Stay in His love.”$d$, $d$What pulls you out of abiding in His love?$d$),
('women', 81, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Kindness of God$d$, $d$Titus 3:4-5$d$, $d$But after that the kindness and love of God our Saviour toward man appeared, Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his mercy he saved us.$d$, $d$God’s kindness appeared not because of your works but because of His mercy. You weren’t saved by being good enough, and you won’t be loved more by being disciplined enough. Your workouts are worship, not payment. Rest in His kindness.$d$, $d$I am saved by His kindness and mercy, not by my works.$d$, $d$Thank You that Your love doesn’t depend on my performance.$d$, $d$Today, exercise from gratitude, not guilt. Choose a movement you enjoy.$d$, $d$Where are you still trying to earn God’s kindness?$d$),
('women', 82, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Rest Day: Beloved$d$, $d$Song of Solomon 2:4$d$, $d$He brought me to the banqueting house, and his banner over me was love.$d$, $d$His banner over you is love. A banner marks what belongs to a king. Over your life, over your body, over your past and future, God has raised one banner: love. Rest under it today.$d$, $d$God’s banner over me is love.$d$, $d$Let me rest under Your banner of love today.$d$, $d$Rest day. Enjoy a nourishing meal slowly, without distraction.$d$, $d$What would it look like to live under His banner of love?$d$),
('women', 83, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Love One Another$d$, $d$John 13:34$d$, $d$A new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another; as I have loved you, that ye also love one another.$d$, $d$Love received becomes love given. The women around you are carrying more than you know. Being rooted in Christ’s love gives you something to offer. Encourage a sister today. Send the text. Pray the prayer. Love the way you’ve been loved.$d$, $d$I love others as Christ has loved me.$d$, $d$Show me who needs Your love through me today.$d$, $d$Invite a friend to walk or work out with you this week.$d$, $d$Who needs encouragement from you today?$d$),
('women', 84, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Love Covers$d$, $d$1 Peter 4:8$d$, $d$And above all things have fervent charity among yourselves: for charity shall cover the multitude of sins.$d$, $d$Fervent love covers a multitude of sins. Not ignoring them, but choosing grace. Some of the hardest love to give is to the people closest to you. Ask God for fervent love today, the kind that keeps no record of wrongs.$d$, $d$I walk in fervent love that covers offenses.$d$, $d$Give me grace to cover offenses with love today.$d$, $d$Release one offense in prayer during today’s workout.$d$, $d$Is there an offense you need to cover with love?$d$),
('women', 85, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Love in Action$d$, $d$1 John 3:18$d$, $d$My little children, let us not love in word, neither in tongue; but in deed and in truth.$d$, $d$Love shows up in deeds: a meal for a new mom, a ride for a friend, a listening ear. Real love moves. Your strong body is a gift you can use to serve others. Let your strength become someone else’s help today.$d$, $d$I love in deed and in truth, not just in words.$d$, $d$Show me one practical way to love someone today.$d$, $d$Do a practical act of service that requires physical effort today.$d$, $d$How can your strength serve someone else this week?$d$),
('women', 86, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Love Never Fails$d$, $d$1 Corinthians 13:8$d$, $d$Charity never faileth.$d$, $d$Plans fail. Bodies change. Seasons end. But love never fails. When everything else shifts, God’s love remains the steady ground under your feet. Build your life on the one thing that never fails.$d$, $d$God’s love never fails me.$d$, $d$Thank You that Your love is the one thing that never fails.$d$, $d$Repeat a workout from earlier this month and notice your growth.$d$, $d$Where have you seen God’s love prove faithful?$d$),
('women', 87, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Kept in His Love$d$, $d$Jude 1:21$d$, $d$Keep yourselves in the love of God, looking for the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ unto eternal life.$d$, $d$You can’t make God love you, but you can keep yourself in His love: staying near, remembering, receiving. Habits of prayer, worship, and the Word are how you stay in the place where love is felt and known.$d$, $d$I keep myself in the love of God.$d$, $d$Help me build habits that keep me close to Your love.$d$, $d$Choose one daily habit that keeps you in His love and start it today.$d$, $d$What habits help you stay aware of God’s love?$d$),
('women', 88, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Love Made Complete$d$, $d$1 John 4:12$d$, $d$If we love one another, God dwelleth in us, and his love is perfected in us.$d$, $d$God’s love is made complete in you as you love others. It flows in and flows through. A love that only flows in becomes stagnant, like water with no outlet. Let His love keep moving through you to the people around you.$d$, $d$God dwells in me, and His love is made complete as I love others.$d$, $d$Let Your love flow through me, not just to me.$d$, $d$Encourage someone in the Eden Strong community today.$d$, $d$Where can God’s love flow through you this week?$d$),
('women', 89, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Rest Day: Secure$d$, $d$Psalm 36:7$d$, $d$How excellent is thy lovingkindness, O God! therefore the children of men put their trust under the shadow of thy wings.$d$, $d$Under the shadow of His wings is the safest place you can be. His lovingkindness is excellent: reliable, generous, and kind. Rest today knowing you are covered and secure.$d$, $d$I trust under the shadow of His wings, secure in His lovingkindness.$d$, $d$Cover me today, Lord. I rest under Your wings.$d$, $d$Rest day. Stretch gently and breathe deeply for ten minutes.$d$, $d$What helps you feel secure in God’s love?$d$),
('women', 90, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Love That Transforms$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 5:14$d$, $d$For the love of Christ constraineth us.$d$, $d$Christ’s love compels you. It moves you, motivates you, and keeps you going when willpower fades. When love is your motivation instead of fear, change lasts longer. Let His love be the reason you take care of yourself and serve others.$d$, $d$The love of Christ compels me.$d$, $d$Let Your love be my motivation in everything.$d$, $d$Before today’s workout, write why you take care of your body, starting with love.$d$, $d$Is fear or love your main motivation for change?$d$),
('women', 91, $d$Rooted and Grounded in Love$d$, $d$Rooted to Rise$d$, $d$Jeremiah 17:7-8$d$, $d$Blessed is the man that trusteth in the LORD, and whose hope the LORD is. For he shall be as a tree planted by the waters, and that spreadeth out her roots by the river.$d$, $d$A tree planted by water doesn’t panic in drought. Its roots reach the river. As this month of being rooted in love ends, notice where your roots have grown deeper. You are planted by living water, and your leaves will stay green in every season.$d$, $d$I am planted by the waters, rooted in His love, and I will flourish in every season.$d$, $d$Keep my roots deep in You, Lord, in every season.$d$, $d$Plant something or care for a plant this week as a reminder of being rooted.$d$, $d$How have your roots in God’s love grown this month?$d$),
('women', 92, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$John 10:10$d$, $d$The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy: I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly.$d$, $d$Jesus names two agendas: the thief’s and His own. One steals, kills, and destroys. The other gives life to the full, until it overflows. Not just survival. Not just getting through the week. Abundance. This month, learn to recognize what steals from you and receive what He came to give.$d$, $d$Jesus came that I may have and enjoy life, and have it in abundance.$d$, $d$Jesus, I receive the abundant life You came to give.$d$, $d$Do something today purely because it makes you feel alive.$d$, $d$What does abundant life look like for you right now?$d$),
('women', 93, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Know the Thief$d$, $d$John 10:10$d$, $d$The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy.$d$, $d$The enemy’s methods haven’t changed: steal your joy, kill your hope, destroy your relationships and health. Naming them helps you resist them. Worry, comparison, exhaustion, shame: these are thieves. They don’t get your life. Jesus already paid for it.$d$, $d$I recognize the thief’s lies, and I refuse to let him steal my joy.$d$, $d$Lord, expose anything that’s been stealing from my life.$d$, $d$Remove one thing that drains you: an app, a habit, or a late-night routine.$d$, $d$What has been stealing your peace or joy lately?$d$),
('women', 94, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$The Good Shepherd$d$, $d$John 10:11$d$, $d$I am the good shepherd: the good shepherd giveth his life for the sheep.$d$, $d$The one who promises you abundant life is the one who gave His life for you. That’s how you know He can be trusted. Shepherds lead, feed, protect, and rescue. Let Him lead you today, even when the path isn’t the one you would have chosen.$d$, $d$Jesus is my Good Shepherd, and He gave His life for me.$d$, $d$Lead me today, Good Shepherd. I trust You.$d$, $d$Take a 20-minute walk and let Psalm 23 guide your prayers.$d$, $d$Where do you need your Shepherd’s leading today?$d$),
('women', 95, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$I Know His Voice$d$, $d$John 10:27$d$, $d$My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me.$d$, $d$Sheep know their shepherd’s voice through time spent with him. The more time you spend with Jesus, the easier it becomes to recognize Him among all the other voices: culture, critics, your inner doubts. His voice always leads to life.$d$, $d$I hear my Shepherd’s voice, and I follow Him.$d$, $d$Tune my ears to Your voice, Jesus.$d$, $d$Spend your workout today with no music, listening for God.$d$, $d$How can you tell the difference between God’s voice and fear?$d$),
('women', 96, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Overflowing Cup$d$, $d$Psalm 23:5$d$, $d$Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over.$d$, $d$Abundance isn’t the absence of enemies. It’s a full table in their presence. God doesn’t always remove the hard things before He blesses you. Sometimes He sets the table right in the middle of them. Your cup can overflow even now.$d$, $d$My cup runs over, even in the presence of difficulty.$d$, $d$Thank You for the table You’ve prepared for me today.$d$, $d$Prepare a beautiful, nourishing meal and eat it slowly.$d$, $d$Where is your cup running over, even in a hard season?$d$),
('women', 97, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Goodness Follows$d$, $d$Psalm 23:6$d$, $d$Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the LORD for ever.$d$, $d$Follow here means to pursue. Goodness and mercy are chasing you. Not occasionally, but all the days of your life. When you feel hunted by worry, remember what’s actually behind you. God’s goodness is pursuing you.$d$, $d$Goodness and mercy pursue me all the days of my life.$d$, $d$Open my eyes to Your goodness chasing me today.$d$, $d$Go for a jog or brisk walk and picture goodness and mercy running with you.$d$, $d$Where have you seen God’s goodness following you lately?$d$),
('women', 98, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Rest in Green Pastures$d$, $d$Psalm 23:1$d$, $d$The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want.$d$, $d$With the Lord as your shepherd, you lack nothing you truly need. That’s abundance. Not having everything, but needing nothing outside of Him. On this rest day, let contentment settle you.$d$, $d$The Lord is my shepherd; I lack nothing.$d$, $d$Lord, You are enough for me.$d$, $d$Rest day. Spend time outdoors on grass or in a park.$d$, $d$What do you truly need today that only He can provide?$d$),
('women', 99, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Living Water$d$, $d$John 7:38$d$, $d$He that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water.$d$, $d$Abundant life isn’t a pond. It’s a river flowing out of you. When you believe, living water rises up and spills over into your home, work, and friendships. You weren’t made to hold God’s life in. You were made to let it flow.$d$, $d$Rivers of living water flow out of me.$d$, $d$Let Your life flow through me to everyone I meet today.$d$, $d$Drink at least eight glasses of water today and thank God for living water.$d$, $d$Who needs the overflow of God’s life in you?$d$),
('women', 100, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Abundant Grace$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 9:8$d$, $d$And God is able to make all grace abound toward you; that ye, always having all sufficiency in all things, may abound to every good work.$d$, $d$All grace, always, all sufficiency, all things, every good work. God’s grace isn’t rationed. It abounds so that you can abound. If you’re running low, it isn’t because His supply is short. Come back to the source and receive more.$d$, $d$God makes all grace abound toward me, and I have all sufficiency in all things.$d$, $d$Lord, I receive Your abounding grace for every need today.$d$, $d$Complete a full workout today and thank God for the grace to finish.$d$, $d$Where do you need abounding grace this week?$d$),
('women', 101, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Joy Made Full$d$, $d$John 15:11$d$, $d$These things have I spoken unto you, that my joy might remain in you, and that your joy might be full.$d$, $d$Jesus wants His joy to remain in you, and your joy to be full. Not fleeting happiness, but His own joy taking up residence. Full joy can sit alongside tears. It is rooted in Him, not in circumstances.$d$, $d$The joy of Jesus remains in me, and my joy is full.$d$, $d$Fill me with Your joy today, Jesus.$d$, $d$Laugh today: call a friend, watch something funny, or play with your kids.$d$, $d$What steals your joy, and what restores it?$d$),
('women', 102, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$A Fruitful Life$d$, $d$Galatians 5:22-23$d$, $d$But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith, Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.$d$, $d$Abundant life looks like fruit: love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, self-control. Notice self-control is on the list. Discipline in eating and training isn’t opposed to the Spirit. It is fruit of the Spirit.$d$, $d$The fruit of the Spirit grows in me, including self-control.$d$, $d$Holy Spirit, grow Your fruit in me, especially where I struggle.$d$, $d$Choose one area where you’ll practice self-control today.$d$, $d$Which fruit of the Spirit do you most want to grow this month?$d$),
('women', 103, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Life in the Word$d$, $d$Deuteronomy 8:3$d$, $d$Man doth not live by bread only, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of the LORD doth man live.$d$, $d$Your body needs food, and your soul needs the Word. Both are daily. You wouldn’t skip meals for a week and expect strength, yet we often skip Scripture and wonder why we feel weak. Feed your spirit as faithfully as you feed your body.$d$, $d$I live by every word that comes from the mouth of God.$d$, $d$Lord, feed me with Your Word today.$d$, $d$Pair your breakfast with five minutes of Scripture reading.$d$, $d$How is your spiritual diet compared to your physical one?$d$),
('women', 104, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Abundantly Above$d$, $d$Ephesians 3:20$d$, $d$Now unto him that is able to do exceeding abundantly above all that we ask or think, according to the power that worketh in us.$d$, $d$God is able to do exceeding abundantly above anything you ask or imagine. Whatever you’re dreaming about, He can do more. And notice where the power works: in us. Dream big, pray boldly, and trust the power already at work in you.$d$, $d$God is able to do exceeding abundantly above all I ask or think.$d$, $d$Lord, I bring You my biggest prayers. Do more than I can imagine.$d$, $d$Write down a big, bold prayer for your health and your family.$d$, $d$What would you ask God for if you truly believed He could do more?$d$),
('women', 105, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Rest Day: Satisfied$d$, $d$Psalm 107:9$d$, $d$For he satisfieth the longing soul, and filleth the hungry soul with goodness.$d$, $d$There’s a hunger only God can fill. We try to satisfy it with food, shopping, approval, or busyness. But He satisfies the longing soul with goodness. Today, bring your deepest hunger to Him.$d$, $d$God satisfies my longing soul and fills me with goodness.$d$, $d$Satisfy me with Your goodness, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. When you feel restless, pause and pray before reaching for anything.$d$, $d$What are you hungry for that only God can satisfy?$d$),
('women', 106, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$He Restores Years$d$, $d$Joel 2:25$d$, $d$And I will restore to you the years that the locust hath eaten.$d$, $d$God restores what was eaten: years lost to sickness, sin, grief, or other people’s choices. He doesn’t just stop the thief. He gives back. Whatever season feels wasted, bring it to Him. He is a God of restoration.$d$, $d$God restores the years that were stolen from me.$d$, $d$Lord, I bring You the years that feel lost. Restore them.$d$, $d$Restart a healthy habit you let go of during a hard season.$d$, $d$What has been taken that you’re trusting God to restore?$d$),
('women', 107, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Abundance in Giving$d$, $d$Luke 6:38$d$, $d$Give, and it shall be given unto you; good measure, pressed down, and shaken together, and running over.$d$, $d$Abundance flows through generosity. When you give your time, encouragement, or resources, God gives back in a measure pressed down and running over. A clenched hand can’t receive. An open one can.$d$, $d$I give generously, and God gives back to me in good measure, running over.$d$, $d$Make me generous with what You’ve given me.$d$, $d$Give something away today: time, encouragement, or a meal.$d$, $d$Where is God inviting you to be more generous?$d$),
('women', 108, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Life in His Presence$d$, $d$Psalm 16:11$d$, $d$Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; at thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore.$d$, $d$Fullness of joy is found in one place: His presence. Not in the perfect body, the perfect home, or the perfect life. When you spend time with Him, joy grows. He shows you the path of life as you walk with Him.$d$, $d$In God’s presence is fullness of joy, and He shows me the path of life.$d$, $d$Draw me into Your presence today, where my joy is full.$d$, $d$Worship for ten minutes before your workout.$d$, $d$When do you feel most aware of God’s presence?$d$),
('women', 109, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Renewed Daily$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 4:16$d$, $d$For which cause we faint not; but though our outward man perish, yet the inward man is renewed day by day.$d$, $d$Your outward body will age. That’s part of being human. But your inward self can be renewed every single day. Take care of your body with gratitude, and put your deepest hope in the renewal happening inside.$d$, $d$My inner self is renewed day by day.$d$, $d$Renew me today, Lord, from the inside out.$d$, $d$Do a mobility session today and thank God for how your body moves.$d$, $d$How have you been renewed inwardly this year?$d$),
('women', 110, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Good Things$d$, $d$Psalm 84:11$d$, $d$For the LORD God is a sun and shield: the LORD will give grace and glory: no good thing will he withhold from them that walk uprightly.$d$, $d$God is your sun and your shield: light and protection. And He doesn’t withhold good things from those who walk with Him. If He’s holding something back, trust that it isn’t good for you right now. His no is protection, not punishment.$d$, $d$The Lord is my sun and shield, and He withholds no good thing from me.$d$, $d$I trust You with what You give and what You hold back.$d$, $d$Get some morning sunlight and thank God for being your sun and shield.$d$, $d$Is there something God has withheld that you can trust Him with?$d$),
('women', 111, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Life and Peace$d$, $d$Romans 8:6$d$, $d$For to be carnally minded is death; but to be spiritually minded is life and peace.$d$, $d$Where your mind goes, your life follows. A mind set on the flesh leads to death. A mind set on the Spirit leads to life and peace. This is a daily choice. What you dwell on today shapes how alive and peaceful you feel.$d$, $d$My mind is set on the Spirit, and I have life and peace.$d$, $d$Set my mind on You today, Holy Spirit.$d$, $d$Start today’s workout by praying one minute about what your mind is set on.$d$, $d$What are you setting your mind on most days?$d$),
('women', 112, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Rest Day: Delight$d$, $d$Isaiah 58:13-14$d$, $d$And call the sabbath a delight... Then shalt thou delight thyself in the LORD.$d$, $d$God calls rest a delight, not a burden. Sabbath isn’t a day of doing nothing. It’s a day of enjoying God, family, and His good gifts without the pressure of producing. Delight in Him today.$d$, $d$I call rest a delight, and I delight myself in the Lord.$d$, $d$Teach me to delight in rest, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Plan one delightful thing to do with your family.$d$, $d$What would make rest a delight for you?$d$),
('women', 113, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Abundant Pardon$d$, $d$Isaiah 55:7$d$, $d$Let him return unto the LORD, and he will have mercy upon him; and to our God, for he will abundantly pardon.$d$, $d$God’s pardon is abundant, not stingy. If you’ve wandered from Him, or from your goals, or into old habits, return. He doesn’t pardon reluctantly. He abundantly pardons. There is always a way back.$d$, $d$God abundantly pardons me, and I return to Him freely.$d$, $d$I’m coming back to You, Lord. Thank You for abundant mercy.$d$, $d$Return to a habit you dropped, without shame.$d$, $d$Where do you need to receive abundant pardon today?$d$),
('women', 114, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Health and Life$d$, $d$3 John 1:2$d$, $d$Beloved, I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth.$d$, $d$John prays for health of body and prosperity of soul together. God cares about both. Your physical health matters to Him, and so does the health of your soul. One isn’t more spiritual than the other. Tend both with care.$d$, $d$I prosper and walk in health, even as my soul prospers.$d$, $d$Lord, prosper my body and my soul together.$d$, $d$Schedule any health checkups you’ve been putting off.$d$, $d$Which needs more care right now: your body or your soul?$d$),
('women', 115, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Overflowing Hope$d$, $d$Romans 15:13$d$, $d$Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, through the power of the Holy Ghost.$d$, $d$God fills you with joy and peace as you believe, so that you overflow with hope. Hope isn’t something you have to manufacture. It overflows when you’re filled with Him. Let the Spirit fill you until hope spills over.$d$, $d$I abound in hope through the power of the Holy Spirit.$d$, $d$God of hope, fill me with joy and peace as I trust You.$d$, $d$Encourage someone today with a word of hope.$d$, $d$Who in your life needs some of your overflowing hope?$d$),
('women', 116, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Not Lacking$d$, $d$Psalm 34:10$d$, $d$The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger: but they that seek the LORD shall not want any good thing.$d$, $d$Even strong lions go hungry. Strength alone doesn’t guarantee provision. But those who seek the Lord won’t lack any good thing. Your security isn’t in your own strength. It’s in seeking Him.$d$, $d$I seek the Lord, and I lack no good thing.$d$, $d$I seek You first today, Lord.$d$, $d$Pray before planning today’s meals and workouts.$d$, $d$Where are you relying on your own strength to provide?$d$),
('women', 117, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Fullness Shared$d$, $d$John 1:16$d$, $d$And of his fulness have all we received, and grace for grace.$d$, $d$Grace upon grace, wave after wave of it. Out of His fullness, you receive again and again. There is no last wave. When one grace is used up, another is already on its way.$d$, $d$Out of His fullness I receive grace upon grace.$d$, $d$Thank You for grace that keeps coming, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a workout with intervals, and between each, thank God for another wave of grace.$d$, $d$What grace have you received this week?$d$),
('women', 118, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Rest Day: Quiet Waters$d$, $d$Isaiah 32:18$d$, $d$And my people shall dwell in a peaceable habitation, and in sure dwellings, and in quiet resting places.$d$, $d$God promises His people peaceful homes and quiet resting places. Make your home a place of peace today. Turn down the noise, light a candle, and rest in the quiet He provides.$d$, $d$I dwell in a peaceful habitation and quiet resting place.$d$, $d$Make my home a place of Your peace, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Create a quiet corner in your home for prayer.$d$, $d$How can you make your home more peaceful?$d$),
('women', 119, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Life More Abundant$d$, $d$John 10:9$d$, $d$I am the door: by me if any man enter in, he shall be saved, and shall go in and out, and find pasture.$d$, $d$Jesus is the door to life. Through Him you go in and out and find pasture. Abundant life isn’t found by trying every door. It’s found through one. As you walk through your days, keep coming back through Him.$d$, $d$Jesus is my door, and through Him I find pasture.$d$, $d$Jesus, You are the way to life. I come through You.$d$, $d$Take a walk and pray through each part of your day.$d$, $d$What doors have you tried that didn’t lead to life?$d$),
('women', 120, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Choose Life$d$, $d$Deuteronomy 30:19$d$, $d$I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live.$d$, $d$God sets two paths before you and urges you: choose life. Every day presents small choices toward life or away from it: what you eat, how you speak, what you watch. Your choices affect not only you but those who come after you.$d$, $d$I choose life, and my family is blessed by my choices.$d$, $d$Help me choose life in every small decision today.$d$, $d$Make one life-giving choice today that your future self will thank you for.$d$, $d$What small choice could you make today that chooses life?$d$),
('women', 121, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$An Abundant Year$d$, $d$Psalm 65:11$d$, $d$Thou crownest the year with thy goodness; and thy paths drop fatness.$d$, $d$God crowns the year with His goodness. As this month ends, look back at the abundance you’ve received: grace, strength, joy, and provision. Keep walking His paths. They overflow with good things.$d$, $d$God crowns my year with His goodness.$d$, $d$Thank You for crowning this year with Your goodness.$d$, $d$Celebrate one win from this month with a healthy treat or a fun outing.$d$, $d$What abundance have you noticed this month?$d$),
('women', 122, $d$Life to the Full$d$, $d$Abundance in the Ordinary$d$, $d$Ecclesiastes 3:13$d$, $d$And also that every man should eat and drink, and enjoy the good of all his labour, it is the gift of God.$d$, $d$Abundant life isn’t only in mountaintop moments. It’s in an ordinary Tuesday: a good meal, honest work, a body that moves, a family around the table. Enjoying these simple gifts is not shallow. Scripture calls it the gift of God. Notice the ordinary abundance today.$d$, $d$I enjoy the good of my labor as a gift from God.$d$, $d$Open my eyes to the abundance hidden in ordinary days.$d$, $d$Enjoy a meal today without your phone, savoring every bite.$d$, $d$What ordinary gift do you want to enjoy more fully?$d$),
('women', 123, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$He Carried It$d$, $d$Isaiah 53:4$d$, $d$Surely he hath borne our griefs, and carried our sorrows.$d$, $d$Griefs, sicknesses, weaknesses, sorrows: Jesus carried them. The word surely means this isn’t a maybe. Whatever you’re carrying in your body or heart this month, He has already carried it to the cross. You don’t have to carry it alone.$d$, $d$The Lord has taken my griefs and carried my sorrows and pains.$d$, $d$Jesus, thank You for carrying what I could never carry.$d$, $d$Take a gentle walk and hand each burden to Jesus, one at a time.$d$, $d$What are you carrying that Jesus already carried?$d$),
('women', 124, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$By His Stripes$d$, $d$Isaiah 53:5$d$, $d$But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed.$d$, $d$Every stripe Jesus took was for you: for your peace, for your wholeness, for your healing. The punishment that brings you peace fell on Him. Healing is part of what He purchased. Receive it by faith, and keep praying, believing, and taking wise steps for your health.$d$, $d$By His stripes I am healed and made whole.$d$, $d$Thank You, Jesus, for the price You paid for my healing and peace.$d$, $d$Read Isaiah 53 aloud slowly, then rest in gratitude.$d$, $d$Where do you need to receive His healing today?$d$),
('women', 125, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Forget Not$d$, $d$Psalm 103:2-3$d$, $d$Bless the LORD, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits: Who forgiveth all thine iniquities; who healeth all thy diseases.$d$, $d$Forgiveness and healing appear side by side. God cares about your soul and your body. When you bless Him, you remember: He forgives all, He heals all. Gratitude strengthens faith. Speak His benefits out loud today.$d$, $d$I bless the Lord and do not forget His benefits. He forgives all my sins and heals all my diseases.$d$, $d$I remember Your benefits, Lord. Thank You for forgiving and healing.$d$, $d$List His benefits during today’s stretch, one benefit per stretch.$d$, $d$Which of God’s benefits have you forgotten lately?$d$),
('women', 126, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Redeemed from the Pit$d$, $d$Psalm 103:4$d$, $d$Who redeemeth thy life from destruction; who crowneth thee with lovingkindness and tender mercies.$d$, $d$God doesn’t just pull you out of the pit. He crowns you. From destruction to a crown of lovingkindness: that’s the journey of redemption. Whatever pit you’ve known, whether illness, depression, or addiction, He is in the business of lifting and crowning.$d$, $d$God redeems my life from the pit and crowns me with lovingkindness and tender mercies.$d$, $d$Lift me higher, Lord, and crown me with Your mercy.$d$, $d$Stand tall and do a posture stretch, remembering you wear His crown.$d$, $d$What pit has God brought you out of?$d$),
('women', 127, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Renewed Like the Eagle$d$, $d$Psalm 103:5$d$, $d$Who satisfieth thy mouth with good things; so that thy youth is renewed like the eagle’s.$d$, $d$God satisfies you with good things and renews your strength like the eagle’s. Renewal isn’t only for the young. It’s for anyone who receives His good things. Nourish your body with good food and your soul with His goodness.$d$, $d$God satisfies me with good things, and my youth is renewed like the eagle’s.$d$, $d$Renew my strength today, Lord. Satisfy me with good things.$d$, $d$Plan your meals this week around foods that nourish and energize you.$d$, $d$Where do you need renewal this month?$d$),
('women', 128, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Life to My Flesh$d$, $d$Proverbs 4:20-22$d$, $d$My son, attend to my words; incline thine ear unto my sayings. Let them not depart from thine eyes; keep them in the midst of thine heart. For they are life unto those that find them, and health to all their flesh.$d$, $d$God’s Word is health to all your flesh. As you attend to it, keep it before your eyes, and hold it in your heart, it brings life to your whole body. Take the Word like medicine, as your routine says: daily, consistently, believing.$d$, $d$God’s Word is life to me and health to my whole body.$d$, $d$Lord, let Your Word bring health to my body and life to my soul.$d$, $d$Write a healing verse on a card and put it on your bathroom mirror.$d$, $d$How can you keep God’s Word before your eyes this week?$d$),
('women', 129, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Rest and Be Healed$d$, $d$Psalm 147:3$d$, $d$He healeth the broken in heart, and bindeth up their wounds.$d$, $d$Some wounds are invisible: a broken heart, a betrayal, a loss. God heals those too. He binds up wounds gently, like a skilled physician. On this rest day, let Him tend to the places that still ache.$d$, $d$God heals my broken heart and binds up my wounds.$d$, $d$Heal the places in my heart that still hurt, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Journal about a hurt you want to give to God.$d$, $d$What heart wound do you want God to heal?$d$),
('women', 130, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$The Lord Who Heals$d$, $d$Exodus 15:26$d$, $d$For I am the LORD that healeth thee.$d$, $d$One of God’s names is Jehovah Rapha: the Lord who heals you. Healing isn’t just something He does. It’s who He is. He heals through miracles, through medicine, through doctors, through rest, and through time. Trust the Healer in every form His healing takes.$d$, $d$The Lord is my healer.$d$, $d$Jehovah Rapha, I trust You as my healer in every way You choose to heal.$d$, $d$Thank God for doctors, nurses, and medicine that He uses to heal.$d$, $d$How has God healed you in the past?$d$),
('women', 131, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Touch His Garment$d$, $d$Mark 5:34$d$, $d$And he said unto her, Daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole; go in peace, and be whole of thy plague.$d$, $d$She pressed through the crowd, weak and ashamed, just to touch His robe. Jesus didn’t just heal her body. He called her Daughter and sent her in peace. He sees the woman who reaches for Him. Press in today. He calls you Daughter too.$d$, $d$I am God’s daughter, and my faith makes me whole.$d$, $d$Jesus, I’m reaching for You. Make me whole.$d$, $d$Press through a tough set today and remember the woman who pressed through the crowd.$d$, $d$What are you pressing through to reach Jesus?$d$),
('women', 132, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Prayer of Faith$d$, $d$James 5:15$d$, $d$And the prayer of faith shall save the sick, and the Lord shall raise him up.$d$, $d$God invites us to pray for healing with faith. Don’t be afraid to ask boldly. Gather your sisters, pray together, and trust the Lord to raise up. Prayer is not a last resort. It’s a first response.$d$, $d$I pray the prayer of faith, and the Lord raises up the sick.$d$, $d$Lord, I bring You my body and the bodies of those I love.$d$, $d$Pray for someone who is sick by name during today’s walk.$d$, $d$Who needs your prayer of faith this week?$d$),
('women', 133, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Whole Person$d$, $d$1 Thessalonians 5:23$d$, $d$And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly; and I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless.$d$, $d$God cares about your whole self: spirit, soul, and body. Faith that ignores the body is incomplete, and fitness that ignores the soul is empty. Eden Strong exists because God wants all of you healthy and whole.$d$, $d$God preserves my whole spirit, soul, and body.$d$, $d$God of peace, make me whole in spirit, soul, and body.$d$, $d$Today, do something for each part: pray (spirit), journal (soul), move (body).$d$, $d$Which part of you has been most neglected?$d$),
('women', 134, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$A Merry Heart$d$, $d$Proverbs 17:22$d$, $d$A merry heart doeth good like a medicine: but a broken spirit drieth the bones.$d$, $d$Joy is medicine. Laughter heals. A merry heart does good to your whole body. If you’ve been carrying heaviness, look for joy on purpose today. Laugh with friends, play with your kids, and let joy do its healing work.$d$, $d$My merry heart does me good like medicine.$d$, $d$Lord, restore my joy and let it bring healing to my body.$d$, $d$Do a playful workout: dance, jump rope, or play outside with your kids.$d$, $d$When did you last laugh until it hurt?$d$),
('women', 135, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Peace Over Anxiety$d$, $d$Proverbs 14:30$d$, $d$A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.$d$, $d$A peaceful heart gives life to the body. Envy and anxiety slowly wear it down. Your emotional health affects your physical health. Guard your peace and release comparison. Your body will thank you.$d$, $d$My sound and peaceful heart gives life to my body.$d$, $d$Free me from envy and anxiety, Lord. Give me a sound heart.$d$, $d$Unfollow one account that stirs comparison in you.$d$, $d$Where is envy or anxiety affecting your peace?$d$),
('women', 136, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Rest Day: Sleep Sweet$d$, $d$Proverbs 3:24$d$, $d$When thou liest down, thou shalt not be afraid: yea, thou shalt lie down, and thy sleep shall be sweet.$d$, $d$Sleep is one of God’s healing gifts. Your body repairs, your mind resets, and your strength returns while you rest. Fear and worry steal sleep, but He promises sweet sleep. Lay your worries down before you lie down.$d$, $d$When I lie down I am not afraid, and my sleep is sweet.$d$, $d$Give me sweet, healing sleep tonight, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Create a calming bedtime routine with no screens for 30 minutes.$d$, $d$What worries keep you awake, and can you give them to God tonight?$d$),
('women', 137, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Temple of the Spirit$d$, $d$1 Corinthians 6:19-20$d$, $d$What? know ye not that your body is the temple of the Holy Ghost which is in you, which ye have of God, and ye are not your own? For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body.$d$, $d$Your body is a temple: a dwelling place for God’s Spirit. That makes it holy, not a project to fix. Caring for it is worship. Eat, rest, and move as someone honoring a sacred place.$d$, $d$My body is a temple of the Holy Spirit, and I glorify God in my body.$d$, $d$Holy Spirit, help me care for Your temple with love.$d$, $d$Make one choice today to honor your body as His temple.$d$, $d$How would you treat your body differently if you saw it as His temple?$d$),
('women', 138, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Healing Light$d$, $d$Malachi 4:2$d$, $d$But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings.$d$, $d$The Sun of Righteousness rises with healing in His wings. Like morning light pushing back darkness, Jesus brings healing as He rises over your life. Look to Him like you’d look for the sunrise.$d$, $d$The Sun of Righteousness rises over me with healing in His wings.$d$, $d$Rise over my life today, Jesus, with healing.$d$, $d$Watch a sunrise this week if you can, and pray Malachi 4:2.$d$, $d$Where do you need His healing light to rise?$d$),
('women', 139, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Strength Restored$d$, $d$Isaiah 41:10$d$, $d$Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.$d$, $d$I will strengthen, I will help, I will uphold. Three promises in one verse. When illness, injury, or exhaustion leaves you weak, God holds you up with His righteous right hand. You won’t fall.$d$, $d$God strengthens me, helps me, and upholds me with His righteous right hand.$d$, $d$Hold me up today, Lord. I lean on You.$d$, $d$If you’re recovering, honor your limits today. Gentle movement is still faithful.$d$, $d$Where do you need God to hold you up right now?$d$),
('women', 140, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Wise Care$d$, $d$1 Timothy 4:8$d$, $d$For bodily exercise profiteth little: but godliness is profitable unto all things, having promise of the life that now is, and of that which is to come.$d$, $d$Paul says physical training has some value. It does! But godliness has value in every way, now and forever. Keep both in their place. Train your body faithfully, and train your soul even more.$d$, $d$I train my body with discipline and my soul with even greater devotion.$d$, $d$Keep my priorities in order, Lord. You first, always.$d$, $d$Pair your workout with a prayer or sermon today.$d$, $d$Has your physical training ever crowded out your spiritual life?$d$),
('women', 141, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Healing in Community$d$, $d$Galatians 6:2$d$, $d$Bear ye one another’s burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ.$d$, $d$Healing often happens in community. God designed us to carry each other’s burdens. Let your sisters help you, and help them in return. You don’t have to heal alone.$d$, $d$I bear others’ burdens, and I let others help carry mine.$d$, $d$Show me whose burden to help carry today, and give me humility to receive help.$d$, $d$Ask a friend to pray for you this week, and offer to pray for her too.$d$, $d$Who could you let in to help you carry something?$d$),
('women', 142, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Mercy for the Weary$d$, $d$Matthew 9:36$d$, $d$But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.$d$, $d$Jesus looks at weary, scattered people with compassion, not frustration. That’s how He sees you when you’re worn out. He is moved by your exhaustion. Let His compassion be the voice you hear today.$d$, $d$Jesus looks on me with compassion, and He shepherds my weary heart.$d$, $d$Thank You for Your compassion when I am weary, Jesus.$d$, $d$Swap an intense workout for a restorative one today.$d$, $d$How does knowing Jesus sees you with compassion change how you see yourself?$d$),
('women', 143, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Rest Day: Still Waters$d$, $d$Psalm 62:5$d$, $d$My soul, wait thou only upon God; for my expectation is from him.$d$, $d$Healing sometimes requires waiting. Your expectation is from Him. Not from the diet, the doctor, or the plan alone, but from God working through them. Wait on Him in hope today.$d$, $d$My soul waits only on God, and my expectation is from Him.$d$, $d$I put my expectation in You, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Spend ten minutes in quiet waiting prayer.$d$, $d$Where is your expectation placed right now?$d$),
('women', 144, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$He Sent His Word$d$, $d$Psalm 107:20$d$, $d$He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered them from their destructions.$d$, $d$God’s Word carries healing power. He sent His Word and healed them. When you speak His promises over your body, you are agreeing with what He has already said. Take His Word like medicine today: personal, spoken, and believed.$d$, $d$God sends His Word and heals me.$d$, $d$Speak Your Word over my body today, Lord.$d$, $d$Speak three healing scriptures out loud during your workout.$d$, $d$Which healing verse speaks to you most?$d$),
('women', 145, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Abundant Health$d$, $d$Jeremiah 30:17$d$, $d$For I will restore health unto thee, and I will heal thee of thy wounds, saith the LORD.$d$, $d$God promises to restore health and heal wounds. Restoration is His heart toward you. Whatever has been broken, whether in your body, your relationships, or your self-image, He is able to restore.$d$, $d$God restores health to me and heals my wounds.$d$, $d$Restore what is broken in me, Lord.$d$, $d$Go for a walk and thank God for every part of your body that works well.$d$, $d$What do you want God to restore this month?$d$),
('women', 146, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Healthy Habits as Worship$d$, $d$Proverbs 3:7-8$d$, $d$Be not wise in thine own eyes: fear the LORD, and depart from evil. It shall be health to thy navel, and marrow to thy bones.$d$, $d$Humility and reverence for God bring health even to your bones. Wisdom from God beats wisdom in your own eyes, including about food, rest, and exercise. Stay humble, keep learning, and walk in His ways.$d$, $d$Fearing the Lord brings health to my body and strength to my bones.$d$, $d$Keep me humble and teachable, Lord.$d$, $d$Learn one new fact about nutrition or recovery this week.$d$, $d$Where might you be wise in your own eyes about your health?$d$),
('women', 147, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Healed Emotions$d$, $d$Isaiah 61:3$d$, $d$To give unto them beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness.$d$, $d$Beauty for ashes. Joy for mourning. Praise for heaviness. God trades what’s broken for what’s beautiful. If heaviness has settled on you, put on the garment of praise today. Worship is a powerful exchange.$d$, $d$God gives me beauty for ashes and the garment of praise for heaviness.$d$, $d$I trade my heaviness for Your praise today, Lord.$d$, $d$Worship for 15 minutes before or during your workout.$d$, $d$What heaviness do you want to exchange for praise?$d$),
('women', 148, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Healing Takes Time$d$, $d$Ecclesiastes 3:1-3$d$, $d$To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven... a time to heal.$d$, $d$There is a time to heal. Healing isn’t always instant. Sometimes it’s a season. Be patient with your body and heart. Trust God’s timing as He restores you step by step.$d$, $d$There is a time to heal, and I trust God’s timing for my healing.$d$, $d$Give me patience in my healing season, Lord.$d$, $d$Celebrate small signs of healing or progress this week.$d$, $d$What healing are you patiently waiting for?$d$),
('women', 149, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Rest Day: Lie Down$d$, $d$Psalm 4:8$d$, $d$I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, LORD, only makest me dwell in safety.$d$, $d$Lie down in peace. Sleep. Rest is part of healing. God alone keeps you safe, so you don’t have to stay up guarding your life. Let Him hold the night.$d$, $d$I lie down in peace and sleep, for God keeps me safe.$d$, $d$I rest in Your safety tonight, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Take a nap or go to bed early tonight.$d$, $d$What would help you rest more deeply?$d$),
('women', 150, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Whole and Complete$d$, $d$Colossians 2:10$d$, $d$And ye are complete in him, which is the head of all principality and power.$d$, $d$You are complete in Him. Not after the weight loss, after healing, or after the next milestone. Complete now. Your health journey flows from wholeness in Christ, not a search for it.$d$, $d$I am complete in Christ.$d$, $d$Thank You that I am already complete in You, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a workout today celebrating what your body can do right now.$d$, $d$How does being complete in Christ change your goals?$d$),
('women', 151, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Praise the Healer$d$, $d$Jeremiah 17:14$d$, $d$Heal me, O LORD, and I shall be healed; save me, and I shall be saved: for thou art my praise.$d$, $d$Jeremiah prays for healing and ends in praise. You are my praise. Whether healing comes quickly or slowly, He remains worthy of praise. Let praise be the way you wait.$d$, $d$The Lord heals me and saves me, and He is my praise.$d$, $d$Heal me, Lord, and I will be healed. You are my praise.$d$, $d$End today’s workout with a song of praise.$d$, $d$How can praise be part of your healing journey?$d$),
('women', 152, $d$Healed and Whole$d$, $d$Walking in Wholeness$d$, $d$Psalm 30:2$d$, $d$O LORD my God, I cried unto thee, and thou hast healed me.$d$, $d$As this month of healing ends, remember the times you cried out and He answered. Healing is part of your testimony. Write it down. Share it. Your story can strengthen another woman’s faith.$d$, $d$I cried to the Lord, and He healed me.$d$, $d$Thank You for every healing in my story, Lord.$d$, $d$Share a testimony of healing with a friend or in the community.$d$, $d$What healing testimony could encourage someone else?$d$),
('women', 153, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Power for the Faint$d$, $d$Isaiah 40:29$d$, $d$He giveth power to the faint; and to them that have no might he increaseth strength.$d$, $d$God gives power specifically to the faint. Not to the already-strong, but to those who feel they have nothing left. If you start this month tired, you are exactly who this promise is for. Bring your weakness, and let Him increase your strength.$d$, $d$God gives power to me when I am faint, and increases my strength when I am weak.$d$, $d$Lord, I come to You tired. Increase my strength.$d$, $d$Do a short, doable workout today. Showing up is the win.$d$, $d$Where do you feel faint right now?$d$),
('women', 154, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Even the Young Grow Tired$d$, $d$Isaiah 40:30$d$, $d$Even the youths shall faint and be weary, and the young men shall utterly fall.$d$, $d$Isaiah admits what we all know: even the strongest people get tired. Youth, energy, and talent run out. Natural strength has limits. That’s not failure. It’s design. It makes room for a strength that doesn’t run out.$d$, $d$My strength is not limited to my natural ability; I draw on God’s strength.$d$, $d$When my natural strength runs out, be my strength, Lord.$d$, $d$Notice when you get tired today and pause to pray instead of pushing past it.$d$, $d$Where have you been relying only on natural strength?$d$),
('women', 155, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Wait and Renew$d$, $d$Isaiah 40:31$d$, $d$But they that wait upon the LORD shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint.$d$, $d$Waiting on the Lord renews strength. Not waiting passively, but hoping in Him, expecting Him, looking for Him. It’s like an exchange: your weariness for His renewal. Eagles don’t flap harder in storms; they ride the wind. Learn to rise on His strength.$d$, $d$I wait on the Lord, and He renews my strength. I rise up like an eagle.$d$, $d$I wait on You, Lord. Exchange my weakness for Your strength.$d$, $d$Memorize Isaiah 40:31 this week while you walk.$d$, $d$What does waiting on the Lord look like in your daily life?$d$),
('women', 156, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Wings Like Eagles$d$, $d$Exodus 19:4$d$, $d$Ye have seen what I did unto the Egyptians, and how I bare you on eagles’ wings, and brought you unto myself.$d$, $d$God carried Israel out of slavery on eagles’ wings, and the destination was Himself. Every rescue He brings you through has the same goal: bringing you closer to Him. Your strength journey isn’t only about getting stronger. It’s about getting nearer.$d$, $d$God carries me on eagles’ wings and brings me to Himself.$d$, $d$Carry me closer to You, Lord.$d$, $d$Stretch your arms wide like wings and take five deep breaths of gratitude.$d$, $d$How has God carried you through a hard season?$d$),
('women', 157, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Run and Not Be Weary$d$, $d$Isaiah 40:31$d$, $d$They shall run, and not be weary.$d$, $d$Some seasons feel like running: busy, demanding, fast-paced. God promises strength for those seasons too. You can run without burning out when your strength comes from waiting on Him first. Start with Him before you start running.$d$, $d$I run and am not weary, because my strength comes from the Lord.$d$, $d$Strengthen me for this busy season, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a run-walk interval workout today.$d$, $d$Which of your current seasons feels like running?$d$),
('women', 158, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Walk and Not Faint$d$, $d$Isaiah 40:31$d$, $d$They shall walk, and not faint.$d$, $d$Most of life isn’t flying or running. It’s walking: ordinary, steady, faithful steps. God gives strength for the long walk too: the daily routines, the endless laundry, the slow progress. Keep walking. You will not faint.$d$, $d$I walk faithfully, and I do not faint.$d$, $d$Give me strength for the ordinary walk of faithfulness, Lord.$d$, $d$Take a long, steady walk today: 30 minutes or more.$d$, $d$Where do you need strength for the long walk?$d$),
('women', 159, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Rest Day: Strength in Quiet$d$, $d$Isaiah 30:15$d$, $d$In quietness and in confidence shall be your strength.$d$, $d$Strength isn’t only built in the gym. It’s built in quietness and confidence. Rest days aren’t lost days. They’re where muscles repair and souls are restored. Trust the strength being built in stillness today.$d$, $d$My strength is found in quietness and confidence in God.$d$, $d$Build my strength in the quiet today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Stay off screens for an hour and enjoy quiet.$d$, $d$How does quietness build strength in you?$d$),
('women', 160, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$My Strength and Song$d$, $d$Exodus 15:2$d$, $d$The LORD is my strength and song, and he is become my salvation.$d$, $d$God is both strength and song: the power to keep going and the joy that makes the journey beautiful. You can sing while you work. Worship isn’t a break from strength-building. It is part of it.$d$, $d$The Lord is my strength and my song.$d$, $d$Be my strength and my song today, Lord.$d$, $d$Make a worship playlist for your workouts.$d$, $d$What song strengthens you most?$d$),
('women', 161, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Girded with Strength$d$, $d$Psalm 18:32$d$, $d$It is God that girdeth me with strength, and maketh my way perfect.$d$, $d$A girdle wraps around your core and holds you steady, like a lifting belt. God girds you with strength. He stabilizes you from the inside out and makes your way steady. Lean into His support today.$d$, $d$God girds me with strength and makes my way perfect.$d$, $d$Wrap me in Your strength today, Lord.$d$, $d$Focus on core strength today: planks, dead bugs, or bird dogs.$d$, $d$Where do you need God to steady you?$d$),
('women', 162, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Feet Like a Deer$d$, $d$Psalm 18:33$d$, $d$He maketh my feet like hinds’ feet, and setteth me upon my high places.$d$, $d$Deer are sure-footed on steep, rocky places. God gives you that kind of footing: stable on hard terrain, confident where others slip. The high places in your life aren’t meant to scare you. He equips you to stand there.$d$, $d$God makes my feet like a deer’s and sets me on high places.$d$, $d$Make my steps sure today, Lord, even on rocky ground.$d$, $d$Do balance work today: single-leg stands or lunges.$d$, $d$What high place is God calling you to stand on?$d$),
('women', 163, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Trained for Battle$d$, $d$Psalm 18:34$d$, $d$He teacheth my hands to war, so that a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.$d$, $d$God trains your hands for the battles you face: spiritual, emotional, practical. Training takes repetition. Every prayer, every hard conversation handled with grace, every faithful choice is training. He is making you strong for what’s ahead.$d$, $d$God trains my hands for battle and strengthens my arms.$d$, $d$Train me for the battles ahead, Lord.$d$, $d$Do an upper-body workout today and pray for strength for your battles.$d$, $d$What battle is God training you for right now?$d$),
('women', 164, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Strength for Today$d$, $d$Deuteronomy 33:25$d$, $d$As thy days, so shall thy strength be.$d$, $d$Your strength will match your days. God doesn’t give you tomorrow’s strength today. He gives today’s strength for today. If you’re dreading what’s ahead, remember: when you get there, the strength will be there too.$d$, $d$As my days are, so is my strength.$d$, $d$Give me today’s strength for today, Lord.$d$, $d$Focus only on today’s workout, not the whole week.$d$, $d$What future day are you worried you won’t have strength for?$d$),
('women', 165, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$I Can Do All Things$d$, $d$Philippians 4:13$d$, $d$I can do all things through Christ which strengtheneth me.$d$, $d$Paul wrote this about contentment in plenty and in want. It isn’t a promise that you can do anything you want. It’s a promise that you can face anything that comes, through Christ. His strength carries you through hunger, abundance, loss, and gain.$d$, $d$I can do all things through Christ who strengthens me.$d$, $d$Strengthen me for whatever today brings, Jesus.$d$, $d$Attempt one more rep than last time on your strongest exercise.$d$, $d$What are you facing that needs Christ’s strength?$d$),
('women', 166, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Rest Day: Refreshed$d$, $d$Jeremiah 31:25$d$, $d$For I have satiated the weary soul, and I have replenished every sorrowful soul.$d$, $d$God refreshes the weary and replenishes the sorrowful. He satisfies what is depleted. On this rest day, let Him refill you. You can’t pour from an empty cup.$d$, $d$God refreshes my weary soul and replenishes me.$d$, $d$Refill me today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Do something that truly refreshes you.$d$, $d$What refreshes you most deeply?$d$),
('women', 167, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Strong and Courageous$d$, $d$Deuteronomy 31:6$d$, $d$Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for the LORD thy God, he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.$d$, $d$Strength and courage come from one truth: God goes with you. He will not fail you. He will not forsake you. You don’t need to feel brave. You only need to remember who walks beside you.$d$, $d$I am strong and courageous, for God goes with me and will never forsake me.$d$, $d$Go with me today, Lord. I won’t be afraid.$d$, $d$Walk into the gym with your head high today.$d$, $d$Where do you need courage this week?$d$),
('women', 168, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Strength of My Heart$d$, $d$Psalm 73:26$d$, $d$My flesh and my heart faileth: but God is the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.$d$, $d$Your flesh will fail at some point. Your heart may fail too. But God remains the strength of your heart. When your body hurts or your heart breaks, He is still your portion: enough, always.$d$, $d$God is the strength of my heart and my portion forever.$d$, $d$When my body and heart are weak, be my strength, Lord.$d$, $d$Do gentle movement today if your body is sore.$d$, $d$Where are you feeling weak, and how is God your portion there?$d$),
('women', 169, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Mighty in Battle$d$, $d$Psalm 24:8$d$, $d$Who is this King of glory? The LORD strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in battle.$d$, $d$The King of glory is strong and mighty in battle. You don’t fight alone. When you face addiction, anxiety, temptation, or hard seasons, the Lord mighty in battle fights for you and with you.$d$, $d$The Lord, strong and mighty, fights my battles.$d$, $d$Fight for me today, mighty King.$d$, $d$Do a powerful workout today and dedicate it to the King of glory.$d$, $d$What battle do you need to let God fight?$d$),
('women', 170, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Rock and Fortress$d$, $d$Psalm 18:2$d$, $d$The LORD is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust.$d$, $d$A rock doesn’t move. A fortress protects. A deliverer rescues. God is all three. Strength begins with trust. Who you trust shapes how strong you stand.$d$, $d$The Lord is my rock, my fortress, and my deliverer. I trust in Him.$d$, $d$You are my rock, Lord. I build my life on You.$d$, $d$Do a grounded strength exercise like deadlifts or glute bridges.$d$, $d$Who or what have you been trusting besides God?$d$),
('women', 171, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Strength in Weakness$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 12:10$d$, $d$Therefore I take pleasure in infirmities... for when I am weak, then am I strong.$d$, $d$Paul discovered something surprising: weakness opened the door for God’s strength. When you admit your limits, Christ’s power rests on you. You don’t have to pretend to be strong. Your weakness can become a testimony of His strength.$d$, $d$When I am weak, then I am strong in Christ.$d$, $d$Let Your strength rest on my weakness, Lord.$d$, $d$Admit one limit today and ask for help instead of pushing through alone.$d$, $d$Where could weakness become a doorway for God’s strength?$d$),
('women', 172, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Fresh Oil$d$, $d$Psalm 92:10$d$, $d$But my horn shalt thou exalt like the horn of an unicorn: I shall be anointed with fresh oil.$d$, $d$Fresh oil means renewal: new anointing for a new season. Yesterday’s strength isn’t meant to last forever. God gives fresh grace, fresh energy, and fresh purpose. Ask for fresh oil today.$d$, $d$I am anointed with fresh oil for this season.$d$, $d$Pour out fresh oil on me today, Lord.$d$, $d$Try a new workout style this week to refresh your routine.$d$, $d$Where do you need a fresh anointing?$d$),
('women', 173, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Rest Day: Renewed Mind$d$, $d$Ephesians 4:23$d$, $d$And be renewed in the spirit of your mind.$d$, $d$Strength starts in the mind. When your thoughts are renewed, your energy follows. On this rest day, let God renew how you think about yourself, your progress, and your future.$d$, $d$I am renewed in the spirit of my mind.$d$, $d$Renew my thoughts today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Write down three lies you’ve believed and replace them with truth.$d$, $d$Which thought needs renewing most?$d$),
('women', 174, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Endurance$d$, $d$Hebrews 10:36$d$, $d$For ye have need of patience, that, after ye have done the will of God, ye might receive the promise.$d$, $d$Endurance is what carries you from doing God’s will to receiving His promise. The gap between them requires patience. Stay faithful in the waiting. The promise is on the other side of endurance.$d$, $d$I endure with patience, and I receive the promise.$d$, $d$Build endurance in me, Lord, in body and in faith.$d$, $d$Do a longer, steady cardio session today.$d$, $d$What promise are you enduring toward?$d$),
('women', 175, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Joy in the Climb$d$, $d$Habakkuk 3:19$d$, $d$The LORD God is my strength, and he will make my feet like hinds’ feet, and he will make me to walk upon mine high places.$d$, $d$Habakkuk wrote this in a season with no fruit on the vine and no cattle in the stalls. Yet he chose joy. God was still his strength. The high places aren’t only for good seasons. He makes you climb in hard ones too.$d$, $d$The Lord God is my strength, and He makes me walk on high places.$d$, $d$Even when things look empty, You are my strength, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a hill or incline walk today.$d$, $d$How can you choose joy in a lean season?$d$),
('women', 176, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Strengthen the Weak Hands$d$, $d$Isaiah 35:3$d$, $d$Strengthen ye the weak hands, and confirm the feeble knees.$d$, $d$God calls the strong to strengthen the weak. As you grow stronger, use it to lift others. Encourage the beginner. Pray for the struggling. Strength is given to be shared.$d$, $d$I use my strength to strengthen others.$d$, $d$Show me who needs strengthening today, Lord.$d$, $d$Encourage a newer member of the community or invite a friend to work out.$d$, $d$Who could you strengthen this week?$d$),
('women', 177, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Steadfast$d$, $d$1 Corinthians 15:58$d$, $d$Therefore, my beloved brethren, be ye stedfast, unmoveable, always abounding in the work of the Lord, forasmuch as ye know that your labour is not in vain in the Lord.$d$, $d$Your labor isn’t wasted. Not the workouts, not the prayers, not the quiet faithfulness nobody sees. In the Lord, nothing is in vain. Stay steadfast and immovable.$d$, $d$I am steadfast and immovable, and my labor is not in vain.$d$, $d$Keep me steady, Lord. Remind me my labor isn’t wasted.$d$, $d$Repeat a workout from the beginning of this month and compare.$d$, $d$What labor feels in vain that you can trust to God?$d$),
('women', 178, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Strength from Above$d$, $d$Psalm 121:1-2$d$, $d$I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help. My help cometh from the LORD, which made heaven and earth.$d$, $d$When you lift your eyes, remember where help comes from: the Lord, maker of heaven and earth. Not the mountain, not your plan, not your strength. Look up today.$d$, $d$My help comes from the Lord, maker of heaven and earth.$d$, $d$I lift my eyes to You, Lord. You are my help.$d$, $d$Take a walk somewhere with a view and pray Psalm 121.$d$, $d$Where do you usually look for help first?$d$),
('women', 179, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Rest Day: Strong in Rest$d$, $d$Mark 6:31$d$, $d$And he said unto them, Come ye yourselves apart into a desert place, and rest a while.$d$, $d$Jesus told His busy disciples to come away and rest. Even ministry needed a pause. If Jesus prioritized rest for His followers, you can too. Come away with Him today.$d$, $d$I come away with Jesus and rest awhile.$d$, $d$Jesus, I come away with You today.$d$, $d$Rest day. Spend an hour alone with God, outside if possible.$d$, $d$Where can you come away and rest this week?$d$),
('women', 180, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Stronger Each Day$d$, $d$Proverbs 4:18$d$, $d$But the path of the just is as the shining light, that shineth more and more unto the perfect day.$d$, $d$Your path grows brighter step by step, like dawn becoming full day. Growth is gradual: in strength, in faith, in character. You may not notice daily changes, but the light is increasing.$d$, $d$My path shines brighter and brighter.$d$, $d$Let my life grow brighter each day, Lord.$d$, $d$Track one fitness metric today to see your progress over time.$d$, $d$How has your path grown brighter this year?$d$),
('women', 181, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Power Within$d$, $d$Acts 1:8$d$, $d$But ye shall receive power, after that the Holy Ghost is come upon you.$d$, $d$The Holy Spirit gives power: courage to speak, strength to stand, boldness to live for Jesus. That power isn’t reserved for apostles. It’s for every woman who believes. Walk in it today.$d$, $d$I have received power through the Holy Spirit.$d$, $d$Holy Spirit, fill me with Your power today.$d$, $d$Do a high-energy workout and pray for the Spirit’s power.$d$, $d$Where do you need the Holy Spirit’s power?$d$),
('women', 182, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Unwearied God$d$, $d$Isaiah 40:28$d$, $d$Hast thou not known? hast thou not heard, that the everlasting God, the LORD, the Creator of the ends of the earth, fainteth not, neither is weary?$d$, $d$God never gets tired. He doesn’t faint or grow weary. The One who gives you strength has an endless supply. When you’re worn out, He isn’t. Lean on the unwearied God.$d$, $d$My God never faints or grows weary, and He strengthens me.$d$, $d$Thank You that You never grow tired of helping me.$d$, $d$Do a gentle recovery session and thank God for His endless strength.$d$, $d$How does God’s endless strength encourage you?$d$),
('women', 183, $d$Renewed Strength$d$, $d$Strength Renewed$d$, $d$Psalm 138:3$d$, $d$In the day when I cried thou answeredst me, and strengthenedst me with strength in my soul.$d$, $d$When David cried out, God answered with strength in his soul. As this month ends, look back at the times you cried out and found strength. He renewed you again and again. He will keep doing it.$d$, $d$When I cry out, God answers me and strengthens my soul.$d$, $d$Thank You for answering me and renewing my strength, Lord.$d$, $d$Celebrate your strength progress this month with your favorite workout.$d$, $d$How has God renewed your strength this month?$d$),
('women', 184, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Dwelling Place$d$, $d$Psalm 91:1$d$, $d$He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty.$d$, $d$Protection begins with dwelling: not visiting God occasionally, but living in His presence. The secret place is where you meet Him daily. When you dwell there, you abide under His shadow, close enough to be covered.$d$, $d$I dwell in the secret place of the Most High and abide under His shadow.$d$, $d$Lord, make my life a dwelling place in Your presence.$d$, $d$Set up a daily prayer spot, your secret place, for this month.$d$, $d$Where is your secret place with God?$d$),
('women', 185, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$My Refuge$d$, $d$Psalm 91:2$d$, $d$I will say of the LORD, He is my refuge and my fortress: my God; in him will I trust.$d$, $d$Notice the psalmist says it out loud: I will say. Declaring who God is strengthens your faith. Say it today: He is my refuge. He is my fortress. In Him I trust. Words of faith build walls of peace.$d$, $d$The Lord is my refuge and my fortress; my God, in Him I trust.$d$, $d$You are my refuge, Lord. I trust You.$d$, $d$Speak Psalm 91:2 aloud before your workout.$d$, $d$What does it mean to you that God is your refuge?$d$),
('women', 186, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Delivered$d$, $d$Psalm 91:3$d$, $d$Surely he shall deliver thee from the snare of the fowler, and from the noisome pestilence.$d$, $d$A snare is hidden. You don’t see it until it springs. God delivers you from traps you never even noticed. Some of His greatest protection happens without your knowledge. Thank Him today for rescues you’ll never see.$d$, $d$God delivers me from every snare and from every plague.$d$, $d$Thank You for protecting me from dangers I never saw.$d$, $d$Take a walk and thank God for unseen protection.$d$, $d$When has God protected you from something you didn’t see coming?$d$),
('women', 187, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Under His Feathers$d$, $d$Psalm 91:4$d$, $d$He shall cover thee with his feathers, and under his wings shalt thou trust: his truth shall be thy shield and buckler.$d$, $d$God describes Himself like a mother bird covering her chicks. Tender and fierce at once. His truth is your shield. When lies and fear come at you, His truth stands in front of you.$d$, $d$God covers me with His feathers, and His truth is my shield.$d$, $d$Cover me today, Lord, and let Your truth shield my mind.$d$, $d$Write down one lie you’ve believed and the truth that shields you from it.$d$, $d$Which truth do you need as your shield today?$d$),
('women', 188, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Not Afraid of the Night$d$, $d$Psalm 91:5$d$, $d$Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night; nor for the arrow that flieth by day.$d$, $d$Night fears and day arrows: anxiety at 2 a.m. and attacks in broad daylight. God covers both. You don’t have to live braced for what might happen. You are covered day and night.$d$, $d$I am not afraid of terror by night or arrows by day.$d$, $d$Guard my nights and my days, Lord.$d$, $d$Pray Psalm 91 before bed tonight.$d$, $d$What fear tends to visit you at night?$d$),
('women', 189, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$It Shall Not Come Near$d$, $d$Psalm 91:7$d$, $d$A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand; but it shall not come nigh thee.$d$, $d$This is one of the boldest promises in Scripture. In the middle of danger, God keeps His people. Hold onto it with faith, even when you don’t understand everything that happens. God’s heart toward you is protection.$d$, $d$Danger shall not come near me, for I am covered by God.$d$, $d$Lord, I trust You to protect me and those I love.$d$, $d$Pray protection over your home, room by room.$d$, $d$Who do you want to pray protection over today?$d$),
('women', 190, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Rest Day: Safe Dwelling$d$, $d$Psalm 91:9-10$d$, $d$Because thou hast made the LORD, which is my refuge, even the most High, thy habitation; There shall no evil befall thee, neither shall any plague come nigh thy dwelling.$d$, $d$Your home can be a place of safety because God is your habitation. Rest today in a covered house. You don’t have to guard everything. He does.$d$, $d$Because I have made the Lord my refuge, no evil shall befall me, nor any plague come near my house.$d$, $d$Cover my home today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Light a candle and pray over your home.$d$, $d$What helps your home feel like a place of peace?$d$),
('women', 191, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Angels Assigned$d$, $d$Psalm 91:11$d$, $d$For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.$d$, $d$God gives His angels charge over you, to keep you in all your ways. On the drive, at the gym, in the hospital, at home. You are never unaccompanied. Heaven is involved in your protection.$d$, $d$God gives His angels charge over me to keep me in all my ways.$d$, $d$Thank You for angels watching over me and my family.$d$, $d$Drive or walk today with a prayer of protection.$d$, $d$How does knowing angels watch over you change your fear?$d$),
('women', 192, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Because I Love Him$d$, $d$Psalm 91:14$d$, $d$Because he hath set his love upon me, therefore will I deliver him: I will set him on high, because he hath known my name.$d$, $d$God speaks directly here: because you have set your love on Me, I will deliver you. Love and knowing His name come first. Protection flows from relationship, not ritual. Set your love on Him today.$d$, $d$Because I have set my love on the Lord, He delivers me and sets me on high.$d$, $d$I set my love on You today, Lord.$d$, $d$Spend your workout thinking about how much you love God.$d$, $d$What does setting your love on God look like?$d$),
('women', 193, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$He Answers$d$, $d$Psalm 91:15$d$, $d$He shall call upon me, and I will answer him: I will be with him in trouble; I will deliver him, and honour him.$d$, $d$Call, and He answers. Trouble, and He is with you. Deliverance, and He honors you. God doesn’t promise a life without trouble. He promises His presence in it. You are never alone in a hard moment.$d$, $d$I call on the Lord, and He answers me. He is with me in trouble.$d$, $d$I’m calling on You today, Lord. Be with me.$d$, $d$Do a workout today and pray through one trouble you’re facing.$d$, $d$What trouble do you need His presence in?$d$),
('women', 194, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Long Life$d$, $d$Psalm 91:16$d$, $d$With long life will I satisfy him, and shew him my salvation.$d$, $d$God promises satisfaction in life, not just length of days but fullness. He wants you to see His salvation in your story. Taking care of your body is part of stewarding the days He gives.$d$, $d$With long life God satisfies me and shows me His salvation.$d$, $d$Satisfy me with long, full life, Lord.$d$, $d$Do one thing for your long-term health today.$d$, $d$What do you want your later years to look like?$d$),
('women', 195, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Whom Shall I Fear?$d$, $d$Psalm 27:1$d$, $d$The LORD is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the LORD is the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?$d$, $d$Two questions with one answer: no one. When the Lord is your light, salvation, and strength, fear loses its grip. Ask these questions out loud when fear rises. Let the answer settle you.$d$, $d$The Lord is my light and my salvation; I will not fear.$d$, $d$You are my light, my salvation, and my strength, Lord.$d$, $d$Speak Psalm 27:1 during each set of today’s workout.$d$, $d$Who or what are you afraid of right now?$d$),
('women', 196, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Hidden in His Pavilion$d$, $d$Psalm 27:5$d$, $d$For in the time of trouble he shall hide me in his pavilion: in the secret of his tabernacle shall he hide me; he shall set me up upon a rock.$d$, $d$In trouble, God hides you, not to keep you from life but to keep you safe in it. Then He sets you on a rock: higher ground, steady footing. Let Him hide you today and lift you tomorrow.$d$, $d$In trouble, God hides me in His pavilion and sets me upon a rock.$d$, $d$Hide me in You today, Lord, and set me on solid ground.$d$, $d$Do grounded exercises today like squats and lunges, focused on stability.$d$, $d$Where do you need God to hide you or lift you?$d$),
('women', 197, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Rest Day: Kept$d$, $d$Psalm 121:7-8$d$, $d$The LORD shall preserve thee from all evil: he shall preserve thy soul. The LORD shall preserve thy going out and thy coming in from this time forth, and even for evermore.$d$, $d$Your going out and coming in are kept. The school run, the commute, the gym, the grocery store. God watches over all of it, forever. Rest today knowing you are kept.$d$, $d$The Lord preserves me and my family from all evil, and keeps our going out and coming in.$d$, $d$Keep my family today, Lord, in every going out and coming in.$d$, $d$Rest day. Pray for each family member’s day.$d$, $d$Who in your family needs prayer for protection this week?$d$),
('women', 198, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$He Never Sleeps$d$, $d$Psalm 121:3-4$d$, $d$He will not suffer thy foot to be moved: he that keepeth thee will not slumber. Behold, he that keepeth Israel shall neither slumber nor sleep.$d$, $d$You need sleep. God doesn’t. He keeps watch so you can rest. Your foot won’t slip because He holds you steady. Let Him take the night shift tonight.$d$, $d$The One who keeps me never slumbers nor sleeps.$d$, $d$Thank You for watching over me while I sleep.$d$, $d$Do balance exercises today and thank God for steadying your steps.$d$, $d$What would you stop worrying about if you trusted God to keep watch?$d$),
('women', 199, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$The Lord Is Your Shade$d$, $d$Psalm 121:5-6$d$, $d$The LORD is thy keeper: the LORD is thy shade upon thy right hand. The sun shall not smite thee by day, nor the moon by night.$d$, $d$Shade is relief from heat. God is your shade: relief from pressure, protection from what would burn you out. Find shade in Him today when life feels too hot.$d$, $d$The Lord is my keeper and my shade.$d$, $d$Be my shade today, Lord, when everything feels too hot.$d$, $d$Work out in the morning or evening to avoid the heat, and pray for His shade.$d$, $d$What pressure do you need relief from?$d$),
('women', 200, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Peace in Your Home$d$, $d$Isaiah 32:17$d$, $d$And the work of righteousness shall be peace; and the effect of righteousness quietness and assurance for ever.$d$, $d$Righteousness produces peace, quietness, and confidence. When God’s ways are honored in your home, peace grows. You can be a woman who brings peace into every room.$d$, $d$My family is kept in perfect peace.$d$, $d$Make me a carrier of peace in my home.$d$, $d$Plan a family walk this week.$d$, $d$How can you bring more peace into your home?$d$),
('women', 201, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$The Name of the Lord$d$, $d$Proverbs 18:10$d$, $d$The name of the LORD is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.$d$, $d$When danger comes, run to His name. Jesus. It’s a strong tower, a place of safety. You don’t need the perfect prayer. You only need to call His name.$d$, $d$The name of the Lord is my strong tower; I run into it and I am safe.$d$, $d$Jesus, I run to You.$d$, $d$Do sprint intervals today and pray “Jesus” with each sprint.$d$, $d$When have you run to the name of the Lord?$d$),
('women', 202, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Covered by the Blood$d$, $d$Revelation 12:11$d$, $d$And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony.$d$, $d$You overcome by the blood of Jesus and the word of your testimony. His sacrifice covers you, and your story declares it. Speak what He has done. Every testimony is a victory over the enemy.$d$, $d$I am covered by the blood of Jesus, and I overcome by the word of my testimony.$d$, $d$Thank You for the blood that covers me, Jesus.$d$, $d$Share a testimony with someone this week.$d$, $d$What part of your testimony could encourage someone today?$d$),
('women', 203, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$He Fights for You$d$, $d$Exodus 14:14$d$, $d$The LORD shall fight for you, and ye shall hold your peace.$d$, $d$Sometimes your part is to stand still. The Lord fights for you. Not every battle requires your effort. Some require your trust. Hold your peace and let Him fight.$d$, $d$The Lord fights for me, and I hold my peace.$d$, $d$I let You fight this battle, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a calm, controlled workout today, focusing on breath.$d$, $d$Which battle do you need to stop fighting and give to God?$d$),
('women', 204, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Rest Day: Safe Arms$d$, $d$Deuteronomy 33:27$d$, $d$The eternal God is thy refuge, and underneath are the everlasting arms.$d$, $d$Underneath you are the everlasting arms. When you fall, you fall into Him. On this rest day, let yourself be held.$d$, $d$Underneath me are God’s everlasting arms.$d$, $d$Hold me today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Do a gentle restorative stretch session.$d$, $d$What would it feel like to be fully held by God?$d$),
('women', 205, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$No Weapon Prospers$d$, $d$Isaiah 54:17$d$, $d$No weapon that is formed against thee shall prosper; and every tongue that shall rise against thee in judgment thou shalt condemn.$d$, $d$Weapons may form, but they won’t prosper. Words spoken against you won’t stand. You are a servant of the Lord, and this is your heritage. Walk confidently today.$d$, $d$No weapon formed against me shall prosper.$d$, $d$Thank You that no weapon against me will succeed, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a strong, confident workout today.$d$, $d$What weapon has been formed against you that you’re trusting God with?$d$),
('women', 206, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Strength and Peace$d$, $d$Psalm 29:11$d$, $d$The LORD will give strength unto his people; the LORD will bless his people with peace.$d$, $d$Strength and peace come as a pair from the same hand. God doesn’t make you choose between being strong and being at rest. He gives both to His people. Receive His strength for today’s work and His peace for tonight’s rest.$d$, $d$The Lord gives me strength and blesses me with peace.$d$, $d$Give me Your strength and Your peace today, Lord.$d$, $d$Pair a strong workout with a peaceful evening wind-down.$d$, $d$Do you tend to have more strength or more peace right now?$d$),
('women', 207, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$He Goes Before$d$, $d$Deuteronomy 31:8$d$, $d$And the LORD, he it is that doth go before thee; he will be with thee, he will not fail thee, neither forsake thee: fear not, neither be dismayed.$d$, $d$God goes before you into tomorrow’s meeting, next week’s appointment, next year’s season. He is already there. You walk into places He has already prepared.$d$, $d$The Lord goes before me, and He will never fail me.$d$, $d$Go before me into every situation, Lord.$d$, $d$Pray over your calendar for the week.$d$, $d$What upcoming event do you need God to go before you into?$d$),
('women', 208, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Hedge of Protection$d$, $d$Job 1:10$d$, $d$Hast not thou made an hedge about him, and about his house, and about all that he hath on every side?$d$, $d$Even Satan acknowledged God’s hedge around Job: around him, his house, and all he had. Pray for that hedge around your family. God’s protection surrounds every side.$d$, $d$God places a hedge of protection around me, my family, and all I have.$d$, $d$Surround my family with Your hedge of protection, Lord.$d$, $d$Walk around your block and pray protection over your home.$d$, $d$Who needs a hedge of protection prayed over them?$d$),
('women', 209, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Fear Not$d$, $d$Isaiah 43:1-2$d$, $d$Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine. When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee.$d$, $d$Through the waters, not around them. God doesn’t promise to keep you out of every flood, but He promises to be with you in it. You are His, called by name. The waters won’t overwhelm you.$d$, $d$I am redeemed and called by name. When I pass through the waters, God is with me.$d$, $d$Be with me in the waters, Lord.$d$, $d$Swim or do a water workout this week if you can.$d$, $d$What waters are you passing through right now?$d$),
('women', 210, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Rest Day: Shepherd’s Care$d$, $d$Isaiah 40:11$d$, $d$He shall feed his flock like a shepherd: he shall gather the lambs with his arm, and carry them in his bosom, and shall gently lead those that are with young.$d$, $d$God gently leads those with young. Mothers, caregivers, women carrying others: He leads you gently. He knows your load. Rest today in His tender care.$d$, $d$God gently leads me and carries me close to His heart.$d$, $d$Lead me gently today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Let someone else help with a task today.$d$, $d$Where do you need God’s gentleness right now?$d$),
('women', 211, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Courage in the Storm$d$, $d$Mark 4:39$d$, $d$And he arose, and rebuked the wind, and said unto the sea, Peace, be still. And the wind ceased, and there was a great calm.$d$, $d$One word from Jesus, and the storm stops. He’s in your boat. Even if He seems asleep, He is not unaware. Speak peace over your storm today in His name.$d$, $d$Jesus speaks peace over my storms, and there is great calm.$d$, $d$Speak peace to my storm, Jesus.$d$, $d$Do a calming yoga or stretch session today.$d$, $d$What storm do you need Jesus to calm?$d$),
('women', 212, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Kept in His Hand$d$, $d$John 10:28-29$d$, $d$And I give unto them eternal life; and they shall never perish, neither shall any man pluck them out of my hand.$d$, $d$No one can snatch you out of His hand. Not circumstances, not enemies, not your own failures. You are held in the safest place there is. As this month ends, rest secure in His grip.$d$, $d$No one can pluck me out of God’s hand.$d$, $d$Thank You for holding me securely, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a grip-strength exercise today and remember His grip on you.$d$, $d$How has God protected you this month?$d$),
('women', 213, $d$Under His Wings$d$, $d$Lift Up Your Head$d$, $d$Psalm 3:3$d$, $d$But thou, O LORD, art a shield for me; my glory, and the lifter up of mine head.$d$, $d$David wrote this while running from his own son. Surrounded, betrayed, and afraid, he still called God his shield and the lifter of his head. When shame or sorrow pulls your eyes down, God gently lifts your chin. You can walk with your head up because He is your shield.$d$, $d$The Lord is my shield, my glory, and the lifter of my head.$d$, $d$Lift my head today, Lord. Be my shield.$d$, $d$Work on posture today: shoulders back, chin level, chest open.$d$, $d$What has been pulling your head down lately?$d$),
('women', 214, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Not a Spirit of Fear$d$, $d$2 Timothy 1:7$d$, $d$For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind.$d$, $d$Fear may visit, but it didn’t come from God. What He gave you is power, love, and a sound mind. When fear speaks, you can recognize it as a voice that doesn’t belong to your Father. This month, learn to live from what He gave you.$d$, $d$God has not given me a spirit of fear, but of power, love, and a sound mind.$d$, $d$Lord, I reject fear and receive power, love, and a sound mind.$d$, $d$Speak 2 Timothy 1:7 aloud before your workout every day this week.$d$, $d$Where has fear been speaking loudest lately?$d$),
('women', 215, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$A Spirit of Power$d$, $d$2 Timothy 1:7$d$, $d$But of power.$d$, $d$Power isn’t pushiness. It’s God’s ability working through you: the strength to say no, the courage to begin, the boldness to pray. You were given power, not timidity. Step into it today in one small brave act.$d$, $d$I walk in the spirit of power God has given me.$d$, $d$Holy Spirit, empower me to do what I’ve been afraid to do.$d$, $d$Try a heavier weight on one exercise today, with good form.$d$, $d$What would you do this week if you weren’t afraid?$d$),
('women', 216, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$A Spirit of Love$d$, $d$2 Timothy 1:7$d$, $d$And of love.$d$, $d$Power without love becomes harsh. God gives both. The power He gives always flows through love, for others and for yourself. Being strong doesn’t mean being hard. The strongest women are often the most tender.$d$, $d$I walk in the spirit of love God has given me.$d$, $d$Let love guide every bit of strength I have today, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a kind act for someone today that requires effort.$d$, $d$Where do you need to combine strength with love?$d$),
('women', 217, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$A Sound Mind$d$, $d$2 Timothy 1:7$d$, $d$And of a sound mind.$d$, $d$A sound mind is calm, balanced, disciplined, and self-controlled. That’s God’s gift to you. Anxiety and chaos aren’t your inheritance. Ask Him to steady your thoughts today and bring order to the noise.$d$, $d$I have a calm, well-balanced, disciplined mind.$d$, $d$Give me a sound mind today, Lord. Steady my thoughts.$d$, $d$Take a slow walk focused on breathing and calming your thoughts.$d$, $d$What makes your mind feel most chaotic?$d$),
('women', 218, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Not Fleshly Weapons$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 10:3$d$, $d$For though we walk in the flesh, we do not war after the flesh.$d$, $d$You live in a body, but your deepest battles aren’t won by physical means. You can’t out-diet anxiety or out-exercise shame. Spiritual battles need spiritual weapons: prayer, the Word, worship, and truth.$d$, $d$Though I live in a body, I do not fight with fleshly weapons.$d$, $d$Teach me to fight my battles with Your weapons, Lord.$d$, $d$Pair today’s workout with prayer about one spiritual battle.$d$, $d$What battle have you been fighting with the wrong weapons?$d$),
('women', 219, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Mighty Weapons$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 10:4$d$, $d$(For the weapons of our warfare are not carnal, but mighty through God to the pulling down of strong holds;)$d$, $d$Your weapons are mighty through God, strong enough to pull down strongholds. A stronghold is a fortified lie: a belief you’ve built defenses around. God’s truth can tear it down, brick by brick.$d$, $d$My weapons are mighty through God to pull down strongholds.$d$, $d$Show me the strongholds in my mind, Lord, and pull them down.$d$, $d$Write one stronghold, a lie you believe, and a verse that destroys it.$d$, $d$What stronghold in your thinking needs to come down?$d$),
('women', 220, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Rest Day: Peaceful Mind$d$, $d$Psalm 131:2$d$, $d$Surely I have behaved and quieted myself, as a child that is weaned of his mother.$d$, $d$A quieted soul is like a child resting on her mother: content, not demanding. On this rest day, quiet your soul. You don’t need to solve everything today.$d$, $d$I have calmed and quieted my soul.$d$, $d$Quiet my soul today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Spend 15 minutes in silence.$d$, $d$What keeps your soul from feeling quiet?$d$),
('women', 221, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Captive Thoughts$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 10:5$d$, $d$Casting down imaginations, and every high thing that exalteth itself against the knowledge of God, and bringing into captivity every thought to the obedience of Christ.$d$, $d$You don’t have to believe every thought you think. Take it captive. Ask: is this true? Does it agree with what God says? If not, cast it down. This is daily spiritual training, and it gets easier with practice.$d$, $d$I take every thought captive to the obedience of Christ.$d$, $d$Help me catch and correct the lies in my thinking, Lord.$d$, $d$Today, catch three negative thoughts and replace them with Scripture.$d$, $d$What thought do you need to take captive today?$d$),
('women', 222, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Arguments Cast Down$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 10:5$d$, $d$Casting down imaginations, and every high thing that exalteth itself against the knowledge of God.$d$, $d$Some thoughts argue with God: You’ll never change. God can’t use you. You’re too far gone. Cast them down. They exalt themselves above His truth. Bring them low, and lift His Word higher.$d$, $d$I cast down every argument that sets itself against the knowledge of God.$d$, $d$I cast down every lie that argues with Your truth, Lord.$d$, $d$During today’s workout, answer negative self-talk with Scripture.$d$, $d$What argument against God’s truth replays in your mind?$d$),
('women', 223, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Guard Your Heart$d$, $d$Proverbs 4:23$d$, $d$Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life.$d$, $d$Everything flows from the heart: words, choices, relationships. That’s why guarding it matters. Be careful what you let in through your eyes and ears. Your heart is worth protecting.$d$, $d$I keep my heart with all diligence, for out of it flow the issues of life.$d$, $d$Help me guard my heart today, Lord.$d$, $d$Choose what you watch and listen to today with intention.$d$, $d$What have you been letting into your heart that needs a gatekeeper?$d$),
('women', 224, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Self-Control$d$, $d$Proverbs 25:28$d$, $d$He that hath no rule over his own spirit is like a city that is broken down, and without walls.$d$, $d$Self-control is a wall of protection. Without it, everything gets in. With it, you choose what enters. Discipline in food, words, and emotions isn’t bondage. It’s strength that keeps you safe.$d$, $d$I have rule over my own spirit, and my walls are strong.$d$, $d$Build walls of self-control in me, Lord.$d$, $d$Choose one area today to practice self-control on purpose.$d$, $d$Where do your walls need rebuilding?$d$),
('women', 225, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Glory to Glory$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 3:18$d$, $d$But we all, with open face beholding as in a glass the glory of the Lord, are changed into the same image from glory to glory, even as by the Spirit of the Lord.$d$, $d$You are being changed from glory to glory, not overnight but step by step, as you behold the Lord. Each time you choose His truth over a lie, you look a little more like Him. Keep beholding. The Spirit is doing the transforming.$d$, $d$I am being changed from glory to glory by the Spirit of the Lord.$d$, $d$Keep transforming me as I look at You, Lord.$d$, $d$Read a chapter of Scripture before checking your phone today.$d$, $d$How has your thinking changed since you started walking with God?$d$),
('women', 226, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Peace Instead of Panic$d$, $d$John 14:27$d$, $d$Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be afraid.$d$, $d$Jesus gives a different kind of peace: not dependent on circumstances. And He gives a command: don’t let your heart be troubled. You have a choice in what you allow to settle in your heart.$d$, $d$I have the peace of Jesus, and I do not let my heart be troubled.$d$, $d$I receive Your peace today, Jesus.$d$, $d$Do a calm, flowing stretch routine today.$d$, $d$What troubles your heart most right now?$d$),
('women', 227, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Rest Day: Sound Sleep$d$, $d$Psalm 127:2$d$, $d$It is vain for you to rise up early, to sit up late, to eat the bread of sorrows: for so he giveth his beloved sleep.$d$, $d$God gives His beloved sleep. Working harder and sleeping less isn’t always faithfulness. Sometimes it’s anxiety. Rest is part of a sound mind. Receive sleep as a gift tonight.$d$, $d$God gives me, His beloved, sweet sleep.$d$, $d$Give me deep, restful sleep tonight, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Put your phone away an hour before bed.$d$, $d$What keeps you from sleeping well?$d$),
('women', 228, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Courage Over Comparison$d$, $d$Galatians 6:4$d$, $d$But let every man prove his own work, and then shall he have rejoicing in himself alone, and not in another.$d$, $d$Comparison steals joy and confidence. God invites you to focus on your own race, your own growth, your own assignment. Rejoice in what God is doing in you, not in how you measure against someone else.$d$, $d$I focus on my own work and rejoice in what God is doing in me.$d$, $d$Free me from comparison, Lord.$d$, $d$Compare today’s workout only to your past self.$d$, $d$Who do you tend to compare yourself to?$d$),
('women', 229, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Bold as a Lion$d$, $d$Proverbs 28:1$d$, $d$The wicked flee when no man pursueth: but the righteous are bold as a lion.$d$, $d$Righteousness produces boldness. Not arrogance, but holy confidence. Because you’re right with God through Christ, you can stand bold as a lion. You don’t have to shrink back.$d$, $d$I am bold as a lion, made righteous in Christ.$d$, $d$Make me bold, Lord, with holy confidence.$d$, $d$Do a powerful, bold workout today: push, pull, and lift with confidence.$d$, $d$Where do you shrink back that God wants you to be bold?$d$),
('women', 230, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Fear vs. Faith$d$, $d$Mark 5:36$d$, $d$Be not afraid, only believe.$d$, $d$Jesus said these words to a father whose daughter had just died. Be not afraid. Only believe. Faith and fear both believe in something unseen. Choose to believe in what God says over what fear predicts.$d$, $d$I am not afraid; I only believe.$d$, $d$Lord, help me choose faith over fear today.$d$, $d$Pray for a situation you’re afraid of during your workout.$d$, $d$What is fear predicting that faith can answer?$d$),
('women', 231, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Mind on Things Above$d$, $d$Colossians 3:2$d$, $d$Set your affection on things above, not on things on the earth.$d$, $d$What you set your mind on shapes your mood, your choices, and your peace. Earthly things matter, but they aren’t ultimate. Set your mind on things above: His love, His promises, His kingdom.$d$, $d$I set my mind on things above.$d$, $d$Lift my thoughts to You today, Lord.$d$, $d$Look up at the sky during your walk and pray Colossians 3:2.$d$, $d$What earthly thing has had too much of your mind?$d$),
('women', 232, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Speak Life$d$, $d$Proverbs 18:21$d$, $d$Death and life are in the power of the tongue.$d$, $d$Your words carry power, including words about yourself. Speak life over your body, your family, your future. Death and life are in the power of the tongue. Choose life today.$d$, $d$I speak life over myself, my family, and my future.$d$, $d$Guard my tongue, Lord, and help me speak life.$d$, $d$Say three life-giving things to yourself in the mirror today.$d$, $d$What do you say about yourself most often?$d$),
('women', 233, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Rest Day: Calm Assurance$d$, $d$Psalm 62:1-2$d$, $d$Truly my soul waiteth upon God: from him cometh my salvation. He only is my rock and my salvation; he is my defence; I shall not be greatly moved.$d$, $d$My soul waits upon God. On this rest day, stop trying to defend yourself or prove anything. He is your rock and your defense. You will not be greatly moved.$d$, $d$My soul waits upon God, and I shall not be greatly moved.$d$, $d$Settle me in You today, Lord. You are my rock.$d$, $d$Rest day. Enjoy a slow, quiet morning.$d$, $d$What would it feel like to stop defending yourself today?$d$),
('women', 234, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Healthy Mind, Healthy Body$d$, $d$Proverbs 23:7$d$, $d$For as he thinketh in his heart, so is he.$d$, $d$What you think in your heart shapes who you become. If you think you’ll always fail, you’ll live defeated. If you believe God’s promises, you’ll live hopeful. Your thoughts become your path.$d$, $d$I think God’s thoughts, and I become who He says I am.$d$, $d$Shape my heart’s thinking, Lord.$d$, $d$Write down who God says you are, and read it before your workout.$d$, $d$What do you believe about yourself in your heart?$d$),
('women', 235, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Overcome Anxiety$d$, $d$1 Peter 5:7$d$, $d$Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.$d$, $d$Cast is an active word: throw it. All your cares, not some. Why? Because He cares for you. Anxiety isn’t something to manage alone. It’s something to hand over again and again.$d$, $d$I cast all my cares on God, because He cares for me.$d$, $d$I throw my worries on You today, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a throwing exercise today, like a medicine ball, and pray as you throw.$d$, $d$What care do you need to cast on God today?$d$),
('women', 236, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Stand Firm$d$, $d$Ephesians 6:13$d$, $d$Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand.$d$, $d$Sometimes victory looks like simply standing. When you’ve done all you can, stand. God’s armor equips you to hold your ground. You don’t have to win everything today. Just don’t give up ground.$d$, $d$I put on the whole armor of God, and I stand.$d$, $d$Help me stand firm today, Lord.$d$, $d$Do standing strength exercises today with a strong, steady stance.$d$, $d$Where do you need to stand firm right now?$d$),
('women', 237, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$The Armor of God$d$, $d$Ephesians 6:14-17$d$, $d$Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness... taking the shield of faith... And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God.$d$, $d$Truth, righteousness, peace, faith, salvation, the Word: God’s armor covers you completely. Put it on daily through prayer. Get dressed spiritually before you get dressed physically.$d$, $d$I put on the full armor of God every day.$d$, $d$Lord, I put on Your armor today, piece by piece.$d$, $d$As you put on your workout clothes, pray through each piece of the armor of God.$d$, $d$Which piece of armor do you most need today?$d$),
('women', 238, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Joy in Trials$d$, $d$James 1:2-3$d$, $d$My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations; Knowing this, that the trying of your faith worketh patience.$d$, $d$Trials produce patience. Just like muscles grow under resistance, faith grows under testing. Count it joy, not because trials are fun but because they’re building something lasting in you.$d$, $d$I count it all joy, for trials are building patience in me.$d$, $d$Help me see what You’re building in me through this trial, Lord.$d$, $d$Add resistance to your workout today and thank God for growth through struggle.$d$, $d$What is your current trial building in you?$d$),
('women', 239, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Overcomer$d$, $d$1 John 5:4$d$, $d$For whatsoever is born of God overcometh the world: and this is the victory that overcometh the world, even our faith.$d$, $d$Born of God means born to overcome. Your faith is the victory. Not your feelings, not your circumstances. Walk today as an overcomer.$d$, $d$I am born of God, and I overcome the world through faith.$d$, $d$Thank You that I am an overcomer through faith, Lord.$d$, $d$Finish a challenging workout today, declaring you’re an overcomer.$d$, $d$What are you overcoming right now?$d$),
('women', 240, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Rest Day: Kept in Peace$d$, $d$Philippians 4:7$d$, $d$And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.$d$, $d$God’s peace guards your heart and mind like a soldier on watch. It doesn’t always make sense, but it holds. Rest today under that guard.$d$, $d$God’s peace guards my heart and mind.$d$, $d$Guard my heart and mind with Your peace today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Take a quiet walk in nature.$d$, $d$Where do you need God’s peace to stand guard?$d$),
('women', 241, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Fearless Love$d$, $d$Romans 8:15$d$, $d$For ye have not received the spirit of bondage again to fear; but ye have received the Spirit of adoption, whereby we cry, Abba, Father.$d$, $d$You didn’t receive a spirit that keeps you afraid. You received the Spirit of adoption. You can call God Abba, Father. Fear belongs to slaves. You are a daughter.$d$, $d$I have received the Spirit of adoption, and I cry, Abba, Father.$d$, $d$Abba, Father, I am Your daughter, not a slave to fear.$d$, $d$Pray to God as Father today, simply and honestly.$d$, $d$How does being a daughter instead of a slave change your fear?$d$),
('women', 242, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Disciplined Living$d$, $d$1 Corinthians 9:27$d$, $d$But I keep under my body, and bring it into subjection.$d$, $d$Paul disciplined his body, not out of hatred, but so his body would serve his calling. Discipline isn’t punishment. It’s training your body to support your purpose, not run your life.$d$, $d$I discipline my body so it serves God’s purpose for my life.$d$, $d$Give me loving discipline over my body, Lord.$d$, $d$Complete your planned workout today even if you don’t feel like it.$d$, $d$Where does your body need loving discipline?$d$),
('women', 243, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$A Mind Made Whole$d$, $d$Isaiah 26:4$d$, $d$Trust ye in the LORD for ever: for in the LORD JEHOVAH is everlasting strength.$d$, $d$As this month ends, remember what you’ve learned: fear isn’t from God, thoughts can be taken captive, and trust brings strength. His strength is everlasting, so your trust can be too. Keep training your thoughts. A sound mind is built daily.$d$, $d$I trust in the Lord forever, for in Him is everlasting strength.$d$, $d$Keep my mind trusting You, Lord, in every season.$d$, $d$Celebrate your mental strength this month with a peaceful long walk.$d$, $d$How has your thought life changed this month?$d$),
('women', 244, $d$Power, Love, and a Sound Mind$d$, $d$Rejoice Instead$d$, $d$Philippians 4:4$d$, $d$Rejoice in the Lord alway: and again I say, Rejoice.$d$, $d$Paul wrote this from prison, and he said it twice. Rejoicing in the Lord isn’t pretending everything is fine. It’s turning your attention from what’s wrong to who is with you. A rejoicing mind has less room for fear. Practice it today, especially if it feels hard.$d$, $d$I rejoice in the Lord always.$d$, $d$Lord, I choose to rejoice in You today, whatever comes.$d$, $d$Put on worship music and finish your workout rejoicing.$d$, $d$What can you rejoice in about God today, even if circumstances are hard?$d$),
('women', 245, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Anxious for Nothing$d$, $d$Philippians 4:6$d$, $d$Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God.$d$, $d$Paul doesn’t say “try to worry less.” He gives a replacement: in everything, pray. Every worry is an invitation to talk to God. This month, practice turning each anxious thought into a prayer.$d$, $d$I will not fret or be anxious about anything; I pray about everything.$d$, $d$Lord, I bring You every worry today.$d$, $d$Every time you feel anxious today, stop and pray one sentence.$d$, $d$What do you worry about most often?$d$),
('women', 246, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$In Every Thing$d$, $d$Philippians 4:6$d$, $d$But in every thing by prayer.$d$, $d$Everything means everything. Your body, your kids’ schedules, your finances, your workout plan, your bad day. God isn’t only interested in big spiritual matters. He wants to hear about it all.$d$, $d$In everything, I make my requests known to God.$d$, $d$Lord, I’m bringing You the small things too.$d$, $d$Pray about your food choices before each meal today.$d$, $d$What small thing have you not brought to God?$d$),
('women', 247, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$With Thanksgiving$d$, $d$Philippians 4:6$d$, $d$With thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God.$d$, $d$Thanksgiving changes the posture of prayer. You remember what He’s done while you ask for what you need. Gratitude reminds your heart that He has been faithful before and will be again.$d$, $d$I make my requests to God with thanksgiving.$d$, $d$Thank You for all You’ve already done, Lord. Here’s what I need today.$d$, $d$Start every prayer today with three thank-yous.$d$, $d$How does gratitude change the way you pray?$d$),
('women', 248, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Peace Beyond Understanding$d$, $d$Philippians 4:7$d$, $d$And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding.$d$, $d$God’s peace doesn’t always make sense. It shows up in hospital waiting rooms, at gravesides, and in the middle of chaos. It passes understanding because it isn’t based on circumstances. It’s based on Him.$d$, $d$I have God’s peace that passes all understanding.$d$, $d$Give me Your peace today, Lord, even if nothing changes yet.$d$, $d$Do a slow, calming yoga or stretch session.$d$, $d$When have you felt peace that didn’t make sense?$d$),
('women', 249, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Peace on Guard$d$, $d$Philippians 4:7$d$, $d$Shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.$d$, $d$The word keep is a military term: to guard like a garrison. God’s peace stands guard over your heart and mind. When worry tries to break in, peace holds the line.$d$, $d$God’s peace garrisons and guards my heart and mind in Christ Jesus.$d$, $d$Station Your peace at the door of my heart, Lord.$d$, $d$Pray Philippians 4:7 before bed tonight.$d$, $d$What tries to break through the guard of your peace?$d$),
('women', 250, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Think on These$d$, $d$Philippians 4:8$d$, $d$Whatsoever things are true... whatsoever things are lovely... think on these things.$d$, $d$Peace is protected by what you think about. Paul gives a list: true, honest, just, pure, lovely, good. Fill your mind with these, and worry has less room to grow.$d$, $d$I think on what is true, lovely, and good.$d$, $d$Fill my mind with what is lovely today, Lord.$d$, $d$Spend your walk noticing lovely things.$d$, $d$What lovely thing can you focus on today?$d$),
('women', 251, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Rest Day: God of Peace$d$, $d$Philippians 4:9$d$, $d$Those things, which ye have both learned, and received, and heard, and seen in me, do: and the God of peace shall be with you.$d$, $d$The peace of God guards you, and the God of peace is with you. Not just a feeling, but a Person. Rest today in His company.$d$, $d$The God of peace is with me.$d$, $d$God of peace, be with me today.$d$, $d$Rest day. Spend unhurried time with family or friends.$d$, $d$How do you experience God’s presence as peace?$d$),
('women', 252, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Content in Every Season$d$, $d$Philippians 4:11$d$, $d$For I have learned, in whatsoever state I am, therewith to be content.$d$, $d$Contentment is learned. Paul learned it through plenty and through hunger. You can learn it too: contentment with your body today, your season today, your progress today. Contentment doesn’t mean you stop growing. It means you stop fretting.$d$, $d$I have learned to be content in every season.$d$, $d$Teach me contentment, Lord.$d$, $d$Thank God for your body exactly as it is today.$d$, $d$Where do you struggle most with contentment?$d$),
('women', 253, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$God Will Supply$d$, $d$Philippians 4:19$d$, $d$But my God shall supply all your need according to his riches in glory by Christ Jesus.$d$, $d$All your need, according to His riches. Not your bank account, your energy level, or your resources. When worry about provision rises, remember whose riches you’re drawing from.$d$, $d$My God supplies all my needs according to His riches in glory.$d$, $d$I trust You to supply what I need, Lord.$d$, $d$Pray over your budget and grocery list this week.$d$, $d$What need are you trusting God to supply?$d$),
('women', 254, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Prayer Before Panic$d$, $d$Psalm 55:22$d$, $d$Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.$d$, $d$God promises to sustain you when you cast your burden on Him. Not remove every burden instantly, but carry you while you carry it. You won’t be moved.$d$, $d$I cast my burden on the Lord, and He sustains me.$d$, $d$I hand You this burden, Lord. Sustain me.$d$, $d$Do a heavy carry exercise today and pray as you walk with the weight.$d$, $d$What burden are you carrying that God wants to sustain you through?$d$),
('women', 255, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Peace in the Night$d$, $d$Psalm 94:19$d$, $d$In the multitude of my thoughts within me thy comforts delight my soul.$d$, $d$When your thoughts multiply, especially at night, God’s comforts delight your soul. Bring the swirl of thoughts to Him. His comfort is stronger than your racing mind.$d$, $d$In the multitude of my thoughts, God’s comforts delight my soul.$d$, $d$Comfort my racing thoughts, Lord.$d$, $d$Keep a notebook by your bed and write worries down to give to God.$d$, $d$What thoughts multiply when you can’t sleep?$d$),
('women', 256, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Lean Not$d$, $d$Proverbs 3:5-6$d$, $d$Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding. In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.$d$, $d$Peace comes from trusting God more than your own understanding. You won’t always know why. But you can always acknowledge Him, and He will direct your path.$d$, $d$I trust in the Lord with all my heart, and He directs my paths.$d$, $d$I trust You even when I don’t understand, Lord.$d$, $d$Pray about a decision you’re facing during a long walk.$d$, $d$Where are you leaning on your own understanding?$d$),
('women', 257, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Peace with God$d$, $d$Romans 5:1$d$, $d$Therefore being justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ.$d$, $d$Before peace in your circumstances, you have peace with God. The war is over. You’re not on probation. Jesus made peace for you. Every other peace flows from this one.$d$, $d$I am justified by faith and have peace with God through Jesus.$d$, $d$Thank You that I have peace with You, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a gentle, grateful workout today.$d$, $d$How does peace with God affect your other worries?$d$),
('women', 258, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Rest Day: Be Still$d$, $d$Psalm 37:7$d$, $d$Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him: fret not thyself.$d$, $d$Fret not. Rest in the Lord. Wait patiently. Three simple commands for an anxious heart. Today, practice all three.$d$, $d$I rest in the Lord, wait patiently, and do not fret.$d$, $d$Help me rest and not fret today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Take a nap or read a peaceful book.$d$, $d$What do you tend to fret about?$d$),
('women', 259, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Prayer Changes Things$d$, $d$James 5:16$d$, $d$The effectual fervent prayer of a righteous man availeth much.$d$, $d$Your prayers matter. They avail much. Fervent, honest, persistent prayer moves the heart of God. Don’t underestimate what happens when you pray.$d$, $d$My fervent prayers avail much.$d$, $d$Lord, I believe my prayers make a difference.$d$, $d$Pray for one person fervently during your workout today.$d$, $d$What prayer are you persistently bringing to God?$d$),
('women', 260, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Ask, Seek, Knock$d$, $d$Matthew 7:7$d$, $d$Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you.$d$, $d$Jesus invites persistence. Ask, seek, knock. Keep asking. Keep seeking. Keep knocking. Prayer isn’t a one-time request. It’s an ongoing conversation with a Father who loves to give.$d$, $d$I ask, seek, and knock, and God answers me.$d$, $d$I’m still asking, still seeking, still knocking, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a repeated-effort workout today, like intervals or circuits.$d$, $d$What are you still asking God for?$d$),
('women', 261, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Peace in Relationships$d$, $d$Romans 12:18$d$, $d$If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men.$d$, $d$Peace with people is partly in your control and partly not. Do your part: speak kindly, forgive quickly, set healthy boundaries. Leave the rest to God.$d$, $d$As much as it depends on me, I live peaceably with everyone.$d$, $d$Show me my part in making peace, Lord.$d$, $d$Take a walk and pray for someone you’re struggling with.$d$, $d$Is there a relationship where you need to do your part for peace?$d$),
('women', 262, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Thanksgiving Habit$d$, $d$1 Thessalonians 5:18$d$, $d$In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.$d$, $d$Gratitude in everything is God’s will for you. Not for everything, but in everything. Even hard days have something to thank Him for. Thanksgiving trains your heart toward peace.$d$, $d$In everything I give thanks.$d$, $d$Help me find something to thank You for in every moment today, Lord.$d$, $d$Write ten things you’re thankful for after your workout.$d$, $d$What can you thank God for in a hard situation?$d$),
('women', 263, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Peace Through Trust$d$, $d$Psalm 56:3$d$, $d$What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.$d$, $d$David didn’t pretend he was never afraid. He said, when I am afraid, I will trust. Fear may come. Trust is your response. You can feel fear and still choose trust.$d$, $d$When I am afraid, I will trust in God.$d$, $d$When fear comes today, I choose to trust You.$d$, $d$Pray Psalm 56:3 when you feel nervous today.$d$, $d$What makes you afraid right now?$d$),
('women', 264, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Rest Day: Peaceful Home$d$, $d$Proverbs 17:1$d$, $d$Better is a dry morsel, and quietness therewith, than an house full of sacrifices with strife.$d$, $d$A simple meal in peace is better than a feast with strife. Peace is worth protecting. Slow down at home today and choose quietness over perfection.$d$, $d$My home is filled with peace, not strife.$d$, $d$Bring peace to my home today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Have a simple, peaceful family meal.$d$, $d$What would make your home more peaceful?$d$),
('women', 265, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Unworried Tomorrow$d$, $d$Matthew 6:34$d$, $d$Take therefore no thought for the morrow: for the morrow shall take thought for the things of itself. Sufficient unto the day is the evil thereof.$d$, $d$Today has enough. Jesus gently reminds you not to borrow tomorrow’s worries. Tomorrow will come with its own grace. Live today with today’s grace.$d$, $d$I don’t worry about tomorrow; today has enough grace.$d$, $d$Keep me in today, Lord.$d$, $d$Plan only today’s workout and meals.$d$, $d$What tomorrow worry are you carrying today?$d$),
('women', 266, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Birds and Lilies$d$, $d$Matthew 6:26$d$, $d$Behold the fowls of the air: for they sow not, neither do they reap, nor gather into barns; yet your heavenly Father feedeth them. Are ye not much better than they?$d$, $d$Jesus points to birds and flowers as proof of the Father’s care. If He feeds birds, He’ll care for you. You are worth much more to Him. Look at creation today and let it calm your worry.$d$, $d$My heavenly Father cares for me more than the birds of the air.$d$, $d$Thank You for caring for me, Father.$d$, $d$Take a walk in nature and notice how God cares for creation.$d$, $d$How does creation remind you of God’s care?$d$),
('women', 267, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$River of Peace$d$, $d$Isaiah 48:18$d$, $d$O that thou hadst hearkened to my commandments! then had thy peace been as a river.$d$, $d$Peace like a river flows steadily, not in trickles. It comes from listening to God and walking in His ways. Obedience isn’t a burden. It’s a channel for peace.$d$, $d$My peace flows like a river as I listen to God.$d$, $d$Help me listen to You, Lord, so my peace flows like a river.$d$, $d$Walk near water this week if you can.$d$, $d$Where could obedience open the way for more peace?$d$),
('women', 268, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Peace in Change$d$, $d$Hebrews 13:8$d$, $d$Jesus Christ the same yesterday, and to day, and for ever.$d$, $d$Seasons change. Bodies change. Circumstances change. Jesus doesn’t. He is the same yesterday, today, and forever. Anchor your peace to the One who never changes.$d$, $d$Jesus Christ is the same yesterday, today, and forever.$d$, $d$Thank You for being unchanging, Jesus.$d$, $d$Repeat a favorite workout from earlier in the year.$d$, $d$What change is unsettling you right now?$d$),
('women', 269, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Peace Spoken$d$, $d$Numbers 6:24-26$d$, $d$The LORD bless thee, and keep thee: The LORD make his face shine upon thee, and be gracious unto thee: The LORD lift up his countenance upon thee, and give thee peace.$d$, $d$This ancient blessing ends with peace. God’s face shining on you. His grace toward you. His peace given to you. Speak this blessing over yourself and your family today.$d$, $d$The Lord blesses me, keeps me, and gives me peace.$d$, $d$Lord, bless and keep my family, and give us Your peace.$d$, $d$Speak this blessing over your family tonight.$d$, $d$Who can you speak this blessing over today?$d$),
('women', 270, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Rest Day: Sabbath Peace$d$, $d$Hebrews 4:9-10$d$, $d$There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of God. For he that is entered into his rest, he also hath ceased from his own works, as God did from his.$d$, $d$A rest remains for God’s people. Ceasing from your own works is an act of faith. It says God is in control. Enter His rest today.$d$, $d$I enter God’s rest and cease from my striving.$d$, $d$I rest in You today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. No workout, no to-do list. Just rest.$d$, $d$What striving do you need to cease today?$d$),
('women', 271, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Peace Within$d$, $d$Colossians 3:15$d$, $d$And let the peace of God rule in your hearts.$d$, $d$Let peace rule like an umpire in your heart, settling disputes and making the call. When you’re unsure, ask: what brings God’s peace? Let that guide your choices.$d$, $d$The peace of God rules in my heart.$d$, $d$Let Your peace make the call in my heart today, Lord.$d$, $d$Make one decision today based on peace rather than pressure.$d$, $d$What decision needs peace to make the call?$d$),
('women', 272, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Prayer Partners$d$, $d$Matthew 18:19-20$d$, $d$Again I say unto you, That if two of you shall agree on earth as touching any thing that they shall ask, it shall be done for them of my Father which is in heaven.$d$, $d$There is power in agreement. Praying with a friend multiplies faith. Find a sister to pray with this week. God is present when you gather in His name.$d$, $d$I agree in prayer with my sisters, and God hears us.$d$, $d$Lord, give me prayer partners who agree with me in faith.$d$, $d$Invite a friend to walk and pray with you this week.$d$, $d$Who could be your prayer partner?$d$),
('women', 273, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Kept in Peace$d$, $d$2 Thessalonians 3:16$d$, $d$Now the Lord of peace himself give you peace always by all means.$d$, $d$Peace always, by all means. As this month ends, receive peace from the Lord of peace Himself. Keep turning worries into prayers. Peace is guarding you.$d$, $d$The Lord of peace gives me peace always, by all means.$d$, $d$Give me Your peace always, Lord.$d$, $d$Celebrate this month with a peaceful outdoor walk.$d$, $d$How has God’s peace guarded you this month?$d$),
('women', 274, $d$Peace That Guards$d$, $d$Quiet Confidence$d$, $d$Psalm 46:1-2$d$, $d$God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble. Therefore will not we fear, though the earth be removed.$d$, $d$A very present help. Not distant, not delayed, but present right now. Because He is near, the psalmist says we will not fear, even if the ground shakes. Peace isn’t built on steady ground. It’s built on a present God.$d$, $d$God is my refuge and strength, a very present help, so I will not fear.$d$, $d$Thank You for being present with me right now, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a grounding exercise today: slow breathing with your feet planted.$d$, $d$Where do you need to remember God is present right now?$d$),
('women', 275, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Without Faith$d$, $d$Hebrews 11:6$d$, $d$But without faith it is impossible to please him: for he that cometh to God must believe that he is, and that he is a rewarder of them that diligently seek him.$d$, $d$Faith pleases God. Not perfection, not performance, but faith. Two beliefs sit at its center: that He is, and that He rewards those who seek Him. This month, let your faith grow by seeking Him diligently.$d$, $d$I believe that God is, and that He rewards me when I diligently seek Him.$d$, $d$Lord, grow my faith this month.$d$, $d$Write down one area where you’re trusting God by faith right now.$d$, $d$What does faith look like in your daily life?$d$),
('women', 276, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$He Is$d$, $d$Exodus 3:14$d$, $d$And God said unto Moses, I AM THAT I AM.$d$, $d$Faith starts with believing that He is. God is not an idea, a mood, or a mascot. He is the great I AM: present, eternal, self-sufficient. Whatever you need Him to be today, He is.$d$, $d$I believe that God is, and He is enough for me.$d$, $d$I AM, I believe You are here and You are enough.$d$, $d$Walk in silence for ten minutes, aware that God is present.$d$, $d$What do you need God to be for you today?$d$),
('women', 277, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Rewarder$d$, $d$Hebrews 11:6$d$, $d$And that he is a rewarder of them that diligently seek him.$d$, $d$God rewards seeking. Not always with what you asked for, but always with more of Himself, which is the greatest reward. Your early mornings with Him aren’t wasted. He sees and rewards.$d$, $d$God rewards me as I diligently seek Him.$d$, $d$I seek You today, Lord. You are my reward.$d$, $d$Wake up early to seek God before your workout.$d$, $d$How has God rewarded your seeking in the past?$d$),
('women', 278, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Substance of Things Hoped For$d$, $d$Hebrews 11:1$d$, $d$Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.$d$, $d$Faith is substance: something real you can stand on before the answer arrives. It’s evidence before you see. Your faith today is the foundation for tomorrow’s answer.$d$, $d$My faith is the substance of things hoped for.$d$, $d$Give me faith that stands firm before I see the answer, Lord.$d$, $d$Set a fitness goal you’ll need faith and consistency to reach.$d$, $d$What are you hoping for that you can’t yet see?$d$),
('women', 279, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Sarah’s Faith$d$, $d$Hebrews 11:11$d$, $d$Through faith also Sara herself received strength to conceive seed, and was delivered of a child when she was past age, because she judged him faithful who had promised.$d$, $d$Sarah laughed at the promise, but she also received strength because she judged God faithful. Her faith wasn’t perfect, but it was enough. If your faith wobbles, take heart. God still keeps His word.$d$, $d$I judge God faithful who has promised, and I receive strength.$d$, $d$Even when my faith wobbles, Lord, I judge You faithful.$d$, $d$Do a workout today that requires strength, and remember Sarah’s strength.$d$, $d$What promise from God has felt too good to be true?$d$),
('women', 280, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Rahab’s Courage$d$, $d$Hebrews 11:31$d$, $d$By faith the harlot Rahab perished not with them that believed not, when she had received the spies with peace.$d$, $d$Rahab’s past didn’t disqualify her. Her faith made her part of God’s story and the line of Jesus. Whatever your past, faith brings you into His family. Courage turns faith into action.$d$, $d$My past does not disqualify me; my faith brings me into God’s story.$d$, $d$Thank You that You use my story, Lord, past and all.$d$, $d$Do one brave thing today you’ve been putting off.$d$, $d$What part of your past have you believed disqualifies you?$d$),
('women', 281, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Rest Day: Faith Rests$d$, $d$Psalm 116:7$d$, $d$Return unto thy rest, O my soul; for the LORD hath dealt bountifully with thee.$d$, $d$Faith knows how to rest because it remembers how bountifully God has dealt with you. Return to rest today, remembering His goodness.$d$, $d$My soul returns to rest, for the Lord has been good to me.$d$, $d$I rest in Your goodness, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Reflect on God’s goodness over the past year.$d$, $d$How has God dealt bountifully with you this year?$d$),
('women', 282, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Hannah’s Prayer$d$, $d$1 Samuel 1:27$d$, $d$For this child I prayed; and the LORD hath given me my petition which I asked of him.$d$, $d$Hannah poured out her soul before God in a season of deep longing. She prayed so honestly that others thought she was drunk. God heard her. Bring your deepest longings honestly before Him.$d$, $d$God hears my prayers and answers my petitions.$d$, $d$Lord, I pour out my heart to You honestly.$d$, $d$Journal an honest prayer about something you long for.$d$, $d$What longing do you need to pour out before God?$d$),
('women', 283, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Ruth’s Loyalty$d$, $d$Ruth 1:16$d$, $d$Whither thou goest, I will go; and where thou lodgest, I will lodge: thy people shall be my people, and thy God my God.$d$, $d$Ruth chose faithfulness in grief and uncertainty. She followed Naomi and Naomi’s God into an unknown future. Her loyalty led her to Boaz and into the line of Jesus. Faithful choices in hard seasons bear fruit.$d$, $d$I choose faithfulness, even when the future is uncertain.$d$, $d$Make me faithful like Ruth, Lord.$d$, $d$Stay faithful to your workout plan this week, even when it’s hard.$d$, $d$Where is God asking you to be faithful in an uncertain season?$d$),
('women', 284, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Deborah’s Leadership$d$, $d$Judges 4:14$d$, $d$And Deborah said unto Barak, Up; for this is the day in which the LORD hath delivered Sisera into thine hand: is not the LORD gone out before thee?$d$, $d$Deborah led with faith and courage, calling others to rise because God had gone before them. You may be leading in your home, workplace, or community. Lead with faith. Remind others that God goes before them.$d$, $d$I lead with faith, knowing the Lord goes before me.$d$, $d$Help me lead others with faith and courage, Lord.$d$, $d$Lead a friend or family member in a workout this week.$d$, $d$Where are you leading, and how can faith shape it?$d$),
('women', 285, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Mary’s Yes$d$, $d$Luke 1:38$d$, $d$And Mary said, Behold the handmaid of the Lord; be it unto me according to thy word.$d$, $d$Mary didn’t understand everything, but she said yes. Be it unto me according to Your word. Faith often looks like a willing yes before you see the full plan.$d$, $d$I say yes to God: be it unto me according to Your Word.$d$, $d$Lord, I say yes to what You’re asking of me.$d$, $d$Say yes to one healthy change you’ve been resisting.$d$, $d$What is God asking you to say yes to?$d$),
('women', 286, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Blessed Is She Who Believed$d$, $d$Luke 1:45$d$, $d$And blessed is she that believed: for there shall be a performance of those things which were told her from the Lord.$d$, $d$Elizabeth blessed Mary for believing. There’s blessing in believing God’s promises before they come to pass. Believe what He has said over your life. It will be fulfilled.$d$, $d$I am blessed because I believe God will fulfill what He has promised me.$d$, $d$I believe what You’ve spoken over me, Lord.$d$, $d$Write down a promise God has given you and keep it with your workout gear.$d$, $d$What promise are you believing God for?$d$),
('women', 287, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith Like a Seed$d$, $d$Matthew 17:20$d$, $d$If ye have faith as a grain of mustard seed, ye shall say unto this mountain, Remove hence to yonder place; and it shall remove.$d$, $d$Faith doesn’t need to be huge. It needs to be real. Mustard-seed faith can move mountains because it’s planted in a big God. Bring your small faith to Him today.$d$, $d$My faith, even as small as a mustard seed, moves mountains.$d$, $d$Here is my small faith, Lord. Use it to move mountains.$d$, $d$Pray about one mountain in your life during a hill walk.$d$, $d$What mountain are you asking God to move?$d$),
('women', 288, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Rest Day: Faithful Father$d$, $d$Lamentations 3:25$d$, $d$The LORD is good unto them that wait for him, to the soul that seeketh him.$d$, $d$God is good to those who wait for Him. Waiting is an act of faith. Rest today, trusting His goodness as you wait.$d$, $d$The Lord is good to me as I wait for Him.$d$, $d$I wait for You today, Lord, trusting Your goodness.$d$, $d$Rest day. Spend time in quiet waiting prayer.$d$, $d$What are you waiting on God for?$d$),
('women', 289, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith Without Seeing$d$, $d$2 Corinthians 5:7$d$, $d$For we walk by faith, not by sight.$d$, $d$Sight says the progress is slow. Faith says God is working. Sight sees obstacles. Faith sees God. Walk by faith today, especially where sight discourages you.$d$, $d$I walk by faith, not by sight.$d$, $d$Help me walk by faith today, Lord.$d$, $d$Take a long walk and pray about what you can’t see yet.$d$, $d$Where does sight discourage you most?$d$),
('women', 290, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith That Works$d$, $d$James 2:17$d$, $d$Even so faith, if it hath not works, is dead, being alone.$d$, $d$Real faith moves. It shows up in action: prayers prayed, steps taken, kindness given. Faith and work go together, including the daily work of caring for your body and serving others.$d$, $d$My faith is alive and shows up in action.$d$, $d$Let my faith be active today, Lord.$d$, $d$Put your faith into action with a full workout today.$d$, $d$Where does your faith need action?$d$),
('women', 291, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith Grows by Hearing$d$, $d$Romans 10:17$d$, $d$So then faith cometh by hearing, and hearing by the word of God.$d$, $d$Faith grows as you hear God’s Word. If your faith feels weak, feed it with Scripture. Listen to it, read it aloud, meditate on it. Faith comes by hearing.$d$, $d$My faith grows as I hear the Word of God.$d$, $d$Grow my faith through Your Word, Lord.$d$, $d$Listen to Scripture during today’s workout.$d$, $d$How can you hear more of God’s Word this week?$d$),
('women', 292, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$The Shunammite Woman$d$, $d$2 Kings 4:26$d$, $d$And she answered, It is well.$d$, $d$Her son had died, yet she said, It is well. Not denial, but faith. She went straight to the man of God, trusting God could still act. Faith speaks well when circumstances look anything but.$d$, $d$It is well with my soul, because I trust God.$d$, $d$Lord, even now, I say it is well.$d$, $d$Sing or listen to “It Is Well” during your stretch.$d$, $d$Where do you need to declare “it is well” by faith?$d$),
('women', 293, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith in Hard Places$d$, $d$Daniel 3:17-18$d$, $d$Our God whom we serve is able to deliver us... But if not, be it known unto thee, O king, that we will not serve thy gods.$d$, $d$God is able. But if not, we still won’t bow. This is mature faith: trusting God’s ability and His sovereignty. You can believe for a miracle and remain faithful if it doesn’t come the way you hoped.$d$, $d$My God is able, and even if not, I will remain faithful.$d$, $d$Give me “but if not” faith, Lord.$d$, $d$Push through a challenging workout today and remain faithful.$d$, $d$What would “but if not” faith look like for you?$d$),
('women', 294, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Rest Day: Peaceful Faith$d$, $d$Psalm 125:1$d$, $d$They that trust in the LORD shall be as mount Zion, which cannot be removed, but abideth for ever.$d$, $d$Those who trust the Lord are like a mountain: steady, unshakable. Rest today in that steadiness.$d$, $d$I trust in the Lord, and I cannot be moved.$d$, $d$Make me steady like a mountain, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Enjoy time outside.$d$, $d$What helps you feel steady in faith?$d$),
('women', 295, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith and Patience$d$, $d$Hebrews 6:12$d$, $d$That ye be not slothful, but followers of them who through faith and patience inherit the promises.$d$, $d$Promises are inherited through faith and patience. Not one or the other. Faith believes. Patience waits. Together they receive. Keep believing and keep waiting.$d$, $d$I inherit God’s promises through faith and patience.$d$, $d$Give me faith and patience together, Lord.$d$, $d$Track your progress this month to see slow, steady growth.$d$, $d$Which do you need more right now: faith or patience?$d$),
('women', 296, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$The Persistent Widow$d$, $d$Luke 18:1$d$, $d$And he spake a parable unto them to this end, that men ought always to pray, and not to faint.$d$, $d$Jesus told the story of a persistent widow to teach us to pray and not give up. Keep praying. Keep knocking. Your persistence is faith in action.$d$, $d$I always pray and do not give up.$d$, $d$Lord, I will keep praying and not give up.$d$, $d$Do a persistent workout today: repeat a set until you hit your goal.$d$, $d$What prayer are you tempted to stop praying?$d$),
('women', 297, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith Over Feelings$d$, $d$Psalm 42:11$d$, $d$Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him.$d$, $d$The psalmist talks to his own soul. Why are you downcast? Hope in God. Faith sometimes means preaching truth to your feelings. You shall yet praise Him.$d$, $d$I hope in God, and I will yet praise Him.$d$, $d$Lord, I speak hope to my soul today.$d$, $d$Speak Psalm 42:11 to yourself during a hard workout.$d$, $d$What do you need to preach to your own soul today?$d$),
('women', 298, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faithful in Little$d$, $d$Matthew 25:21$d$, $d$Well done, thou good and faithful servant: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things.$d$, $d$Faithfulness in a few things leads to more. God notices the small, daily faithfulness. Your consistency in prayer and health matters to Him. Well done is waiting.$d$, $d$I am faithful in little things, and God entrusts me with more.$d$, $d$Help me be faithful in the little things, Lord.$d$, $d$Complete every small habit on your list today.$d$, $d$What small faithfulness is God asking of you?$d$),
('women', 299, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith for Family$d$, $d$Acts 16:31$d$, $d$Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved, and thy house.$d$, $d$Your faith matters for your household. Keep praying for your family, believing God for their hearts. Your faithfulness can light the way for those you love.$d$, $d$I believe God for my household.$d$, $d$Lord, draw every member of my family to You.$d$, $d$Pray for each family member by name during a walk.$d$, $d$Who in your family are you believing God for?$d$),
('women', 300, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Rest Day: Faith Sabbath$d$, $d$Exodus 20:8$d$, $d$Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy.$d$, $d$Resting one day a week is an act of faith. It says God provides even when you stop working. Keep this day holy and restful.$d$, $d$I remember the Sabbath and keep it holy.$d$, $d$Help me rest in faith today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Unplug for a few hours.$d$, $d$What does a holy rest day look like for you?$d$),
('women', 301, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith in the Fire$d$, $d$1 Peter 1:7$d$, $d$That the trial of your faith, being much more precious than of gold that perisheth, though it be tried with fire, might be found unto praise and honour and glory at the appearing of Jesus Christ.$d$, $d$Your tested faith is more precious than gold. Fire refines, it doesn’t destroy. The trials you face are purifying something beautiful in you.$d$, $d$My tested faith is more precious than gold.$d$, $d$Refine my faith in this fire, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a high-intensity workout today and thank God for refining.$d$, $d$What is God refining in you through your current trial?$d$),
('women', 302, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Author and Finisher$d$, $d$Hebrews 12:2$d$, $d$Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith.$d$, $d$Jesus started your faith, and He will finish it. Fix your eyes on Him. When you look at yourself, you’ll see weakness. When you look at Him, you’ll see the finisher.$d$, $d$I look to Jesus, the author and finisher of my faith.$d$, $d$Jesus, I fix my eyes on You.$d$, $d$Finish a challenging workout today, keeping your focus on Jesus.$d$, $d$Where have your eyes drifted from Jesus?$d$),
('women', 303, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith Remembers$d$, $d$Psalm 77:11$d$, $d$I will remember the works of the LORD: surely I will remember thy wonders of old.$d$, $d$Remembering builds faith. Look back at what God has done: answered prayers, rescues, provision. If He did it before, He can do it again.$d$, $d$I remember the works of the Lord and His wonders.$d$, $d$I remember Your faithfulness, Lord.$d$, $d$Write a list of answered prayers from this year.$d$, $d$What answered prayer strengthens your faith today?$d$),
('women', 304, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Bold Faith$d$, $d$Hebrews 4:16$d$, $d$Let us therefore come boldly unto the throne of grace, that we may obtain mercy, and find grace to help in time of need.$d$, $d$Faith comes boldly, not timidly. You can approach God’s throne with confidence because of Jesus. Bring your needs boldly today. Grace is waiting.$d$, $d$I come boldly to the throne of grace.$d$, $d$I come to You boldly, Lord, for grace in my need.$d$, $d$Pray boldly for something big during your workout.$d$, $d$What do you need to bring boldly to God?$d$),
('women', 305, $d$Faith That Pleases Him$d$, $d$Faith That Pleases$d$, $d$Hebrews 11:39-40$d$, $d$And these all, having obtained a good report through faith, received not the promise: God having provided some better thing for us.$d$, $d$The heroes of faith didn’t see everything fulfilled, but they obtained a good report through faith. As this month ends, know this: your faith pleases God, whether or not you see every answer yet.$d$, $d$My faith pleases God, and I obtain a good report through faith.$d$, $d$Thank You that my faith pleases You, Lord.$d$, $d$Celebrate your faithfulness this month with a favorite workout.$d$, $d$How has your faith grown this month?$d$),
('women', 306, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Surrounded by Favor$d$, $d$Psalm 5:12$d$, $d$For thou, LORD, wilt bless the righteous; with favour wilt thou compass him as with a shield.$d$, $d$God’s favor surrounds you like a shield. Favor isn’t luck. It’s the kindness of God going before you and around you. This month, expect His favor and watch for it.$d$, $d$I am favored, and God surrounds me with favor like a shield.$d$, $d$Thank You for surrounding me with favor, Lord.$d$, $d$Walk today and look for signs of God’s favor in your life.$d$, $d$Where have you seen God’s favor recently?$d$),
('women', 307, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Work of My Hands$d$, $d$Deuteronomy 28:12$d$, $d$The LORD shall open unto thee his good treasure, the heaven to give the rain unto thy land in his season, and to bless all the work of thine hand.$d$, $d$God promises to bless the work of your hands: your job, your home, your family, your business, your training. Your work isn’t outside His interest. Invite Him into all of it.$d$, $d$The work of my hands is blessed, and I prosper in all I do.$d$, $d$Bless the work of my hands today, Lord.$d$, $d$Dedicate today’s work and workout to God.$d$, $d$What work do you want God to bless?$d$),
('women', 308, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Establish My Work$d$, $d$Psalm 90:17$d$, $d$And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it.$d$, $d$Moses prayed twice for God to establish the work of their hands. Work established by God lasts. Ask Him to make your efforts count and to let His beauty rest on what you do.$d$, $d$God establishes the work of my hands, and His beauty rests on me.$d$, $d$Establish what I build, Lord, and let Your beauty rest on it.$d$, $d$Pray over your work tasks before starting today.$d$, $d$What work are you asking God to establish?$d$),
('women', 309, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Open Doors$d$, $d$Revelation 3:8$d$, $d$Behold, I have set before thee an open door, and no man can shut it.$d$, $d$When God opens a door, no one can shut it. Not a person, not a past mistake, not your fear. Watch for the open doors He sets before you, and walk through with courage.$d$, $d$Doors of opportunity open for me today, and no one can shut them.$d$, $d$Show me the doors You’re opening, Lord, and give me courage to walk through.$d$, $d$Say yes to one new opportunity this week.$d$, $d$What door might God be opening for you?$d$),
('women', 310, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Favor with God and People$d$, $d$Luke 2:52$d$, $d$And Jesus increased in wisdom and stature, and in favour with God and man.$d$, $d$Jesus grew in wisdom, in stature, and in favor with God and people. Growth in every area is part of a healthy life: mind, body, spirit, and relationships. Ask God for growth in all four.$d$, $d$I increase in wisdom, strength, and favor with God and people.$d$, $d$Grow me in every area, Lord, like Jesus.$d$, $d$Do something today for each area: mind, body, spirit, and relationships.$d$, $d$Which area of growth needs attention right now?$d$),
('women', 311, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Joseph’s Favor$d$, $d$Genesis 39:21$d$, $d$But the LORD was with Joseph, and shewed him mercy, and gave him favour in the sight of the keeper of the prison.$d$, $d$Joseph found favor even in prison. God’s favor doesn’t disappear in hard places. It often shows up there. If you’re in a difficult season, His favor is still with you.$d$, $d$The Lord is with me, and I have favor even in hard places.$d$, $d$Thank You for favor in hard places, Lord.$d$, $d$Do your workout today even if circumstances are difficult.$d$, $d$Where have you found God’s favor in a hard season?$d$),
('women', 312, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Rest Day: Blessed Rest$d$, $d$Psalm 127:1$d$, $d$Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it.$d$, $d$Your labor matters, but God builds the house. Resting is a reminder that He is the true builder. Rest today in His work.$d$, $d$The Lord builds my house, and I rest in Him.$d$, $d$Build my life, Lord. I rest in You.$d$, $d$Rest day. Let your body recover fully.$d$, $d$What are you trying to build without God’s help?$d$),
('women', 313, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Diligent Hands$d$, $d$Proverbs 10:4$d$, $d$He becometh poor that dealeth with a slack hand: but the hand of the diligent maketh rich.$d$, $d$Diligence brings increase in your finances, your health, and your relationships. God blesses diligent hands. Show up faithfully today in your work and your training.$d$, $d$My hands are diligent, and they bring increase.$d$, $d$Make me diligent in all I do, Lord.$d$, $d$Complete every set of today’s workout with full effort.$d$, $d$Where could more diligence bring increase?$d$),
('women', 314, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$As Unto the Lord$d$, $d$Colossians 3:23$d$, $d$And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men.$d$, $d$Whatever you do, work at it heartily, as for the Lord. Laundry, spreadsheets, workouts, carpools: all of it can be worship when done for Him. You don’t need an audience. He sees.$d$, $d$Whatever I do, I do it heartily, as unto the Lord.$d$, $d$Let all my work today be for You, Lord.$d$, $d$Do today’s workout heartily, as an offering to God.$d$, $d$What task could you do as worship today?$d$),
('women', 315, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$The Virtuous Woman’s Work$d$, $d$Proverbs 31:17$d$, $d$She girdeth her loins with strength, and strengtheneth her arms.$d$, $d$The Proverbs 31 woman strengthens her arms for her work. Physical strength serves her purpose. Your strength isn’t vanity. It’s preparation for the work God gives you.$d$, $d$I gird myself with strength and strengthen my arms for my work.$d$, $d$Strengthen me for the work You’ve given me, Lord.$d$, $d$Do an arm and shoulder workout today.$d$, $d$What work does your strength serve?$d$),
('women', 316, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$She Considers a Field$d$, $d$Proverbs 31:16$d$, $d$She considereth a field, and buyeth it: with the fruit of her hands she planteth a vineyard.$d$, $d$She considers, she decides, she plants. The virtuous woman is wise and enterprising. God blesses women who think carefully and act boldly. Plant something today that will bear fruit later.$d$, $d$I consider wisely, act boldly, and plant fruitful vineyards.$d$, $d$Give me wisdom and courage to plant for the future, Lord.$d$, $d$Start a long-term health habit today.$d$, $d$What field are you considering?$d$),
('women', 317, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Fruitful Branches$d$, $d$Psalm 1:3$d$, $d$And he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper.$d$, $d$Rooted in God’s Word, you bear fruit in season and your leaves don’t wither. Whatever you do prospers. Stay planted by the water of His Word.$d$, $d$I am planted by rivers of water, and whatever I do prospers.$d$, $d$Keep me planted by Your Word, Lord.$d$, $d$Read Psalm 1 before your workout.$d$, $d$What fruit is God growing in your life this season?$d$),
('women', 318, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Grateful Heart$d$, $d$Psalm 100:4$d$, $d$Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, and into his courts with praise: be thankful unto him, and bless his name.$d$, $d$Thanksgiving is the gate into God’s presence. Gratitude opens the way. As you enter this season of thanksgiving, start every prayer with thanks.$d$, $d$I enter His gates with thanksgiving and His courts with praise.$d$, $d$Thank You, Lord, for everything. I bless Your name.$d$, $d$Write ten things you’re thankful for after your workout.$d$, $d$What are you most thankful for this year?$d$),
('women', 319, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Rest Day: Thankful Rest$d$, $d$Psalm 107:1$d$, $d$O give thanks unto the LORD, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.$d$, $d$He is good. His mercy endures forever. Rest today with a thankful heart.$d$, $d$I give thanks to the Lord, for He is good.$d$, $d$Thank You for Your enduring mercy, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Share a thankful meal with family or friends.$d$, $d$How has God’s mercy endured in your life?$d$),
('women', 320, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Blessed to Bless$d$, $d$Genesis 12:2$d$, $d$And I will bless thee, and make thy name great; and thou shalt be a blessing.$d$, $d$God blesses you so that you can be a blessing. Favor isn’t meant to stop with you. Let it flow through you to others.$d$, $d$I am blessed to be a blessing.$d$, $d$Make me a blessing to someone today, Lord.$d$, $d$Bless someone today with your time or encouragement.$d$, $d$How can your blessing flow to someone else?$d$),
('women', 321, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Increase$d$, $d$Psalm 115:14$d$, $d$The LORD shall increase you more and more, you and your children.$d$, $d$God promises increase, more and more, for you and your children. Increase in strength, wisdom, joy, and faith. Your family benefits from your growth.$d$, $d$The Lord increases me more and more, me and my children.$d$, $d$Increase me in every good way, Lord, me and my family.$d$, $d$Increase your workout slightly today: one more set or a little more weight.$d$, $d$What increase are you believing God for?$d$),
('women', 322, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Favor at Work$d$, $d$Nehemiah 2:8$d$, $d$And the king granted me, according to the good hand of my God upon me.$d$, $d$Nehemiah received favor from the king because God’s good hand was on him. Pray for favor in your workplace, with your boss, your clients, your coworkers. God’s hand can move hearts.$d$, $d$The good hand of my God is upon me, and I have favor at work.$d$, $d$Give me favor in my work, Lord.$d$, $d$Pray for favor before an important meeting or task.$d$, $d$Where do you need favor at work?$d$),
('women', 323, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Wisdom for Work$d$, $d$Proverbs 16:9$d$, $d$A man’s heart deviseth his way: but the LORD directeth his steps.$d$, $d$Plan your work, but let God direct your steps. He may redirect you. Hold your plans loosely and trust His leading.$d$, $d$I make plans, and the Lord directs my steps.$d$, $d$Direct my steps today, Lord.$d$, $d$Plan your week, then pray over it.$d$, $d$Where might God be redirecting your plans?$d$),
('women', 324, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Fruit That Remains$d$, $d$John 15:16$d$, $d$Ye have not chosen me, but I have chosen you, and ordained you, that ye should go and bring forth fruit, and that your fruit should remain.$d$, $d$You were chosen and appointed to bear fruit that lasts. Your influence, kindness, and faithfulness leave a lasting mark. Lasting fruit grows from lasting connection to Jesus.$d$, $d$I am chosen to bear fruit that remains.$d$, $d$Let my life bear lasting fruit, Lord.$d$, $d$Invest in someone’s growth this week: mentor, encourage, or teach.$d$, $d$What lasting fruit do you want your life to bear?$d$),
('women', 325, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Rest Day: Content$d$, $d$Hebrews 13:5$d$, $d$Be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.$d$, $d$Contentment flows from His presence: I will never leave you. Rest today in what you have and Who you have.$d$, $d$I am content, for God will never leave me.$d$, $d$Thank You for never leaving me, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Enjoy what you have without striving for more.$d$, $d$What helps you feel content?$d$),
('women', 326, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Generous Hands$d$, $d$Proverbs 11:25$d$, $d$The liberal soul shall be made fat: and he that watereth shall be watered also himself.$d$, $d$Generosity brings refreshing. When you water others, you’re watered too. Give your time, encouragement, or resources, and watch God refresh you.$d$, $d$I am generous, and as I water others, I am refreshed.$d$, $d$Make me generous, Lord.$d$, $d$Give generously to someone in need this week.$d$, $d$Where could you be more generous?$d$),
('women', 327, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Season of Harvest$d$, $d$Psalm 126:5-6$d$, $d$They that sow in tears shall reap in joy. He that goeth forth and weepeth, bearing precious seed, shall doubtless come again with rejoicing, bringing his sheaves with him.$d$, $d$Seeds sown in tears bring a harvest of joy. If you’ve been sowing through hard seasons, take heart. Harvest is coming, with rejoicing.$d$, $d$I sow in tears, and I reap in joy.$d$, $d$Bring a harvest of joy from my tears, Lord.$d$, $d$Celebrate a harvest of progress in your health this year.$d$, $d$What harvest are you waiting for?$d$),
('women', 328, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Wholehearted Work$d$, $d$Ecclesiastes 9:10$d$, $d$Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do it with thy might.$d$, $d$Whatever is in front of you today, do it with all your might. Not halfway, not distracted. Wholehearted work honors God and brings satisfaction.$d$, $d$Whatever my hand finds to do, I do it with all my might.$d$, $d$Help me give my whole heart to today’s work, Lord.$d$, $d$Do today’s workout with full focus and effort.$d$, $d$Where are you working halfheartedly?$d$),
('women', 329, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Favor Like a Crown$d$, $d$Proverbs 4:9$d$, $d$She shall give to thine head an ornament of grace: a crown of glory shall she deliver to thee.$d$, $d$Wisdom crowns you with grace and glory. As you walk in wisdom, favor rests on you like a crown. Choose wisdom today in small decisions.$d$, $d$Wisdom crowns me with grace and glory.$d$, $d$Crown me with wisdom and grace today, Lord.$d$, $d$Make one wise health choice today.$d$, $d$What wise choice can you make today?$d$),
('women', 330, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Thankful in All$d$, $d$Ephesians 5:20$d$, $d$Giving thanks always for all things unto God and the Father in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.$d$, $d$Giving thanks always, for all things. Gratitude reshapes your heart and your view of your life. Practice it all day today.$d$, $d$I give thanks always for all things.$d$, $d$Thank You for all things, Lord.$d$, $d$Thank God out loud for each part of your workout.$d$, $d$What are you thankful for that you usually overlook?$d$),
('women', 331, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Rest Day: Gratitude Sabbath$d$, $d$Psalm 92:1$d$, $d$It is a good thing to give thanks unto the LORD, and to sing praises unto thy name, O most High.$d$, $d$It is good to give thanks. Rest today with songs of praise and grateful prayers.$d$, $d$It is good for me to give thanks to the Lord.$d$, $d$I praise You, Most High.$d$, $d$Rest day. Sing praise songs with your family.$d$, $d$What song of praise is on your heart?$d$),
('women', 332, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$God Gives Increase$d$, $d$1 Corinthians 3:7$d$, $d$So then neither is he that planteth any thing, neither he that watereth; but God that giveth the increase.$d$, $d$You plant and water, but God gives the increase. Do your part faithfully and trust Him with the results.$d$, $d$I plant and water faithfully, and God gives the increase.$d$, $d$I trust You with the results, Lord.$d$, $d$Do your workout faithfully today and leave the results to God.$d$, $d$What results are you trying to control?$d$),
('women', 333, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Favor Rests$d$, $d$Psalm 30:5$d$, $d$For his anger endureth but a moment; in his favour is life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning.$d$, $d$In His favor is life. Weeping may last for a night, but joy comes in the morning. Hard seasons don’t last forever. Morning is coming.$d$, $d$In God’s favor is life, and joy comes in the morning.$d$, $d$Bring morning joy to my night season, Lord.$d$, $d$Do an early-morning workout this week as a reminder that joy comes in the morning.$d$, $d$What night season are you waiting to see morning in?$d$),
('women', 334, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Pleasant Places$d$, $d$Psalm 16:6$d$, $d$The lines are fallen unto me in pleasant places; yea, I have a goodly heritage.$d$, $d$As this month of favor and fruitful work ends, look at the boundary lines of your life: your family, your work, your health, your faith. In Christ, they have fallen in pleasant places. Thank Him for the heritage He has given you and the fruit He has grown.$d$, $d$The lines have fallen for me in pleasant places, and I have a goodly heritage.$d$, $d$Thank You for the life and heritage You’ve given me, Lord.$d$, $d$Write down the fruit God has grown in your life this year.$d$, $d$What fruit has God grown in you this year?$d$),
('women', 335, $d$Favor and Fruitful Work$d$, $d$Fruit in Old Age$d$, $d$Psalm 92:14$d$, $d$They shall still bring forth fruit in old age; they shall be fat and flourishing.$d$, $d$God’s plan for your fruitfulness doesn’t expire. The righteous still bear fruit in old age, full of life and flourishing. Caring for your body now is an investment in decades of fruitful living, serving your family and your community for years to come.$d$, $d$I will bear fruit in every season of life, flourishing and full of life.$d$, $d$Let me flourish and bear fruit all my life, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a mobility session today to invest in long-term strength.$d$, $d$What kind of woman do you want to be in your later years?$d$),
('women', 336, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Light of the World$d$, $d$Matthew 5:14$d$, $d$Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid.$d$, $d$Jesus doesn’t say you could be light someday. He says you are. A city on a hill can’t be hidden. Your life, your joy, your strength, your faith shine whether you notice or not. This month, let your light shine on purpose.$d$, $d$I am a light wherever I go and a solution to every challenge.$d$, $d$Lord, let Your light shine through me today.$d$, $d$Smile at and encourage three people today.$d$, $d$Where is God asking you to shine this month?$d$),
('women', 337, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Let It Shine$d$, $d$Matthew 5:16$d$, $d$Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.$d$, $d$Your light points to the Father. Good works aren’t for applause. They’re for His glory. When people see your faithfulness, kindness, and joy, they catch a glimpse of God.$d$, $d$My light shines so that others glorify my Father in heaven.$d$, $d$Let my good works point people to You, Lord.$d$, $d$Do a good deed today without telling anyone.$d$, $d$How can your daily life point people to God?$d$),
('women', 338, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Arise and Shine$d$, $d$Isaiah 60:1$d$, $d$Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of the LORD is risen upon thee.$d$, $d$Arise. Shine. Your light has come. The glory of the Lord has risen on you. It’s time to get up from discouragement and shine. Not by your own glow, but by His glory on you.$d$, $d$I arise and shine, for the glory of the Lord has risen upon me.$d$, $d$I arise today, Lord. Shine on me and through me.$d$, $d$Do an energizing morning workout to start your day with light.$d$, $d$What has kept you from rising and shining?$d$),
('women', 339, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Lamp on a Stand$d$, $d$Matthew 5:15$d$, $d$Neither do men light a candle, and put it under a bushel, but on a candlestick; and it giveth light unto all that are in the house.$d$, $d$Lights aren’t meant to be hidden. Your gifts, your story, your faith are meant to give light to everyone in the house: your family, your friends, your community. Don’t hide your light.$d$, $d$I put my light on a stand, and it gives light to everyone in my house.$d$, $d$Help me stop hiding the light You’ve given me, Lord.$d$, $d$Share your faith or your fitness journey with someone this week.$d$, $d$What light have you been hiding?$d$),
('women', 340, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Light in Darkness$d$, $d$John 1:5$d$, $d$And the light shineth in darkness; and the darkness comprehended it not.$d$, $d$Darkness can’t overcome light. One small candle changes a dark room. Wherever you go today, even in dark places, the light of Christ in you is stronger than the darkness around you.$d$, $d$The light in me shines in darkness, and the darkness cannot overcome it.$d$, $d$Let Your light in me overcome every darkness, Jesus.$d$, $d$Light a candle during your evening prayer this week.$d$, $d$Where is there darkness that your light could reach?$d$),
('women', 341, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Children of Light$d$, $d$Ephesians 5:8$d$, $d$For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in the Lord: walk as children of light.$d$, $d$You were once darkness, but now you are light in the Lord. Not just carrying light, but being light. Walk as a daughter of light today: honest, joyful, kind.$d$, $d$I am light in the Lord, and I walk as a child of light.$d$, $d$Help me walk as Your child of light today, Lord.$d$, $d$Take a sunrise or sunset walk this week.$d$, $d$What does walking as a child of light look like for you?$d$),
('women', 342, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Rest Day: Light and Rest$d$, $d$Psalm 36:9$d$, $d$For with thee is the fountain of life: in thy light shall we see light.$d$, $d$In His light, you see light. Rest today in His presence, the fountain of life.$d$, $d$In God’s light, I see light.$d$, $d$Let me rest in Your light today, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Enjoy natural light and quiet.$d$, $d$How does God’s light help you see clearly?$d$),
('women', 343, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$A Solution, Not a Problem$d$, $d$Proverbs 31:26$d$, $d$She openeth her mouth with wisdom; and in her tongue is the law of kindness.$d$, $d$Being a solution often starts with your words. Wisdom and kindness on your tongue can turn conflict to peace and confusion to clarity. Be a source of wise, kind words today.$d$, $d$I open my mouth with wisdom, and kindness is on my tongue.$d$, $d$Fill my words with wisdom and kindness today, Lord.$d$, $d$Offer a helpful, kind word to someone who is struggling.$d$, $d$Where can your words bring a solution today?$d$),
('women', 344, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Salt and Light$d$, $d$Matthew 5:13$d$, $d$Ye are the salt of the earth.$d$, $d$Salt preserves and adds flavor. You bring something to the places you go. Your faith adds goodness and preserves what is right. Don’t lose your saltiness by blending in.$d$, $d$I am the salt of the earth, bringing goodness wherever I go.$d$, $d$Keep me salty and bright for You, Lord.$d$, $d$Cook a flavorful, healthy meal and share it with someone.$d$, $d$What do you bring to the places you go?$d$),
('women', 345, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Radiant Faces$d$, $d$Psalm 34:5$d$, $d$They looked unto him, and were lightened: and their faces were not ashamed.$d$, $d$Those who look to God are radiant. Their faces aren’t covered with shame. As you look to Him, His light reflects on you. Shame has no place on a face turned toward God.$d$, $d$I look to God and I am radiant; my face is not ashamed.$d$, $d$Make me radiant as I look to You, Lord.$d$, $d$Do your workout today with your head up and a smile.$d$, $d$What shame are you ready to release?$d$),
('women', 346, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Light for Others$d$, $d$Isaiah 58:10$d$, $d$And if thou draw out thy soul to the hungry, and satisfy the afflicted soul; then shall thy light rise in obscurity, and thy darkness be as the noonday.$d$, $d$When you pour yourself out for others, your light rises. Serving the hurting brings light into your own darkness. Look for someone to serve this week.$d$, $d$As I pour out for others, my light rises and shines like noonday.$d$, $d$Show me who to serve this week, Lord.$d$, $d$Serve at a local food bank or bless a neighbor with a meal.$d$, $d$Who is hungry or hurting that you could serve?$d$),
('women', 347, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Advent Hope$d$, $d$Isaiah 9:2$d$, $d$The people that walked in darkness have seen a great light: they that dwell in the land of the shadow of death, upon them hath the light shined.$d$, $d$Into a dark world, a great light came: Jesus. As you move toward the end of the year, remember the Light that came for you. He still shines into every dark place.$d$, $d$I have seen a great light, and His light shines on me.$d$, $d$Thank You for coming as the Light of the world, Jesus.$d$, $d$Take an evening walk and look at the lights around you.$d$, $d$Where has the light of Jesus shone in your darkness this year?$d$),
('women', 348, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Immanuel$d$, $d$Matthew 1:23$d$, $d$Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us.$d$, $d$God with us. Not distant, not detached, but with us. In your workout, your kitchen, your hard conversations, and your quiet mornings, He is with you.$d$, $d$God is with me, Emmanuel.$d$, $d$Thank You for being with me, Emmanuel.$d$, $d$Pray throughout your workout, aware that God is with you.$d$, $d$Where do you need to remember that God is with you?$d$),
('women', 349, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Rest Day: Wonderful Counselor$d$, $d$Isaiah 9:6$d$, $d$For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulder: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace.$d$, $d$Wonderful Counselor. Mighty God. Everlasting Father. Prince of Peace. The government is on His shoulders, not yours. Rest today under His rule.$d$, $d$Jesus is my Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, and Prince of Peace.$d$, $d$Prince of Peace, I rest in Your rule today.$d$, $d$Rest day. Read Isaiah 9:6 slowly and worship.$d$, $d$Which name of Jesus do you need most right now?$d$),
('women', 350, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Good Tidings$d$, $d$Luke 2:10$d$, $d$And the angel said unto them, Fear not: for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, which shall be to all people.$d$, $d$Fear not. Great joy. For all people. The message of Jesus is good news for everyone, including the woman who feels behind, broken, or unseen. Let great joy fill you today.$d$, $d$I receive good tidings of great joy, and I do not fear.$d$, $d$Fill me with the great joy of Your coming, Jesus.$d$, $d$Share good news or encouragement with someone today.$d$, $d$Who needs to hear good news from you?$d$),
('women', 351, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Treasured Things$d$, $d$Luke 2:19$d$, $d$But Mary kept all these things, and pondered them in her heart.$d$, $d$Mary treasured and pondered. As the year winds down, take time to treasure what God has done. Ponder the moments that mattered. Gratitude grows in reflection.$d$, $d$I treasure and ponder all that God has done in my heart.$d$, $d$Help me treasure what You’ve done this year, Lord.$d$, $d$Journal your favorite moments from this year.$d$, $d$What moment from this year do you want to treasure?$d$),
('women', 352, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Glory to God$d$, $d$Luke 2:14$d$, $d$Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men.$d$, $d$Glory to God and peace on earth. Worship and peace go together. Give God glory today, and carry His peace to the people around you.$d$, $d$I give glory to God in the highest, and I carry His peace.$d$, $d$Glory to You in the highest, Lord.$d$, $d$Worship for ten minutes before your workout.$d$, $d$How can you carry God’s peace to others this week?$d$),
('women', 353, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Shine Together$d$, $d$Philippians 2:15$d$, $d$That ye may be blameless and harmless, the sons of God, without rebuke, in the midst of a crooked and perverse nation, among whom ye shine as lights in the world.$d$, $d$You shine like stars in the world. Not alone, but together with your sisters in faith. Encourage another woman today to keep shining.$d$, $d$I shine as a light in the world.$d$, $d$Let me shine like a star, Lord, and help my sisters shine too.$d$, $d$Invite a friend to join you in a workout or Bible study.$d$, $d$Which sister in faith could you encourage today?$d$),
('women', 354, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Walk in the Light$d$, $d$1 John 1:7$d$, $d$But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanseth us from all sin.$d$, $d$Walking in the light means honesty, confession, and fellowship. Nothing hidden. As you walk in the light, you’re cleansed and connected. Let the light into every room of your life.$d$, $d$I walk in the light, and I am cleansed and connected.$d$, $d$Help me walk in the light, honest and open before You, Lord.$d$, $d$Be honest with a trusted friend about a struggle this week.$d$, $d$What do you need to bring into the light?$d$),
('women', 355, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Lit From Within$d$, $d$Proverbs 20:27$d$, $d$The spirit of man is the candle of the LORD, searching all the inward parts of the belly.$d$, $d$Your spirit is the lamp of the Lord. He lights you from within and searches your heart. Let Him search you gently and shine light where it’s needed.$d$, $d$My spirit is the lamp of the Lord.$d$, $d$Search my heart, Lord, and light up every corner.$d$, $d$Spend ten minutes in quiet reflection and prayer.$d$, $d$What is God gently showing you in your heart?$d$),
('women', 356, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Rest Day: Peace on Earth$d$, $d$John 16:33$d$, $d$These things I have spoken unto you, that in me ye might have peace. In the world ye shall have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world.$d$, $d$In the world, trouble. In Him, peace. Be of good cheer: He has overcome the world. Rest today in His victory.$d$, $d$In Jesus I have peace, for He has overcome the world.$d$, $d$Thank You for overcoming the world, Jesus.$d$, $d$Rest day. Enjoy a peaceful day with family.$d$, $d$Where do you need His peace in the middle of trouble?$d$),
('women', 357, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$The Word Made Flesh$d$, $d$John 1:14$d$, $d$And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us.$d$, $d$God took on flesh. He knows what it’s like to be tired, hungry, and hurting. Your body matters to Him because He had one too. He understands your physical struggles.$d$, $d$The Word was made flesh, and He understands my weakness.$d$, $d$Thank You for knowing what it’s like to be human, Jesus.$d$, $d$Thank God for your body during today’s workout.$d$, $d$How does Jesus becoming human comfort you?$d$),
('women', 358, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Gifts Given$d$, $d$Matthew 2:11$d$, $d$And when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.$d$, $d$The wise men brought their treasures to Jesus. What gift can you bring Him this season? Your time, your heart, your strength, your praise. Present your best to Him.$d$, $d$I bring my best gifts to Jesus.$d$, $d$Here’s my heart, my time, and my strength, Jesus.$d$, $d$Give God your first hour tomorrow morning.$d$, $d$What gift can you offer Jesus this season?$d$),
('women', 359, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Joy to the World$d$, $d$Psalm 98:4$d$, $d$Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all the earth: make a loud noise, and rejoice, and sing praise.$d$, $d$Make a joyful noise! Sing loud, rejoice, praise. Joy is a powerful light. Let your joy be loud today.$d$, $d$I make a joyful noise to the Lord.$d$, $d$I rejoice in You today, Lord!$d$, $d$Have a dance workout with worship music today.$d$, $d$What fills you with joy right now?$d$),
('women', 360, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$A Savior Is Born$d$, $d$Luke 2:11$d$, $d$For unto you is born this day in the city of David a Saviour, which is Christ the Lord.$d$, $d$Unto you. Personal. Specific. A Savior was born for you. Every gift, every promise, every devotional this year flows from this one gift. Celebrate Him today.$d$, $d$A Savior was born for me, Christ the Lord.$d$, $d$Thank You for coming for me, Jesus.$d$, $d$Spend time worshiping with your family today.$d$, $d$What does it mean to you that Jesus came for you?$d$),
('women', 361, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Rest Day: Christmas Peace$d$, $d$Luke 2:20$d$, $d$And the shepherds returned, glorifying and praising God for all the things that they had heard and seen.$d$, $d$The shepherds returned glorifying and praising God. After the wonder comes the return to ordinary life, now filled with praise. Rest and praise today.$d$, $d$I glorify and praise God for all I have heard and seen.$d$, $d$I praise You for all You’ve done, Lord.$d$, $d$Rest day. Rest and enjoy your family.$d$, $d$What have you seen God do that you can praise Him for?$d$),
('women', 362, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Forgetting What Is Behind$d$, $d$Philippians 3:13-14$d$, $d$Forgetting those things which are behind, and reaching forth unto those things which are before, I press toward the mark for the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus.$d$, $d$As the year ends, let go of what’s behind: failures, regrets, and even past successes. Press forward. Your calling is ahead of you, not behind.$d$, $d$I forget what is behind and press toward the prize of God’s high calling.$d$, $d$Help me let go of this year and press forward, Lord.$d$, $d$Write down what you’re leaving behind and what you’re pressing toward.$d$, $d$What do you need to leave behind this year?$d$),
('women', 363, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Finished Well$d$, $d$2 Timothy 4:7$d$, $d$I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith.$d$, $d$Fought, finished, kept the faith. You may not feel like you finished perfectly, but you kept going. That matters. Celebrate your faithfulness this year.$d$, $d$I have fought a good fight, and I have kept the faith.$d$, $d$Thank You for helping me keep the faith this year, Lord.$d$, $d$Celebrate your year of workouts with a favorite routine.$d$, $d$What are you proud of from this year?$d$),
('women', 364, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$The Good Work Continues$d$, $d$Philippians 1:6$d$, $d$Being confident of this very thing, that he which hath begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ.$d$, $d$You started the year with this verse, and you end it here too. He who began a good work in you is still working. He isn’t finished with you. Step into the new year confident in His faithfulness.$d$, $d$I am convinced and sure that He who began a good work in me will bring it to full completion.$d$, $d$Thank You for the good work You’ve done this year and for what’s ahead, Lord.$d$, $d$Set your goals for next year with prayer.$d$, $d$What good work do you see God continuing in you?$d$),
('women', 365, $d$A Light Wherever I Go$d$, $d$Go Forth in Victory$d$, $d$1 Corinthians 15:57$d$, $d$But thanks be to God, which giveth us the victory through our Lord Jesus Christ.$d$, $d$Thanks be to God, who gives the victory. As this year of devotions ends, carry your morning routine forward: pray Ephesians, confess the Word, speak your declarations. You are a light wherever you go. Go forth in victory.$d$, $d$I declare that God gives me the victory through Jesus Christ. I go forth in victory today!$d$, $d$Thank You for the victory, Lord. I go forth in Your strength.$d$, $d$Read your seven Morning Declarations aloud and celebrate a full year with God.$d$, $d$How has this year with God changed you?$d$);
